    <node id="&quot;POLYURETHANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyurethane is a type of plastic mentioned as one of the six major polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a type of plastic that is commonly used in packaging and other applications."&lt;SEP&gt;Polyurethane, also referred to as PUR or PU, is a type of plastic polymer that is widely used in various applications, including packaging, kitchen sponges, and insulation foams, making up 7.4% of thermoplastics. It is a synthetic polymer with a highly complex chemical structure, which makes its recycling process challenging. Polyurethane is known to be resistant to biodegradation and has low biodegradability, contributing to plastic pollution. However, recent studies have shown that it can be degraded by certain microorganisms, such as Pseudomonas aeruginosa, Cladosporium sp. P7, and enzymes, as well as by a novel bacterial consortium and a landfill microbial culture. Additionally, polyurethane has been found to be biodegradable by various insects, including the yellow mealworm, Tenebrio molitor, and superworms, with mass reduction efficiencies of up to 53.2% after 58 days. The biodegradability of polyurethane is being studied extensively, and it is considered one of the most hazardous plastics to the environment and human health. Despite its resistance to biodegradation, polyurethane is being tested for its biodegradability and ecotoxicity, and researchers are exploring ways to break down this complex polymer. Overall, polyurethane is a widely used material with a significant environmental impact, and ongoing research aims to understand its degradation and develop more sustainable solutions.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f102938f307d7404d3f31b7200d93768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae42540a18795e5e2ad9054b7a0edfc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c3165b5b483903ac54f813f43b4076d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67425e341a5b2c8102281581fa148554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16c2c8ec44f02a1180cfb4b9e4fb90f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326</data>
