    <node id="&quot;XPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A method used to characterize the elemental content and chemical composition of a material's surface, including polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS is a technique used to investigate the surface chemical components of materials, including polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS, or X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy, is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS, or X-ray Photoelectron Spectroscopy, is a technique used to analyze the surface chemistry of materials, such as polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS is a technology used to analyze the chemical composition of materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS is a type of technique used to analyze the surface chemical composition and functional groups of HDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS is a technology that has been used to study the degradation of materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS is a technique used to analyze the surface composition of PS films, detecting changes after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS, or X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy, is a technique used to analyze the surface chemistry of PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS, or X-ray photoelectron spectroscopy, is a technique used to analyze the surface chemistry of materials, including PS films."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS is a type of polystyrene foam used for packaging, which is being degraded by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS is a type of polystyrene foam used in packaging materials, such as food packaging containers and coffee cups."&lt;SEP&gt;"XPS, or extruded polystyrene, is another type of plastic that mealworms can consume and degrade."</data>
