    <node id="&quot;TGA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TGA (Thermogravimetric Analysis) is a technique used to analyze the thermal modifications of polymers during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA is a type of analysis used to study the biodegradation of PP by T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;TGA, or Thermogravimetric Analysis, is a technique used to analyze the thermal stability and composition of various materials, including polyether-PU foam, polystyrene microplastics, polyurethane, and plastics such as polystyrene and LDPE. TGA is utilized to study the thermal properties, thermal decomposition, and thermal degradation of these materials. It is also employed to examine the biodegradation of plastics, including the analysis of frass samples and the detection of thermal modifications in materials such as surgical mask material and larvae from pristine Styrofoam to frass. Additionally, TGA is used to characterize the changes in thermal properties of materials like polyurethane foam and to confirm the biodegradation and oxidation of plastics. The technique provides valuable information on the thermal stability and composition of materials, supporting findings from other analytical methods such as NMR analysis. Overall, TGA is a versatile analytical technique that plays a crucial role in understanding the thermal properties and behavior of various materials, particularly in the context of biodegradation and environmental studies.&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA (Thermogravimetric Analysis) is a technique used to measure the thermal stability of substances, in this case, LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA is a biochemical measure used to analyze the thermal properties of LDPE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA is a technique used to analyze the thermal properties of LDPE and its biodegradation products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16c2c8ec44f02a1180cfb4b9e4fb90f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GPC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">GPC (Gel Permeation Chromatography) is a technique used to analyze the molecular weight of various substances, including plastics, polymers, and other materials. GPC is a biochemical measure and technique that provides valuable insights into the properties and behavior of these materials by determining their molecular mass and molecular weight distribution. It is utilized to examine the composition and degradation of polymers such as polyether-PU foam, polystyrene microplastics, PET polymers, PVC fragments, HDPE, and polypropylene. GPC is also employed to separate and analyze the molecular weight of substances, including the extract of frass and Styrofoam, as well as to characterize the molecular weight of polymers in frass and to compare the composition of mealworm fecula to the polystyrene feedstock. Additionally, GPC is used to assess molecular weight distribution in frass, although it may not be used in certain studies due to potential interference from metabolites. GPC is a versatile technology used in various fields to analyze the molecular weight and distribution of different materials, including the biodegradation of PP by T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae, and the degradation products of PS. It is also used to analyze the molecular weight of PS residuals after biodegradation, and to study the changes in molecular weight distribution of materials after biodegradation. Overall, GPC is a powerful tool for analyzing the molecular weight of a wide range of substances, providing important information about their properties and behavior.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb00229bf45a3bd9b8a17e10a1c93d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e16c2c8ec44f02a1180cfb4b9e4fb90f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
