    <node id="&quot;POLYPROPYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polypropylene is a type of plastic mentioned as one of the six major polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypropylene is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypropylene is a type of product that can be broken down by microorganisms through biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypropylene is a type of product that can be degraded by certain microorganisms, and its biodegradation is being studied."&lt;SEP&gt;Polypropylene is a type of plastic material, specifically a thermoplastic, that is widely used in daily life, making up 18.9% of thermoplastics and being the second most widely used plastic. Polypropylene, also referred to as PP, is commonly used in packaging and other applications, such as the production of masks, including disposable surgical masks, as well as in making containers and boxes. Despite being known to be a highly persistent non-hydrolyzable polymer with a high molecular weight and long carbon chains, making it resistant to biodegradation, recent studies have shown that Polypropylene can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms. These microorganisms include those found in the gut of yellow mealworms, also known as Tenebrio molitor, and superworms, also known as Zophobas atratus, which can biodegrade Polypropylene through a gut-microbe-dependent process. Additionally, other insects, such as Ephesia cautella, Plodia interpunctella, and certain species of beetle larvae, can penetrate or biodegrade Polypropylene. The yellow mealworm and the superworm have been found to consume Polypropylene, with an average consumption rate ranging from 0.0125 mg per day per mealworm to 2.53 to 4.55 mg per 100 mealworms per day, although at a lower rate than polystyrene. The biodegradation of Polypropylene is thought to occur through gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization in the mealworm gut, similar to the degradation of polyethylene. Furthermore, other microorganisms, such as Bacillus sp. and Rhodococcus sp., have also been found to biodegrade Polypropylene. Researchers are continuing to explore the biodegradation properties of Polypropylene and its potential environmental impact, as well as its impact on insect metabolism. Overall, Polypropylene is a complex plastic that is still being researched and studied to fully understand its biodegradation capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f79f3fee16e3f983c9f04a66e4d50760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff8edff5632