    <node id="&quot;POLYACTIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyactic Acid is a chemical compound that is being studied in the research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of biodegradable plastic that has been found to be broken down by certain species of insects, including Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms, the larvae of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of plastic that can be ingested and consumed by certain insects, such as the yellow mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of plastic that is being biodegraded by various organisms, including the yellow mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of plastic that is being studied for its potential to be degraded by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of toxin that can affect the pupation of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of biodegradable plastic that is being compared to polyethylene plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of plastic that can be degraded by certain microorganisms or enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic Acid is a type of biodegradable plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of plastic that has been found to be biodegradable by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of bioplastic that can be biodegraded by the larvae of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of bioplastic that can be broken down by earthworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyactic acid is a type of biodegradable plastic that can be disintegrated by earthworms."</data>
