    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The wax moth is an insect that can degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth is the larvae of Galleria mellonella and are known for their ability to ingest and consume plastic diets containing recalcitrant plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moths, specifically Galleria Mellonella, are capable of degrading polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth is a genus of moths that includes Galleria mellonella, which is known for its ability to degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax Moth (WM) is an insect model used to study the impact of plastics on central carbon metabolism, exhibiting elevated Vitamin B6 metabolism when exposed to certain plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax Moth is an insect model used to study the effects of plastics on metabolism and microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax Moth, or WM, is an insect species used in the study for evaluating the impact of plastic on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth (Galleria mellonella) is a species of insect that is known to degrade plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The wax moth is an insect whose larvae are capable of biodegrading polyethylene."</data>
