    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Tenebrio molitor larvae, also known as mealworms or yellow mealworms, are the immature stages of the mealworm beetle. They are capable of biodegrading various types of plastics, including polyethylene, polystyrene, polyvinyl chloride (PVC), polyactic acid, polyethylene terephthalate (PET), polypropylene, and polyurethane. The larvae's diverse gut microbiome, which includes bacteria such as Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450, Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451, and Bacillus sp. PELW2042, plays a crucial role in the breakdown of recalcitrant plastics. Tenebrio molitor larvae have been found to degrade plastics like LDPE, LLDPE, and HDPE, as well as PET polymers, with a half-life of 0.15 to 0.39 days. They are also capable of metabolizing styrene and biodegrading Styrofoam, making them a potential solution for plastic waste management. The larvae's gut microbiota aids in digestion and detoxification, and their physiological responses to microplastics are being evaluated. Additionally, Tenebrio molitor larvae are influenced by different feed types and are used as an alternative protein source for monogastric animals. They have been reared at Aarhus University for experimental purposes and are a significant subject of study due to their unique ability to degrade plastics and their potential applications in addressing environmental issues related to plastic waste, with a mass reduction efficiency of 71.03% and 73.28% for PET. Tenebrio molitor larvae are also the source of PS-degrading bacterial strains and have been found to contain microorganisms capable of degrading nanopolystyrene. They are capable of consuming and degrading plastic materials, showing changes in lipid and protein composition, making them a promising area of research for novel food sources and plastic waste management. Overall, Tenebrio molitor larvae are a crucial entity in the field of plastic biodegradation and have the potential to contribute significantly to environmental sustainability. They are commonly used as a food source for animals and have been studied for their ability to biodegrade plastics, including polyethylene and polystyrene microplastics, producing various degradation products. Furthermore, Tenebrio molitor larvae experience oxidative stress and negative physiological responses when biodegrading microplastics, including PE,</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ea4395a1eb1886507c72cdf33db169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa27760a0a889fe7b58360dbb150cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f141d484320c21ec01b892a9b7d56486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68f3ddf96d927254424a036cd8b9acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e88a3caade44f7fbc493dfc1c3ca8f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f21478b87845df31740b3dab37d197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBIOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbiota are able to decompose lignocelluloses and play a crucial role in the digestion of various types of food by mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbiota are microorganisms that live in the gut of insects and can provide them with essential nutrients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of an organism, and can be affected by the presence of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the digestive tract of an organism, such as an insect."&lt;SEP&gt;Gut Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of an organism, including insects such as mealworms, Tenebrio molitor larvae, and waxworms, as well as other animals like swine and humans. The Gut Microbiota plays a crucial role in the health and development of these organisms and is involved in various functions, including the biodegradation of polystyrene, polyethylene terephthalate (PET), polypropylene (PP) polymers, low-density polyethylene (LDPE), and other recalcitrant plastics. Additionally, the Gut Microbiota aids in the breakdown and digestion of various types of food, as well as the degradation of microplastics, lignocelluloses, PVC, and Styrofoam. Furthermore, the Gut Microbiota is involved in cell wall digestion and glucoside detoxification in Tenebrio molitor larvae. The composition and activity of the Gut Microbiota can be affected by different diets, feedstocks, and antibiotic treatments. The Gut Microbiota also contributes to nitrogen fixation and is essential for maintaining the health and well-being of the host organism. Overall, the Gut Microbiota is a vital component of an organism's digestive system, and its functions are essential for various physiological processes, highlighting its importance in the digestive system of various organisms.&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota of insects, including dry-wood termites, is diverse in structure and function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbiota is the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of an organism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e540abd667582c77f4d2222836147ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c038f908eb10a4a5715fb9cff3e05527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6464a2f3ca18442f70e254b9341a3e1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb