    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter Sp. is a type of bacteria that has been found to degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a bacterial strain isolated from the gut of the larvae of Indian mealmoth, with the capability of LDPE-degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a bacterium that can biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that can degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that has been isolated from the gut of the greater wax moth and has been found to be involved in the degradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that has been found to be associated with the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP) in the gut microbiome of Zophobas atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a type of gut microbe that is strongly associated with the PP-fed gut microbiome of Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. is a species of bacterium that is related to Strain LG3 and has been reported to have the ability to degrade PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPERGILLUS FLAVUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspergillus flavus is a fungus that can produce laccase-like multicopper oxidases to degrade synthetic plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus flavus is a fungus that contributes to the biodegradation of plastic waste, especially in the context of insect digestion and intestinal microflora."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus flavus is a species of fungus that can biodegrade polyethylene microplastic particles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus flavus is a type of fungus that can degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus flavus is a type of fungus that has been isolated from the gut of the greater wax moth and has been found to be involved in the degradation of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exiguobacterium sp. is a PS-degrading bacteria strain that has been isolated from mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a bacterial strain that can degrade PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a type of bacteria that can degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a species of bacteria that has been found to have the ability to degrade PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a type of bacteria that can be found in the gut microbiota of certain insects, including mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a type of bacteria that has been isolated from the gut of the yellow mealworm and has been found to be involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a type of bacteria that is associated with PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a microorganism capable of creating biofilms and degrading polystyrene in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a type of bacteria that has been found to be capable of creating biofilms and degrading polystyrene in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. is a type of bacteria that has been reported to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
