    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas Sp. is a bacterium that has been studied for its ability to biodegrade flexible polyurethane foams."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterium isolated from the gut of superworms that can biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a type of bacteria that can degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a microorganism that can biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterium that has been found to degrade low-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a species of bacteria that has been found to have the ability to transform styrene to phenylacetate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a microorganism that can biodegrade polystyrene, isolated from the gut of superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a type of bacterium that has been isolated from the gut of superworms and has been shown to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a species of bacteria that has been found to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a type of bacteria that has been isolated from the gut of the superworm and has been found to be involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a type of bacteria that can degrade polyethylene wax in sterilized compost conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a species of bacteria that appeared to be overrepresented in PS samples compared to CT samples, with a Log2-fold change of 6.5 and 4.1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a bacterium that can biodegrade polystyrene, isolated from the gut of superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a type of bacteria that has been reported to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. is a microorganism capable of degrading and metabolizing synthetic plastics and associated products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e77298fbeb95f87269261b74c2158d5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACINETOBACTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria associated with plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria present in the gut of yellow mealworms, with an increased relative abundance in the PP-fed group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been found to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been identified as potentially playing a role in the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a type of bacteria that can degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a type of bacterium that has been isolated from the larvae of Tribolium castaneum and has been found to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a type of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of the Tenebrio species, associated with the degradation of polyethylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria that includes a polystyrene-degrading species, indicating its potential role in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria that includes species capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a type of bacteria that has been isolated from the gut of the red flour beetle and has been found to be involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a type of bacterium that can degrade polystyrene, a common plastic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a genus that increased in relative abundance in the PP-fed group, suggesting its potential role in PP degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a type of bacteria that is dominant in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae fed with polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria that can decompose polystyrene, and some species have hydrophobic cell surfaces that contribute to autoaggregation and adhesion to polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been found to be capable of biodegrading polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8917166a3e45f4bf51e2e04949f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLYUYERA SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Klyuyera sp. is a type of bacteria that can degrade polypropylene."</data>
