    <node id="&quot;PLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PLA is a material used in the study, with mealworms showing a significant mass loss when fed PLA."&lt;SEP&gt;"PLA, or polylactic acid, is a biodegradable polyester that can be decomposed by microorganisms in the gut of mealworms, and is used as a food source for them, although it does not provide sufficient energy for their growth."&lt;SEP&gt;The PLA (Polylactic Acid) is a type of bio-based degradable plastic that is being studied for its properties and potential applications. It is a biodegradable polymer that can be ingested and consumed by certain insects, such as the yellow mealworm and Tenebrio molitor larvae. The PLA is also known to affect the metabolism and microbiota of insect models, and it has a positive interaction with certain model insects, indicating its potential for degradation. With a number average molecular weight of 30.5 kDa, the PLA is highly preferred by Tenebrio molitor larvae for degradation, which can achieve a removal efficiency of 85.2% by larvae fed with plastics only, and 76.5% by larvae fed with plastics plus bran. The PLA is compared to PET in terms of degradation rates and mass reduction efficiencies, and it is also being tested for its biodegradability and effects on Tenebrio molitor larvae. Additionally, the PLA can be disintegrated by earthworms, and it is used as a food source for plastic-degrading larvae. Overall, the PLA is a type of biodegradable plastic material with high degradability, and it is a potential area of future research on plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92bf00317a1d0d9ffccab121661a18a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
