hunk-3b2f11b2dff6f9e39c409f2bbd26c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e276f74ca596eed69175a31dab0bf51b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-304c1b42a6d3f439e83f380d2d64420a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-109486cd939a227e73354d0478c59ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHER-PU FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of foam material that is composed of polyether and urethane bonds, and is being studied for its biodegradation properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyether-PU foam is a material that is being consumed by mealworms, showing changes in its structure and morphology over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyether-PU foam is a type of plastic material that can be degraded by certain bacterial strains, including Enterobacteriaceae and Staphylococcus epidermidis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyether-PU foam is a type of plastic material used in this study to investigate its biodegradation by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyether-PU foam is a type of polymer that undergoes chemical structure modification as a result of mealworm ingestion."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PU WASTES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PU wastes refer to the polyether-PU foam used in this study, which is a type of plastic material."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBIAL COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbial community is a community of microorganisms that lives in the gut of an organism and plays a crucial role in its health and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial community refers to the microorganisms present in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbial community of mealworms, such as T. molitor, plays a crucial role in the degradation of polyether-PU foam, with changes in the community observed after feeding on polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbial community refers to the microorganisms present in the gut of the yellow mealworm, which plays a role in the biodegradation of polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbial community refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of an insect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial community refers to the collection of microorganisms that live in the gut of an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbial community refers to the collection of microorganisms that live in the gut of an organism, and play a crucial role in its health and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbial community refers to the complex community of microorganisms living in the gut of Tenebrio species, which is affected by the ingestion of different PE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbial community of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial community refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of the insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial community refers to the microorganisms present in the gut of the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbial community of Alphitobius diaperinus is composed of various microorganisms, including bacteria and fungi, that play a role in degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial community is the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbial community of mealworms is diversified and can be affected by the ingestion of frass, melted skeletons, and dead mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59453e4c878e72ac6985a08043cdf126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOLUENE 2,4-DIISOCYANATE (TDI)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Toluene 2,4-Diisocyanate (TDI) is a chemical used in the production of polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toluene 2,4-diisocyanate (TDI) is a chemical used to synthesize polyether-PU foam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHER-PU FOAM DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyether-PU foam degradation refers to the process by which yellow mealworms break down the polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The degradation of polyether-PU foam by mealworms is a biological process involving the consumption and breakdown of the material."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM SURVIVAL RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm survival rate refers to the percentage of yellow mealworms that survive when fed a particular diet, in this case, polyether-PU foam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Frass is the residue that is excreted by mealworms after they degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;FRASS is a complex biological material produced by various insect larvae, including mealworms, during the biodegradation of plastics and other materials. It is essentially the waste material produced by these insects after consuming various plastics, including polystyrene (PS), polyethylene, polyether-PU foam, polyurethane, polyethylene terephthalate, and polypropylene. The composition of FRASS includes manure and feed residuals, undigested residual microplastics, partially degraded plastics, and other fractions, such as water-soluble, ethanol-extractable, and solvent-extractable fractions. FRASS serves as a biological marker of degradation, indicating the presence of microorganisms that break down polymers, and contains various bioactive compounds. It is used to assess the digestibility of feedstock and to analyze the biodegradation of plastics. FRASS is produced by mealworms and other insects as they degrade plastics, and its characteristics are affected by the feed conditions. The production of FRASS by insects can impact soil microbial communities and metal bioavailability. Furthermore, FRASS has potential applications in waste management, agriculture, and construction, and can be used as a medium for plant growth. It is also a valuable tool for studying biodegradation, containing degraded microplastics, and can be sold as fertilizer. Additionally, FRASS can be ingested by mealworms, affecting their gut microbial community, and its analysis can provide valuable insights into the biodegradation process. Overall, FRASS plays a significant role in assessing the biodegradation of plastics, and its characteristics are analyzed in various experiments to understand its composition, properties, and potential applications.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e4