    <node id="&quot;SEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">SEM, or Scanning Electron Microscopy, is a technique used to analyze the surface morphology of various materials, including polyurethane, polyethylene plastics, polyether-PU foam, and polystyrene (PS) films and sheets. It is a technology used to visualize the surface alterations of plastics, detect changes after biodegradation, and examine the surface morphology of bacteria and microorganisms. SEM is also utilized to characterize the surface structure and texture of materials, observe the morphological characteristics of microorganisms and plastic materials, and analyze the surface morphology of PS/CS samples. Additionally, SEM is employed to observe the micro-morphological images of raw materials, such as CS and PS feedstocks, and to examine the surface of PS films and the formation of biofilms and other structures by bacteria. Furthermore, SEM is used to analyze the biodegradation of polyethylene plastics, the degradation of nanoplastic particles, and the morphological differences among original foam plastics, frass of plastics-fed larvae, and floating plastics. Overall, SEM is a versatile technique that provides valuable insights into the surface morphology and characteristics of various materials, making it a useful tool in various fields of research.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f102938f307d7404d3f31b7200d93768&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3646a65acc7cbdc1d20742888b17613a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FTIR SPECTROMETER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR Spectrometer is a biochemical measure used to identify the primary functional groups of virgin PE-MPs compared to frass residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectrometer is a device used for analyzing the chemical composition of substances, made available for the research by professor Jacek Katzer."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectrometer, or Fourier Transform Infrared spectrometer, is a technique used to investigate the changes of functional groups in the PU polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"The FTIR spectrometer is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of the insects and the polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectrometer is a device used to analyze the chemical composition of PP foam and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectrometer is a technology used to determine the main changes of the functional groups of PS and PE plastics after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR Spectrometer is a technology used to perform FTIR analysis."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e6ccf223c8c62d59ba994731f546ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19868f1234aac10de61c710c8352c076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TGA ANALYZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"TGA analyzer is a device used for thermal characterization of materials, in this case, polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analyzer, or Thermogravimetric analyzer, is a technique used to perform thermal characterization of polyether-PU foam and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analyzer was used to characterize the thermal variation of the PS and CS feedstocks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">BRAN is a nutrient-rich food source and feed used as a diet for various larvae, including Tenebrio molitor, superworms, and yellow mealworms. It serves as a conventional diet of mealworms, providing sufficient nutrients, rich in carbohydrates and proteins, for the growth and survival of these insects. BRAN is used in experiments as a control food source, a type of feedstock, and a nutrient that supports the development and mitigates oxidative stress in mealworms. It is a crucial component in the study of mealworm larvae's ability to biodegrade polyethylene (PE) microplastics and polystyrene (PS). BRAN is used to feed the larvae of T. molitor and T. obscurus, and it is also used to compare the consumption of low-density polyethylene (LDPE) by these larvae. As a dietary component, BRAN affects the removal efficiency of plastics by larvae, with co-diet BRAN showing significantly higher plastic mass reduction. The addition of BRAN to the diet of mealworms can promote their development, although it may slightly disturb the removal of microplastics in their intestinal tracts and affect the PE removal efficiency in the gut microenvironment. BRAN can relieve the constraint of lack of nitrogen sources and other nutrients in PS, providing energy and supporting growth in mealworms. It is used in combination with PE microplastics to improve their digestibility and biodegradation, and with PS to study its effect on biodegradation. In experiments, BRAN is used as a normal diet for superworms, serving as a comparison to the Styrofoam diet, and its composition and effect on mealworm growth are important factors in the study. BRAN is also used to feed the mealworms before the polystyrene degradation tests and as a control diet to compare its consumption to other materials such as polyurethane (PU) foam. Additionally, BRAN is used to mix with PE microplastics at a 1:1 ratio during incubation. Overall, BRAN plays a vital role in the study of mealworm larvae's ability to biodegrade PE and PS, and its effects are being closely monitored in various experiments. As a dietary component, BRAN serves as a nutrient-rich food source used to supplement the diet of plastic-degrading larvae, and its effects on the larvae's physiological responses to microplastics are being evaluated. BRAN is</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e415042ae4079ee5fe96c7105eb534c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9de