    <node id="&quot;WHEAT BRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Wheat Bran is a nutrient-rich food additive and feed supplement that plays a significant role in the diet and nutrition of various insects, including Tenebrio molitor, Zophobas atratus, yellow mealworms, Black Soldier Fly (BSF) larvae, and Mealworm (MW) larvae. It is a nutrient source for mealworms, containing carbohydrates, fat, proteins, and vitamins, and serves as a control food source for mealworms in experiments. Wheat Bran is commonly used as a co-diet or control diet in experiments studying the biodegradation of plastics, such as polystyrene (PS), and the effects of microplastics on these insects. It provides necessary nutrients for the growth and development of these insects and is used to facilitate plastic degradation. Wheat Bran can improve the resistance of mealworms to the negative effects caused by microplastics and is added to their diet to enhance their growth, support their biodegradation activities, and increase their consumption rate of plastics. As a standard culture substrate, Wheat Bran is often composed of 70% wheat bran, 25% corn, and 5% soybean, and is used as a dietary supplement to evaluate its effects on the larvae's physiological responses to microplastics. Additionally, Wheat Bran is used to compare the effects of different PE polymers on the gut microbial community of Tenebrio species and as a control diet to compare with plastic diets. It is a type of plant material that can be degraded by certain insects, including mealworms, and is utilized to feed these insects, providing them with necessary nutrients for growth and development. Wheat Bran has been found to be the best feed for the growth and development of mealworms, resulting in low larval mortality and good nutritional value, with an approximate nutritional value of 1,100 kJ/262 kcal, 4.0 g of fat, 18.0 g of carbohydrates, and 17.0 g of protein. Overall, Wheat Bran is a nutritious substance that can be used to breed mealworms and other insects, and is provided by various sources, accelerating mealworm development and having a positive effect on life cycle speed, making it an ideal feed for rearing these insects. It is also a normal food source for mealworm larvae, providing energy for their growth and survival. As a nutritional component, Wheat Bran is studied for its composition and quality, and its high fiber content makes it a</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8a706f2bd66291a3ef925114ffd9300&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5911f995d46a77458be83382b8c67f9b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8bb63b06976c3a8e6f2cea85c1ecf518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0afd02f25b584d6e3a755fc7272b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9578db0f9ed0398705827be5d4ee450&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb3edd44829125161ad624ea793ae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a57c5d6ee92292f1b1bd3dbe76e612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYPROPYLENE CONTAINER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polypropylene container is a type of container used to store the yellow mealworms and the polyether-PU foam in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polypropylene container is the material used to hold the habitat, with specific dimensions and holes for ventilation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT DISSECTION NEEDLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect dissection needle is a tool used to extract the gut of the yellow mealworms in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOXHLET EXTRACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soxhlet extractor is a biochemical measure used to extract crude fat from the mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soxhlet extractor is a device used to extract lipids from the mealworms' bodies using chloroform."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soxhlet extractor is a device used to extract polyether-PU fragments from the frass of the yellow mealworms in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TETRAHYDROFURAN (THF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"THF is the solvent used for extracting PS and PVC polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a chemical property used as a solvent in the extraction of Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a chemical used as a solvent in various applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used to extract polyether-PU fragments from the frass of the yellow mealworms in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a chemical used for extraction of polystyrene (PS) and polyvinyl chloride (PVC)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used to extract polystyrene (PS) from frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran is a chemical used as a solvent in the extraction process of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used in the experiment to extract the degraded products from the fecula, and its properties are important for understanding the extraction process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used to extract the degraded products from the fecula."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used to extract the residual polymer from the frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a chemical used in the experiment, purchased from Merck."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran is a chemical property that is used as a solvent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used to dissolve PS feedstock and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tetrahydrofuran (THF) is a solvent used to dissolve PS materials."</data>
