    <node id="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Mealworms, the larvae of the mealworm beetle, specifically the Tenebrio species, such as Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, also known as the yellow mealworm beetle, are insects that possess a unique ability to biodegrade various types of plastics. They are capable of degrading major plastic polymers, including high-crystallinity PET, polyurethane, polystyrene, polypropylene, and other microplastics such as PVC, LDPE, LLDPE, and HDPE, as well as polyethylene and vinyl plastics. This biodegradation process is facilitated by microorganisms and extracellular enzymes in their gut, as well as their gut microbiota, which includes certain bacterial strains, including nitrogen-fixing bacteria. Mealworms are characterized by their voracity, resistance to unfavorable environmental conditions, and rapid biomass growth, making them a valuable tool in the quest to develop sustainable solutions for plastic waste management. They have potential applications in a zero-waste circular economy, with their ability to break down and modify the backbone of various plastics having been observed. Mealworms are being studied for their ability to degrade different types of feedstocks, including lignocellulose and polystyrene, through a series of metabolic pathways and enzymatic reactions. Their gut microbiome plays a crucial role in their digestion process, and they are capable of adapting to new diets. Mealworms are also capable of consuming expanded polystyrene (EPS) at a faster rate than the adult stage. The growth and development of Mealworms are affected by the consumption of polystyrene, and their degradation efficiency is influenced by factors such as nutrient supplements and temperature. Additionally, Mealworms are the larvae of darkling beetles and can be used as a food source, with nutritional value and potential impact on food security. However, it is worth noting that Mealworms experience oxidative stress and negative physiological responses when ingesting microplastics, which can affect their growth and survival. Despite this, Mealworms are an important subject of study in the context of environmental science and technology, and their unique characteristics and abilities make them a crucial component in the development of innovative solutions for plastic waste management. Overall, Mealworms are a promising solution for plastic waste management, and their potential to utilize polystyrene and other plastics is being thoroughly studied, with their effectiveness and potential applications being continuously explored.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e4030ea35bee29093c1a8f19bc90774&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1684575ed5f73a2ebe1adc7fbbb3b942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa9972450967f344c19cb747d7ce649e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb1740bb657b0f90c48ee5e6d75945ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cc0afd02f25b