    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial Community refers to the community of microorganisms present in the gut of the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;The Microbial Community is a biological concept referring to a group of microorganisms that live together in a specific environment, such as the gut of an insect or other animals, and interact with each other to perform various functions. This community can be found in various environments, including wastewater treatment plants and the gastrointestinal tract of mealworm larvae. The composition and diversity of the Microbial Community can vary depending on the diet and environment of the host. The Microbial Community plays a crucial role in biodegradation processes, particularly in the gut microbiome of insects, where they work together to break down organic matter, including plastics like polyether-PU foam and microplastics. The community composition shifts during the degradation process, and the microorganisms aid in the biodegradation and mineralization of materials such as polystyrene. The Microbial Community is also involved in the biodegradation of aged microplastics and is essential for the degradation of organic materials. The community includes a diverse group of microorganisms, such as nitrogen-fixing bacteria, that live in the guts of mealworms, including Tenebrio molitor larvae, and contribute to the biodegradation process. Overall, the Microbial Community is a complex group of microorganisms that coexist, interact, and work together to perform various functions, including the degradation of organic materials and plastics.&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial community is a group of microorganisms that live in the larval gut of the mealworm and are involved in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbial community inhabiting the gastrointestinal tract of mealworm larvae changes depending on the diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-032b3b0fe0366e6e76e86abf8c48d200&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043ac4479b542b2eb2620db8d408349b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68f3ddf96d927254424a036cd8b9acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RRNA GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16S rRNA Gene is a gene that is used to study the diversity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA Gene is a genetic concept used to analyze the community richness and diversity of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA gene is a gene that is used to sequence and analyze the microorganisms in the gut of the insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA gene is a gene used to identify and classify microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;The 16S RRNA GENE is a genetic concept that encodes a component of the ribosome and is widely used as a target for PCR amplicon sequencing and microbial community analysis. It serves as a genetic marker to identify, classify, and characterize microorganisms, including bacteria found in various environments, such as the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae, mealworms, and superworms. The 16S RRNA GENE is utilized to investigate the effect of different diets, including plastic and mask diets, on the bacterial community of these organisms. Additionally, it is used to identify and analyze the microbial community composition, providing information on the taxonomy and phylogenetic relationships of microorganisms. The 16S RRNA GENE has also been employed to identify specific bacterial strains, such as those responsible for degrading polystyrene and PE, including strain BIT-26. Overall, the 16S RRNA GENE is a valuable tool for understanding the diversity and composition of microbial communities, and its sequencing results offer insights into the phylogenetic analysis and identification of bacterial species.&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA gene is a genetic marker used to identify and analyze the microorganisms in the gut core microbiome of the yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S rRNA gene is a gene that is used to analyze the microbial community in the gut of the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA gene is a genetic marker that is used to identify and classify microorganisms such as Strain LG3 and Strain SCGB1."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA gene is a type of gene used to identify and classify bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S rRNA gene is a genetic marker used to identify and classify bacteria, including nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA gene is a gene used as a marker for microbial community analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S rRNA gene is a genetic concept used to identify bacterial groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-512840a413df7ae3d881389c5cf1feb3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-94bf67bf1b585ce1050569a2eb0000cd</data>
    </node>
