    <node id="&quot;THF&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"THF (Tetrahydrofuran) is a solvent used for extraction and analysis of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used in the analysis of polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF, or tetrahydrofuran, is a solvent used to extract residual polymers from the frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used in the extraction process of PS polymers from the frass and EPS feedstock."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is an abbreviation for Tetrahydrofuran, a solvent used to dissolve PVC and frass specimens."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a chemical used to stop biological activity in experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used for extracting PS from frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF (Tetrahydrofuran) is a solvent used to extract plastic residues from insect frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a chemical reaction used to extract PS residuals from frass samples for GPC analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used to extract PS from the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used to extract the residual PS polymer from the frass of the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a solvent used to extract and analyze the degradation products of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF is a chemical property used to extract residual PS polymers from frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"THF, or tetrahydrofuran, is a chemical substance used as an organic solvent to extract the plastic components from the frass."</data>
