    <node id="&quot;ALPHA DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alpha diversity is a biochemical measure used to analyze the diversity of microorganisms present in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alpha diversity is a biological concept that refers to the diversity of species within a single sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alpha diversity is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms within a community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alpha diversity refers to the diversity of microorganisms within a particular environment or community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alpha diversity refers to the diversity of microorganisms within a single sample or group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alpha diversity is a measure of the diversity of the gut microbiome being analyzed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alpha diversity refers to the diversity of microorganisms within a community."</data>
