    <node id="&quot;SURVIVAL RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survival rate is a measure of the percentage of T. molitor larvae that survive under different dietary conditions, and is being studied to understand their development and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rate is a measure of the percentage of mealworms that survive under different feeding conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rate is a measure of the percentage of microorganisms that survive over a given period of time, in this case, T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;The Survival Rate is a physiological and biological measure used to evaluate the impact of various factors, such as plastic, microplastics, and different diets, on the metabolism and health of insects, specifically Tenebrio molitor larvae, also known as mealworms. It refers to the percentage of larvae or mealworms that survive over a given period, under certain conditions, and is influenced by factors such as nutrition, biodegradation, and the ingestion of plastics. The Survival Rate is a crucial parameter in assessing the effect of polystyrene (PS) on T. molitor larvae and is used to calculate the survivability of mealworms in different habitats and conditions. It is a health measure that is affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms and is used to evaluate the survival of mealworms during the biodegradation process. The Survival Rate is also used to evaluate the effect of different diets on Tenebrio molitor larvae and is a measure of how well mealworms survive in different habitats and conditions, including the ingestion of plastics. Overall, the Survival Rate is a comprehensive measure that provides insight into the physiological and biological responses of mealworms to various environmental and dietary factors.&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival rate is a physiological response of T. molitor larvae to microplastic ingestion, with lower survival rates observed in larvae fed with microplastics compared to those fed with bran."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2f11b2dff6f9e39c409f2bbd26c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5af82472112cbc9e76b1fd1ac6e8c54e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth is a biological process that is affected by plastic feeding in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a biological process that occurs in lesser waxworms as they consume and digest nutrients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a biological process that occurs in superworms and yellow mealworms, and can be affected by plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a health measure that is affected by the biodegradation of PE, with PE-fed larvae showing reduced growth rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth refers to the increase in size and biomass of mealworm larvae, which is affected by the biodegradation of PE microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth refers to the increase in size or biomass of the mealworms over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth refers to the increase in size or weight of the larvae during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a physiological response of mealworms to microplastic consumption, which can be affected by the larval age and consumption rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a physiological response of mealworms to the consumption of plastics and nutrients."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth refers to the increase in size and development of mealworms, which is influenced by their diet and nutrient sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"The growth of mealworms is affected by their diet, including plastic feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth refers to the increase in size or biomass of an organism, such as the T. molitor larvae, over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a biological process that was studied in the mealworms, including their weight and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is the process by which Tenebrio molitor develop and increase in size."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a biological process that occurs in mealworms, and it is affected by their diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a life stage of mealworms that can be affected by the ingestion of PS polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth is a biological process that occurs in organisms as they increase in size and develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth refers to the increase in size and development of the larvae, influenced by factors such as nutrition and energy availability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth refers to the increase in size and mass of an organism, which is supported by energy from food sources and reserves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7768b61a3d166f2cd01d4e87ac88cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9</data>
