    <node id="&quot;OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidation is a chemical reaction that can occur during the biodegradation of plastics, including polypropylene (PP)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidation is a chemical reaction that occurs during the degradation of plastics by the yellow mealworms, and it affects the formation of their degradation products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidation is a chemical reaction that occurs in the gut of the larvae and is involved in the degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;OXIDATION is a chemical reaction that involves the loss of electrons and is a crucial step in the biodegradation process of various plastics, including polyether-PU foam, polyethylene, polystyrene, PET polymers, and polypropylene masks. This reaction occurs in the breakdown of plastics by superworms and yellow mealworms, resulting in the formation of new compounds and the incorporation of oxygen into the polymer chains. OXIDATION is also observed in the frass excreted by mealworms and is proposed to be involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene by these organisms. Furthermore, OXIDATION is a process that modifies the functional groups of microplastics, leading to their degradation, and is a biological process that occurs during the degradation of PS film by certain microorganisms. It is also a chemical reaction that occurs on the surface of PS films, providing evidence of biodegradation. Overall, OXIDATION plays a significant role in the biodegradation of plastics, resulting in the formation of new compounds and the breakdown of polymer chains, and is involved in the metabolism of microplastics by mealworms, such as Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus.&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidation is a type of chemical reaction that can occur during the biodegradation of polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidation is a type of chemical reaction that occurs during the biodegradation of PP by T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidation is a chemical reaction that occurs on the surface of microplastics, leading to the formation of oxygen-containing groups and facilitating biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidation is a chemical reaction that occurs during the biodegradation of LDPE, resulting in the formation of new functional groups and the breakdown of long chain polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02a57c5d6ee92292f1b1bd3dbe76e612&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f</data>
