    <node id="&quot;YANG ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">Yang et al. are a research group that has made significant contributions to the field of biodegradation, particularly in the area of plastic degradation by microorganisms and insects. They have studied the biodegradation of various plastics, including polyethylene, polyether-PU foam, polystyrene, and low-density polyethylene, with a focus on the ability of microorganisms, insects, and mealworms to degrade these plastics. Specifically, Yang et al. have investigated the biodegradation of plastics by microorganisms, as well as the role of mealworms, such as Tenebrio obscurus and T. molitor, in degrading plastics like polystyrene and polyethylene. Their research has also explored the antioxidant enzyme activities and the mineralization of polystyrene in mealworms, the trophic transfer of microplastics in mealworms, and the biodegradable activity of microorganisms isolated from mealworm guts. Additionally, Yang et al. have developed methods for isolating bacteria that can degrade certain types of plastics, including the isolation of a PS-degrading bacterial strain Exiguobacterium sp. YT2 from the guts of T. molitor larvae. They have also studied the consumption of expanded polystyrene (EPS) cups by mealworms and the degradation of EPS by mealworms. Furthermore, Yang et al. have conducted studies on the life cycle and development of T. molitor, and have developed a method for carbon mass balance analysis. Their work has been cited in various studies, including those on the biodegradation of polypropylene masks, and has provided a reference for comparison with current studies on the biodegradation of plastics by insect larvae and mealworms. Overall, Yang et al. are a prominent research group in the field of biodegradation, with a strong focus on the role of microorganisms and insects in degrading plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2f11b2dff6f9e39c409f2bbd26c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d03c0a2dce3f57876d209a83a2e82a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df4c8c66bfbbfc37ed842f53d2b8796c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f</data>
