    <node id="&quot;ZHU ET AL.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A researcher who has studied the biodegradation of polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zhu et al. is a reference to a study on the effects of microplastics on earthworms and Folsomia candida."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zhu et al. refers to a research group that studied the food chain model for predator-prey relationships."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zhu et al. are researchers who reported on the biodegradation of plastics by yellow mealworms and superworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical element that is present in polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient that is transformed by the activity of certain enzymes in the digestive tract of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a chemical element that is a major component of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a chemical element that is present in LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads and is used as a sole carbon and energy source by isolated bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient required by microorganisms like Priestia megaterium S1 for growth and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient that is necessary for the growth and survival of microorganisms, including those in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutritional component that is obtained by mealworms from the digestion of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient that is being utilized by the PS-degrading bacteria, with the PS film serving as a carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient that is being measured in the Styrofoam, mealworms, and fecula over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is an element present in EPS and frass, with potential uses in various industries and applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient found in polyurethane foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a type of nutrient that is being used by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient that is essential for the survival of the larvae, and the diet had an effect on the availability of carbon."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is an essential element for energy and growth metabolism in insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a nutrient that is involved in the degradation of EPS by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is an element that is present in the molecular structure of Styrofoam and is affected by the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a chemical element present in PS films, detected by XPS analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a chemical element that is involved in the structure of PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is a chemical property that is captured during carbon capture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon is an element that is converted into CO2 during the biodegradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc75b7e672a7f7c036713dfa2675d79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXYGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical element that is present in polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a chemical element that is consumed during the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a chemical element that is present in LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads and is used as a sole carbon and energy source by isolated bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a chemical element that can be incorporated into the molecular structure of PS during its degradation, resulting in changes in functional groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a chemical element that can contribute to the degradation of EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a nutrient that can affect microbial activity and degradation of LDPE substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is an element that is present in the molecular structure of degraded Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is incorporated into the plastics during degradation, indicating an oxidative process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a chemical element present in PS films, detected by XPS analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxygen is a chemical element that is involved in the degradation of PS film."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16700b183fc641abfa74ad7fbb0917fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NITROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Nitrogen is a chemical element that is present in various forms and has multiple applications. It is a gas used in Thermal Gravimetric Analysis (TGA) to study the pyrolysis of samples, as well as a high-purity gas in the thermal decomposition process. Nitrogen is also an atmosphere used in the thermogravimetric analysis of samples and is used as a gas for drying and nebulizing in the mass spectrometry process. Additionally, nitrogen is a nutrient that is essential for the growth and development of living organisms, including insects such as mealworms, lesser waxworms, and Tenebrio molitor larvae. It is acquired through nitrogen fixation by the gut microbiome and is a component of insects' biomass, used to determine the crude protein content. Nitrogen is also found in polyurethane foam, polyether-PU foam, and worm frass, with potential applications in fertilization and plant growth. The nutrient is affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) in mealworms and is converted by microorganisms, which are involved in amino acid synthesis. Nitrogen is an essential element for protein and nucleic acid synthesis, as well as growth metabolism in insects. Its fixation is an important process in the ecosystem, and it is a nutrient that is analyzed in insects' biomass using the Dumatherm Nitrogen/Protein analyzer. The content of nitrogen in insects' frass is affected by different diets, and it can be provided to crops through the use of insect frass as a fertilizer. Nitrogen is also a key element in the study of nitrogen-fixing bacteria and their ability to convert atmospheric nitrogen into a usable form. Overall, nitrogen is a vital element with various applications in industries such as agriculture, and its role in the ecosystem and insect physiology is crucial for growth, development, and survival. Furthermore, nitrogen is a component of polyurethane plastics, which can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms, and its total content can be determined using the Kjeldahl method.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be14442602a613e0ddfef5b30f6d023d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e37da2fbe64f85c50c36da45006f4c23&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92b1e432ea4bee0f332d7303188e6de7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
