      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dichloromethane is a chemical compound used in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a chemical solvent that is commonly used in GPC analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a type of chemical used to dissolve PS balls, frass, and worm carcasses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a solvent used in the extraction process of LDPE samples from the frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a chemical used to prepare plastic emulsions for biodegradation studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a solvent used in the preparation of polymer emulsions, which is evaporated during the process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a solvent used to dissolve polystyrene, which is later volatilized."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a solvent that is being used to dissolve and analyze the daughter products of polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a solvent used to extract polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a solvent used to extract the polyethylene plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a chemical used to dissolve EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a solvent used to dissolve PS foams."&lt;SEP&gt;"Dichloromethane is a solvent used to prepare PS emulsion."</data>
