    <node id="&quot;SIMPSON INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Simpson Index is a biological concept used to analyze the community diversity of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simpson index is a biological measure that represents the evenness of microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Simpson index is a biological concept used to measure the diversity of the bacterial community in the gut of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Simpson index is a measure of biodiversity used to analyze the gut bacterial community of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simpson index is a measure used to quantify the diversity of gut microflora."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Simpson index is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms within a particular environment or community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simpson index is a measure of diversity used to analyze the bacterial communities in the gut of Alphitobius diaperinus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simpson index is a measure used to estimate the diversity of bacterial communities in PS and CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Simpson index is a measure of diversity, used to study the diversity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Simpson index is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms in the yellow mealworms' gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be9cf34196820cc6cfcf8a91406db608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACE INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ACE index is a biological measure that represents the richness of microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"ACE index is a measure of diversity, used to study the diversity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ACE index is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms in the yellow mealworms' gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAO1 INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chao1 index is a biological measure that represents the richness of microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SHANNON INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Shannon Index is a biological concept used to analyze the community diversity of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a biological measure that represents the diversity of microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Shannon index is a biological concept used to measure the diversity of the bacterial community in the gut of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Shannon index is a measure of biodiversity used to analyze the gut bacterial community of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a measure of the diversity of gut microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a measure used to quantify the diversity of gut microflora."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a measure of diversity, with a value of 1.691 for the bran-fed group and 0.731 for the EPS-fed group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a measure used to compare the diversity of the microbial flora between the bran-fed and EPS-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Shannon Index is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms within a particular environment or community."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Shannon index is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms in a sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a measure of species richness and diversity in the gut microbiome of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a measure of diversity used to analyze the bacterial communities in the gut of Alphitobius diaperinus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a measure used to estimate the diversity of bacterial communities in PS and CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon index is a measure of diversity, used to study the diversity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Shannon index is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms in the yellow mealworms' gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Shannon Index is a measure of the diversity of the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Shannon index is a measure of the diversity and richness of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Shannon index is a measure of the diversity of gut bacteria in mealworms, which can be affected by the biodegradation of PS polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a14229bceb339a4ca1baf0772b47ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be9cf34196820cc6cfcf8a91406db608&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RAREFACTION CURVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rarefaction curves are a biological measure that is used to assess the diversity of microbial communities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCOA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCoA is a biological measure that is used to analyze the similarity between microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCoA is a principal coordinate analysis used to compare the gut microbial community of larvae fed with different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCoA is a technique being used to analyze the beta diversity of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCoA is a technique used to analyze and visualize the similarity between communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCoA refers to Principal Coordinate Analysis, a method used to analyze the gut microbiome of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAY-CURTIS DISSIMILARITY INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bray-Curtis dissimilarity index is a biological measure that is used to analyze the similarity between microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bray-Curtis dissimilarity index is a measure used to quantify the difference in community structure of gut microflora."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PU-FED GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PU-fed group is a group in the study where larvae are fed with polyurethane (PU)."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU-fed group is a life stage that refers to the mealworms that are fed with polyether-PU foam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAN-FED GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bran-fed group is a control group in the experiment where mealworms are fed with bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran-fed group is a life stage that refers to the mealworms that are fed with bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran-fed group is a control group in the study, where larvae are fed with bran instead of plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bran-fed group is a control group in the study, where the yellow mealworms are fed a diet of bran."</data>
