    <node id="&quot;STAPHYLOCOCCUS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Staphylococcus sp. is a bacterial strain associated with polyether-PU-fed microbiome, with Staphylococcus epidermidis strain KH found able to grow on polyether-PU foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Staphylococcus sp. is a type of bacteria associated with the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae fed with both polystyrene and corn straw."&lt;SEP&gt;"Staphylococcus sp. is a bacterium that has been studied for its ability to degrade polystyrene, particularly in the context of microbiome research and environmental cleanup."&lt;SEP&gt;"Staphylococcus sp. is a type of bacterium that has been found to be capable of degrading polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4</data>
    </node>
