      <data key="d2">chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE (PE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE is a type of plastic that is widely used and is comprised of a linear carbon backbone, making it highly resistant to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene (PE) is a type of plastic that has been found to have both beneficial uses and significant environmental drawbacks. While it is considered non-biodegradable due to its extreme durability and resistance to degradation, recent studies have shown that it can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, such as Priestia megaterium S1, Enterobacteriaceae, Bacillus amyloliquefaciens, and other bacterial strains, as well as by insects like yellow mealworms, superworms, the larvae of Achroia grisella, and Tenebrio molitor larvae. Additionally, Polyethylene (PE) can be degraded by the mealworm larvae, including Tenebrio molitor, which can consume it with varying rates depending on the source and presence of additional substances. Other organisms, such as the lesser wax-worm and certain fungi, also have the ability to biodegrade Polyethylene (PE). The biodegradation of Polyethylene (PE) by these microorganisms and insects can lead to oxidative stress and other physiological effects, including affecting the central carbon metabolism of insect models. Polyethylene (PE) has specific properties, such as density and molecular weight, and is widely used in various applications, including packaging and agricultural films, due to its resistance to enzymatic depolymerization or degradation. It is similar to polypropylene (PP) but has a different chemical structure and biodegradation mechanism. Polyethylene (PE) is also compared to other materials, such as PU Foam, in terms of its biodegradation by mealworms. Despite its slow biodegradation rate, Polyethylene (PE) is a significant environmental problem due to its chemical inertness, macromolecular structure, and hydrophobicity. Nevertheless, it has been used in experiments as a diet for mealworms to study its biodegradation, and its biodegradation is an area of ongoing research and study. Overall, Polyethylene (PE) is a complex material with both beneficial uses, such as in packaging, and significant environmental drawbacks.&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene (PE) is a type of polymer that undergoes limited-extent depolymerization by insects, resulting in an increase in molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene (PE) is a type of petro-based polymer ingested by mealworms, causing oxidative stress and damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d27c41781c64c2b407faecc4bc31466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2359b10600f30376fe077f5e942cc999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-beb3c133fa4d5851f0feff55507c6874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2e818c436fabed80b9d3d720ebf491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-463ac9dfa68274d35700c61208f4ea85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85ce