    <node id="&quot;OTU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OTU (Operational Taxonomic Unit) is a unit of measurement used to analyze the diversity of microorganisms in a sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTU is a biological concept used to analyze the gut microbiomes of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTU is an operational taxonomic unit used to classify and compare the gut microbiome of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTU is a unit of measurement that was used to analyze the diversity of the microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTU, or operational taxonomic unit, is a biological concept used to investigate the impact of mask diets on the gut bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTU is a biological concept used to analyze the community richness and diversity of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTU is a unit of measurement used to study the diversity of microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b628b0a97e61f2c75e67585a9b07fc71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PU&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PU (Polyurethane) is a type of plastic associated with Mangrovibacter in superworms, indicating its potential role in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU (Polyurethane) is a type of plastic material that can be degraded by certain bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of plastic, specifically polyurethane, used in biodegradation experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of polyurethane that has been degraded by microorganisms and extracellular enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of plastic that is degraded by certain microorganisms, including Enterobacteriaceae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of diet fed to yellow mealworms, resulting in changes in the gut bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of plastic being studied for its degradation by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of plastic polymer, associated with biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms, with a unique structure that leads to greater enrichment of fungal colonies in the gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is a type of plastic, specifically polyurethane, used as an experimental feedstock in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PU is likely an abbreviation for a chemical or material property, but its exact meaning is unclear without further context."</data>
