    <node id="&quot;FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY (FTIR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of a substance, such as frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy (FTIR) is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy (FTIR) is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy (FTIR) is a technique used to detect changes in the functional groups of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a method used to characterize chemical modifications of polymer structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a method used to identify decomposition products from samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of plastic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy is a method used to characterize the functional groups of the extracted residual PS or PE polymers from the frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a biochemical measure used to analyze the composition of Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of polyurethane foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR was used to characterize the major functional groups of the PS and CS feedstocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of plastics before and after biodegradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a method used to characterize the functional groups of PS feedstock and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a technique used to analyze the biodegradation of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy (FTIR) is a technique used to characterize the functional groups of MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fourier Transform Infrared Spectroscopy (FTIR) is a process used to characterize the major functional groups in the frass of LDPE-fed larvae versus respective LDPE feedstocks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6ccf223c8c62d59ba994731f546ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a131a2ef26575f9f4b81bb622ef823e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GEL PERMEATION CHROMATOGRAPHY (GPC)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Gel Permeation Chromatography (GPC) is a biochemical technique used to analyze the molecular weight of polymers, such as polystyrene (PS), and other materials. GPC is an analytical method that can be used to determine the molecular weights and molecular weight distribution of plastic polymers, including microplastics and Styrofoam. This technique is used to separate and analyze the molecular weight of polymers, and to assess changes in molecular weight of polystyrene (PS) and other plastics. GPC can also be used to detect and identify polymer residues in the frass and carcasses of mealworms and superworms, and to investigate the physical and chemical changes in degraded PS films. Additionally, GPC is used to characterize the molecular weight of polystyrene and to analyze the molecular weight distribution of degraded polystyrene. The technique is also applied to study depolymerization and biodegradation of plastics, and to determine the molecular weight distribution of polymers after degradation. GPC is a method used to characterize the changes in molecular weights of ingested microplastics and to analyze the molecular weight of Styrofoam and its degradation products. Furthermore, GPC may be used to understand the impact of molecular weight of PE material on biodegradation. Overall, Gel Permeation Chromatography (GPC) is a versatile analytical method that provides valuable information about the molecular weight and molecular weight distribution of polymers, and is widely used in various fields, including materials science, biochemistry, and environmental science. GPC is used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers, such as PS, and to investigate the biodegradation of microplastics. It is a technique used to quantify the molecular weights of the residual polymer in the frass, and to analyze the molecular weight of plastics, showing how mealworms break down these materials.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6621e8191c2fc4d28a63e80e5d467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44565f26e7290c5eb0f26935608a5f16&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
