      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyurethane (PU) is a plastic material that has been shown to be biodegradable by T. molitor, indicating its potential for environmental degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PU) is a type of plastic that can be degraded by certain microorganisms and enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PU) is a type of plastic that is consumed by T. molitor mealworms, with different consumption rates for different types of PU."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane (PU) is a type of plastic that can be degraded by certain microorganisms, including those found in the gut of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by superworms and yellow mealworms."</data>
