      <data key="d1">"Bacillus Subtilis is a type of bacteria found in the mealworm gut, capable of degrading plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a bacterium that can biodegrade polyester polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a type of bacterium used as a standard in the TaqMan assay."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a species of Bacillus that can secrete surfactants to improve the efficiency of PE degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a type of microorganism that is capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a type of bacteria that can degrade polyurethane (PU)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a species of bacteria that has been shown to degrade polystyrene foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a type of bacterium that has been found to be capable of degrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus subtilis is a type of bacterium used as a standard in the TaqMan assay."</data>
