    <node id="&quot;POLYLACTIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polylactic Acid, or PLA, is a type of plastic used in the study to evaluate its impact on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a synthetic polymer that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a type of biodegradable plastic that has been shown to be broken down by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a type of biodegradable plastic that can be broken down by certain microorganisms, including those found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a type of plastic that has been found to be degraded by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a type of biodegradable plastic that is commonly used in packaging and other applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a type of plastic that has been found to be biodegradable by certain species of insects, including Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a type of biodegradable plastic that is being studied for its potential to replace traditional plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid is a type of biodegradable plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid, also known as PLA, is a biodegradable polyester used in various applications, including packaging and textiles, and can be decomposed by microorganisms in the gut of mealworms."</data>
