    <node id="&quot;EXPANDED POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Expanded Polystyrene is a type of plastic that is widely used in packaging, building materials, and insulation, commonly known as Styrofoam. It is difficult to decompose, which has made it a significant environmental pollutant due to its contribution to plastic debris. Expanded Polystyrene is being studied for its biodegradation properties and potential impact on the environment. Recent studies have shown that Expanded Polystyrene can be biodegraded by certain species of insects, such as the yellow mealworm, specifically the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, as well as by land snails like Achatina fulica. Additionally, it can be biodegraded by microorganisms. The biodegradation of Expanded Polystyrene by these organisms is being studied to understand the effects of polymer size on biodegradation and to analyze the ability of mealworms to degrade it. Furthermore, Expanded Polystyrene has been shown to be toxic to aquatic invertebrates. The substance is also being tested for its toxicological effects when ingested by Tenebrio molitor L. Overall, Expanded Polystyrene is a type of plastic that has negative environmental impacts, but its biodegradation by certain organisms, including mealworms, beetles, and microorganisms, offers a potential solution to mitigate these effects. Researchers are continuing to study the biodegradation properties and potential environmental impact of Expanded Polystyrene, with the goal of finding ways to reduce its harmful effects on the environment. It is used in various applications, including packaging and building insulation, and its biodegradation by mealworm larvae can lead to changes in cellular lipids and protein alteration.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c1e1694d44433fcf53dc8120c479ca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a47a21d3773bb9ea3318d47bb077597f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c2e7d253d2108b0ed94be7f2dc7466&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf641df5c55c7ff41895611514cdd22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b</data>
