    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER SP. D1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter Sp. D1 is a type of microorganism that is capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterium that can biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. d1 is a species of bacteria that has been found to be capable of biodegrading polyethylene, and is found in the guts of certain insects, including the wax moth Galleria mellonella."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a type of bacterium that has been isolated from the mealworm gut microbiome and is capable of degrading plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter sp. D1 is a bacterium capable of biodegrading polyethylene."</data>
