    <node id="&quot;GALLERIA MELLONELLA LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Galleria Mellonella larvae are the immature stage of the greater wax moth and are capable of degrading polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae are a type of insect that has been found to have microorganisms in its gut that can break down plastic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae of Galleria mellonella, which can biodegrade polystyrene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae are the larval stage of the greater wax moth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae are insects that can degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae are insects that have the ability to digest and biodegrade plastic products such as PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Galleria mellonella larvae are a type of insect that may be affected by microplastic biodegradation, similar to Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
