    <node id="&quot;GUT-MICROBE-DEPENDENT DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A process by which microorganisms in the gut of an organism break down polymers into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which certain organisms can break down plastics with the help of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of certain insects, such as Tenebrio molitor and Zophobas atratus, break down polypropylene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of an organism break down polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which certain microorganisms, such as Tenebrio molitor, break down plastics with the aid of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of animals break down polymers into smaller molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of an organism break down complex polymers, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization refers to the process by which insects break down plastics with the help of microorganisms in their gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of insects break down plastics into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of insects break down plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization refers to the process by which microorganisms in the gut of an organism, such as Tenebrio molitor larvae, break down polymers like polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of insects break down plastics into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of an organism break down plastics into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which microorganisms in the gut of certain insects, such as yellow mealworms, break down plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-551c06d3562ff01465354b3a954b1145&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
