    <node id="&quot;TGA ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dfcb3f2424bd027b5888293a0d01d3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen atmosphere is used as a condition in the TGA analysis to perform thermal characterization of polyether-PU foam and frass samples in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis, or thermogravimetric analysis, is a biochemical measure used to analyze the thermal stability of plastics such as PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis is a technique used to analyze the thermal properties of a substance, in this case, polystyrene and its biodegradation products."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis is a technique used to analyze the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis is a technique used to characterize the changes in the thermal properties of the polyurethane foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis is used to study the decomposition stages of PS and CS."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis is a technique used to evaluate the presence of PS in the frass of the insects by heating the samples and analyzing the thermograms."&lt;SEP&gt;"TGA analysis is a method used to study the thermal modifications of ingested PS, showing different thermal properties of the biodegraded PS."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
    </node>
