    <node id="&quot;FUNGI&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2e818c436fabed80b9d3d720ebf491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165679126b891785de849b020c1548f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-463ac9dfa68274d35700c61208f4ea85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59453e4c878e72ac6985a08043cdf126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e540abd667582c77f4d2222836147ac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630d06d8ab372b4cadd7e3772d8fa1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brunner et al. has studied the biodegradation of plastics by fungi."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that are involved in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that are capable of biodegrading polyethylene and other plastics, and play important roles in the microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that are capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that are being studied for their ability to biodegrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that may be involved in degrading plastic, although their role is not explicitly mentioned in the text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi is a type of microorganism that is part of the composition of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that can biodegrade polyethylene (PE) waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are organisms that, along with insects and bacteria, can convert natural polymers into smaller fragments, facilitating enzymatic reactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are the predominant microorganisms responsible for degrading soil-buried polyester polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that play a crucial role in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that can biodegrade organic materials, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that can be found in a variety of environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that are being studied for their potential to degrade plastics, including polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that are present in the gut of Alphitobius diaperinus and are involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungi are a type of microorganism that has been found to be efficient in degrading synthetic polymers."</data>
