    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Mealworm larvae, specifically Tenebrio molitor, are the immature stages of insects in the family Tenebrionidae. They are a source of microorganisms, including Pseudomonas aeruginosa M8 and Achromobacter xylosoxidans M9, as well as Achromobacter, which have been found to have the ability to biodegrade polystyrene. Mealworm larvae are capable of digesting food that is not found in their natural environment, including polyethylene, polystyrene, and cellulose waste. They are able to digest and assimilate plastics, including polyethylene and polystyrene, and have been found to be efficient in degrading plastics, with their efficiency varying depending on the type of waste and other factors. The gut microbiome of mealworm larvae plays a crucial role in this biodegradation process. Mealworm larvae consume polystyrene and produce frass, and their ability to biodegrade expanded polystyrene has also been observed. However, the process of biodegrading plastics has been shown to have negative effects on their physiological responses, including weight loss, biomass reduction, and decreased survival rates, as well as oxidative stress and lipid peroxidation. Despite these challenges, mealworm larvae are being used in experiments to test the biodegradation of different types of plastics, including polyurethane and lignocellulose, and to investigate their ability to produce biodiesel. Their growth and development are important factors in the production process. Mealworm larvae are also being grown on various substrates to analyze their protein content, fatty acids, and genetic and biochemical digestive tract analysis, which can vary depending on the type of feed. They have been found to show changes in lipid and protein composition when degrading polystyrene. Overall, mealworm larvae are a promising area of research in the field of plastic biodegradation, with their unique ability to digest and degrade plastics making them a valuable tool in the fight against plastic waste.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f8516b10110f884279870c2ef887f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa64e5cd2c08637934509262e56ab363&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26138366e1d9310732edc569ba338bfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e56bce8206396081e0b7dccc47a10c9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1</data>
