    <node id="&quot;MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">Microplastics are a type of toxin that can harm the environment and human health. They are small plastic particles, typically less than 5 millimeters in size, that result from the disintegration and fragmentation of larger plastic debris, such as polystyrene, polyethylene, and polyethylene terephthalate. Microplastics can be found in various environments, including oceans, soils, and freshwater ecosystems, and pose a significant challenge to the ecosystem. They can cause physical damage to biological tissues, induce oxidative damage, and trigger inflammatory responses in living organisms. Microplastics can enter an organism's body and accumulate, potentially causing harm to their health, and have significant potential impacts on the environment. 

Microplastics are produced through the biodegradation of larger plastic materials and can be ingested by animals, including insects such as mealworms, leading to toxic effects on their health and the environment, potentially causing harm, including weight loss and higher mortality. Certain microorganisms, as well as mealworm larvae, are capable of biodegrading microplastics, although this process can induce oxidative stress and lipid peroxidation in the larvae. Microplastics are associated with the physicochemical properties of polymers, including PE, PS, and PVC, which are being studied for their effects on the environment and human health.

The effects of microplastics on organisms, such as Tenebrio molitor, are a subject of ongoing research, highlighting the need for optimization of the degradation process to mitigate their negative effects. Microplastics can affect the feeding and metabolism of organisms and can accumulate in the bodies of mealworms, potentially causing harm to the environment and human health. As persistent pollutants, microplastics are a concern for the environment and human health, and further research is needed to understand their effects and develop effective strategies for mitigating their impacts. Overall, microplastics are a significant environmental concern, and their effects on organisms and ecosystems are a subject of ongoing research.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a72a9944bcd114b6a3be55ad9b596c77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df896f6505a6c800d1edd6c75fce9b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7768b61a3d166f2cd01d4e87ac88cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38283df790b03806f99ca90272a1000f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38