    <node id="&quot;OXIDATIVE STRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidative stress is a biological response of mealworms to the ingestion of PS polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress is induced in mealworms as a result of biodegrading PS polymers, particularly those with ultrahigh molecular weights."&lt;SEP&gt;Oxidative Stress is a biological concept that refers to the imbalance between the production of free radicals, also known as reactive oxygen species (ROS), and the body's ability to detoxify them. This imbalance can be caused by various factors, including the ingestion of microplastics, the biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene (PS) by mealworms, and exposure to other environmental stressors. Oxidative Stress is a type of physiological stress response that can occur in organisms, including Tenebrio molitor larvae, also known as mealworms, and can have negative impacts on ecosystems and human health. The production of ROS and other reactive molecules can lead to damage to cellular structures and biomacromolecules, such as membrane lipids, and can be measured using various biological assays. Oxidative Stress can be alleviated by supplementing with certain substances, such as bran. In mealworms, Oxidative Stress has been studied in the context of biodegradation of microplastics, resulting in negative physiological responses, including tissue damage and toxic effects. The ability of microorganisms to produce enzymes that break down lipid hydroperoxides can also influence Oxidative Stress. Overall, Oxidative Stress is an important consideration in the development of insect-based food products and is being investigated in various contexts, including the health status of insects and the effects of microplastic ingestion.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59879670a8110deb87c1843ffdb71c75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19bc661af07a194ef5a3f48c337c8d59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIONIDAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrionidae is a family of beetles that includes the species Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrionidae is a family of insects that includes the species T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrionidae is a family of beetles, also known as darkling beetles, that includes a diverse range of species, such as Tenebrio molitor, also known as the yellow mealworm, Tenebrio obscurus, and Zophobas atratus, also known as the superworm. The family Tenebrionidae is notable for its potential in biodegrading plastic waste, with some species capable of degrading various types of plastics, including polyurethane, polystyrene, and polyethylene. Tenebrio molitor, in particular, has been studied for its ability to biodegrade plastics, and the yellow mealworm can digest and biodegrade polystyrene. Additionally, mealworms and superworms, also part of the Tenebrionidae family, can consume and degrade polystyrene. The genus Tenebrio, which is part of the Tenebrionidae family, has the ability to depolymerize polystyrene. Some species within the Tenebrionidae family, such as Tenebrio molitor and Alphitobius diaperinus, have been found to have microorganisms capable of degrading polystyrene. The family Tenebrionidae is relevant to environmental studies due to the capabilities of its species to utilize and biodegrade plastics, making them an important area of study. Overall, Tenebrionidae is a significant family of beetles that has garnered attention for its potential in addressing environmental issues related to plastic waste, with species like T. molitor, T. obscurus, and Zophobas atratus being studied for their role in polystyrene biodegradation and mineralization.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eed7e10fb1cc08baaecab1b1cffad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ea4395a1eb1886507c72cdf33db169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fa884bb7540491e8ab975e29c46d1f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff228c7711f9