    <node id="&quot;COLEOPTERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coleoptera is an order of insects that includes beetles, such as the yellow mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coleoptera is an order of insects that includes the family Tenebrionidae."&lt;SEP&gt;COLEOPTERA is an order of insects that encompasses a diverse range of beetles, including mealworms, superworms, and the darkling beetle. This order comprises several families, such as Tenebrionidae, to which species like Zophobas atratus, Tenebrio molitor, also known as the mealworm or yellow mealworm, and Tenebrio obscurus belong. COLEOPTERA is notable for including insects capable of biodegrading plastics, with species like the darkling beetle and the yellow mealworm found to biodegrade polystyrene. Some species within this order, particularly Tenebrio molitor, have been found to biodegrade plastics and are important subjects of study in ecological and environmental research. Additionally, some species within COLEOPTERA have larvae that can degrade nanoplastic particles. The family Tenebrionidae, which is part of COLEOPTERA, has been found to have species capable of degrading polystyrene. COLEOPTERA includes species that have been observed taking plastics as a food supply and can decompose them in vivo. Overall, COLEOPTERA is a diverse and complex order of insects, with its members exhibiting unique characteristics and capabilities that make them important subjects of scientific study, particularly in the areas of polystyrene biodegradation and mineralization. As a significant group in the insect world, COLEOPTERA's members are vital components of various ecosystems.&lt;SEP&gt;"Coleoptera is an order of insects that includes the family Tenebrionidae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cff93a2e1d68c6ed1fcd9f720197238f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-35eed7e10fb1cc08baaecab1b1cffad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ea4395a1eb1886507c72cdf33db169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d1301f6942d17092ef7b22ac40f19f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0014171c7ef07a60c6be3b57e791688c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ff228c7711f94fb27152b187b1fa3eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cfbd751517e11b1b4052961a01008cbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2e818c436fabed80b9d3d720ebf491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d417