    <node id="&quot;DARKLING BEETLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Darkling beetle is a genus of insects that has been found to be capable of biodegrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Darkling beetle is the genus of beetle that includes the mealworm beetle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Darkling beetle is a species that can accelerate its development if rearing conditions improve, but with limitations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Darkling beetle is another name for Tenebrio molitor, the species of insect used in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The darkling beetle is another name for Tenebrio molitor, a species of edible insect."&lt;SEP&gt;"The darkling beetle, referring to T. molitor, is a microorganism capable of biodegrading polypropylene (PP)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Darkling beetle is the common name of the family Tenebrionidae, which comprises approximately 20,000 species across 2300 genera worldwide and includes species capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Darkling beetles are a family of insects that include Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, which are capable of biodegrading LDPE polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC WASTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic waste is a major environmental concern and includes products such as polystyrene foam and microplastic particles."&lt;SEP&gt;Plastic Waste is a major environmental issue that refers to the accumulation of plastic materials in the environment, posing a significant threat to ecosystems and human health. It is a type of waste composed of plastics, including polystyrene, that are discarded and not biodegradable. Plastic Waste is a hazardous material and a physical contaminant that can harm the environment, wildlife, and human health, with its durability and resistance to natural degradation contributing to its persistence in the environment. The biodegradation of Plastic Waste is crucial for sustainable management, and it is being addressed through various studies, including the use of superworms and mealworms, which can degrade plastic waste, with superworms being more efficient. Additionally, recycling is also a potential solution to mitigate the environmental problems caused by Plastic Waste. The consumption of plastics by mealworms, such as Tenebrio molitor larvae, is also being explored as a means to address the growing environmental problem of Plastic Waste. Overall, Plastic Waste is a significant environmental problem that requires attention and action to mitigate its harmful effects on the environment and human health.&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste refers to the accumulation of plastic debris in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste is a type of waste that can be degraded by mealworms and other organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste is a type of waste that is being studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic waste is a type of waste that is generated by human activities and is a major environmental problem."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71372e333b39cee7eea0c53f89bec5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40407fe311340b08da856202f38b459c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908b8bfa7e446694958cf9bd0cfbc583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-078b6698be699eb7105b7cffadf709af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ECOSYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ecosystems are affected by microplastics and other environmental pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecosystems are communities of living organisms and their environment, which can be harmed by plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecosystems are communities of living organisms and their environment, which can be harmed by plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecosystems refer to the complex networks of living organisms and their interactions with the environment, which can be harmed by plastic pollution."</data>
