    <node id="&quot;BIODIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodiversity refers to the variety of different species of microorganisms, such as Tenebrio molitor and Galleria mellonella, that can biodegrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiversity refers to the variety of living organisms within an ecosystem, which can be harmed by plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiversity refers to the variety of different species of plants, animals, and microorganisms that live in an ecosystem."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiversity refers to the variety of microorganisms present in the gut of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiversity refers to the variety of different species of plants, animals, and microorganisms that live in an ecosystem, and is affected by plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiversity refers to the variety of different species, including microorganisms, that exist in an ecosystem, which can be affected by plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiversity refers to the variety of different species that live in a particular environment, including the gut of an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiversity refers to the variety of different species that live in an ecosystem, and it is influenced by the ability of microorganisms to biodegrade organic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d57e056cd3b06b37d22117fc75e3a4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79e833cbc3a0a6e2c80e1b69da50317e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e</data>
