    <node id="&quot;LANDFILLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Landfills are a common disposal method for EPS, but can result in the generation of environmental pollutant byproducts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Landfills are a type of location where municipal solid waste, including polystyrene (PS) products, is disposed of."&lt;SEP&gt;"Landfills are areas where waste is disposed of, which can contribute to plastic waste accumulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Landfills are where EPS waste ends up, highlighting the need for biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3b2f11b2dff6f9e39c409f2bbd26c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617</data>
    </node>
