    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymer is a biological concept that refers to the type of plastic being degraded by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of material being studied for biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of material that can be degraded by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer refers to a large molecule composed of many smaller molecules, such as polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer refers to the type of plastic used in the experiment, including polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer refers to the chemical property of microplastics, which can be broken down into smaller fragments through depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of material that is being studied for its biodegradation patterns and processes, including polypropylene (PP)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of molecule that makes up PET, with different molecular weights being tested for their effect on biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of product that includes PET, which is being biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer refers to the type of material used to make surgical masks, which can be degraded by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a general term for a class of materials that can be degraded by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of material that is composed of long chains of molecules, and it is the general category of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of chemical compound that includes EVA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of material that includes plastics such as PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a product that is broken down by T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of material that includes LDPE, which can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of material that is being studied for its biodegradation and properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer is a type of product that can be broken down by microorganisms through biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e6ccf223c8c62d59ba994731f546ad9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b</data>
    </node>
