    <node id="&quot;WATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water is a chemical used in the extraction solvent for lipid analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a component of the biomass levels of the mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a nutrient that is added to some diets consumed by T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a nutrient that is added to some diets, which facilitates better PS consumption and higher survival rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a nutrient that is used by Tenebrio molitor for survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is an essential nutrient added to some of the diets in the experiment to study its effect on biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is used to wet the media and support the growth of the grafted cacti."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a component of the diet fed to the mealworm larvae during the biodegradation study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a component of the diet used in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a nutrient used in the diet of the larvae in the study of polystyrene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a nutrient being added to some of the diets, with its effect on the insects' growth and metabolic activity being studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a nutrient that affects the thermal degradation of PS, with its presence influencing the transition temperatures and molecular mass of PS, particularly in the presence of bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a nutrient used in the experiment, fed to the Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a physical characteristic used to hydrate the Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water is a physical environment where microplastics can be found and can affect the physiology and behavior of organisms that live in it."</data>
