    <node id="&quot;FAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fat is a component of the biomass levels of the mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a type of lipid that is present in the mealworm larvae and affects their growth and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a lipid extracted from the insects using hexane in a Soxhlet system, to determine its percentage in the nutrient composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat, or lipid content, is reduced in mealworms fed with Styrofoam, suggesting a shift in energy storage and utilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a nutrient found in the barley."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a nutrient that is being measured in the experiment using the Soxhlet method, with its content reported as an average value and standard error in g/100 g DM."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a nutritional component being measured in the larvae and excrement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat is a source of energy for insects, accumulated in the insect fat body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">PROTEIN is a biological molecule that contains nitrogen and is essential for the growth and development of living organisms, including insects such as Tenebrio molitor L. and Zophobas morio, as well as for human health. As a crucial component of the biomass levels of various organisms, PROTEIN plays a vital role in homeostasis regulation in neurodegenerative diseases. It is a relatively stable and resistant biomolecule, with only slight effects observed due to food type. However, the type of diet mealworms are fed can affect their PROTEIN content, with some diets resulting in higher or lower PROTEIN levels. For example, mealworms fed with Styrofoam have been found to have higher amounts of PROTEIN, indicating a potential adaptation mechanism. Additionally, the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) in mealworms can also affect the PROTEIN content. PROTEIN is also provided by nitrogen-fixing bacteria to the larvae, although in limited amounts. It is an essential nutrient for growth and development in insects and is found in the biomass of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus. The content of PROTEIN in mealworms varies between 16.01-23.38 ng/mg. PROTEIN is being extracted and characterized from various insect species, including Tenebrio molitor, and studied for its potential effects on cell cytotoxicity. Moreover, PROTEIN is a nutrient that is lacking in plastics, which can affect the growth and viability of mealworms consuming them. The content of PROTEIN can be determined using methods such as the Kjeldahl method or the Dumatherm Nitrogen/Protein analyzer, and is often reported as an average value and standard error in g/100 g DM. Overall, PROTEIN is a nutrient-rich component of yellow mealworm larvae, abundant in Tenebrio molitor larvae, making it a valuable source of nutrition and a potential alternative protein source for livestock feed, also found in other sources, including barley bran, where it makes up 14.7% of its composition. PROTEIN is important for body functioning and can be used as a source of energy during starvation, and it is beneficial for the growth and development of T. molitor and other living organisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c038f908eb10a4a5715fb9cff3e05527&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2359b10600f30376fe077f5e942cc999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c095cc3175666d5093fe411f9a39cb66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed</data>
