    <node id="&quot;SUPEROXIDE DISMUTASE (SOD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SOD is an antioxidant enzyme being measured in the mealworm larvae to assess their antioxidant performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD is an antioxidant enzyme that is being measured in the larvae to evaluate their oxidative stress response."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD is an enzyme that was analyzed in mealworms to reflect antibiotic performance."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superoxide Dismutase (SOD) is an enzyme that reflects antibiotic performance in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superoxide dismutase (SOD) is an enzyme that plays a role in reducing oxidative stress in Tenebrio molitor larvae by converting superoxide into hydrogen peroxide and oxygen."</data>
