    <node id="&quot;MALONDIALDEHYDE (MDA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MDA is a measure of lipid peroxidation in the larvae, and its levels are being evaluated in response to microplastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA is a molecule being measured in the mealworm larvae to assess their lipid peroxidation level."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA is a metabolite that was analyzed in mealworms to indicate lipid peroxidation levels."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde (MDA) is a metabolite that indicates lipid peroxidation levels in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Malondialdehyde (MDA) is a metabolite that is produced during lipid peroxidation, indicating the level of oxidative damage caused by microplastic biodegradation in Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
