      <data key="d1">"Peng et al. are researchers who compared the PS degradation efficiencies of yellow mealworms and dark mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. are researchers who have published studies on plastic biodegradation by mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. are researchers who have studied the ability of insects to break down and modify the backbone of various plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. are researchers who observed that a sole PLA diet accelerated the pupation of mealworms but led to failure in becoming adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a reference to a study on the effects of polyactic acid on mealworm pupation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. refers to a research group that conducted previous studies on biodegradation of EPS and LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. are researchers who studied the biodegradation of plastics by insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a researcher who has studied the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a research group that has conducted studies on the plastic degradation mechanism of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a reference to a research study that investigated the ability of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus to oxidize PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. are researchers who have published studies on the degradation of EPS by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a research group that has conducted studies on the biodegradation of EPS by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. refers to a study on the consumption of plastics by superworms, providing a reference for comparison with the current study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. refers to a research study that is cited in the text, which provides context for the biodegradation of polypropylene masks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a reference to a study on biodegradation of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a reference to a study on the biodegradation of plastics by insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a researcher who has published studies on the degradation of polystyrene by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a research group that has published studies on the gut microbiota and its role in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. refers to the researchers who previously reported on the biodegradation of PP foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Peng et al. is a reference to a previous study on PS degradation by T. obscurus versus T. molitor."</data>
