    <node id="&quot;CARBOHYDRATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbohydrate is a type of biomolecule that is affected by starvation in mealworms, with a decrease in level observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrate is a type of nutrient that is present in the bran and affects the growth and biodegradation of the mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are a type of biomolecule that can be found in mealworms and superworms, and their content can be affected by consuming polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrates are a type of nutrient that is found in the biomass of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbohydrate is a type of nutrient that is essential for the growth and development of living organisms, including mealworms."</data>
