    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE + BRAN-FED LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE + bran-fed larvae are a life stage of mealworm larvae that have been fed a diet of both PE and bran."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survival is a biological process that is affected by polystyrene diet in yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival is a health measure that is affected by the biodegradation of PE, with PE-fed larvae showing reduced survival rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival is a physiological response of mealworms to microplastic consumption, which can be affected by the larval age and consumption rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival is a physiological response of mealworms to the consumption of plastics and nutrients, which allows them to live and thrive."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival refers to the ability of mealworms to live and thrive, which is influenced by their diet and nutrient sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival refers to the ability of yellow mealworms to survive, which can be affected by the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival is a measure of the ability of microorganisms, such as T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae, to survive over a given period of time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Survival is a biological process that occurs in mealworms, and it is affected by their diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMASS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomass is a biochemical measure that refers to the amount of living matter in an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass is a nutritional component that is converted into energy during bioenergy production."&lt;SEP&gt;BIOMASS refers to the total amount of living matter in a given area or volume, encompassing a broad range of biological concepts. It is a measure of the amount of living material in an organism or ecosystem, often used to study biodegradation and assess the growth of organisms such as Tenebrio molitor larvae and Priestia megaterium S1. BIOMASS is affected by various factors, including the biodegradation of plastics, such as polystyrene, polyethylene, and expanded polystyrene (EPS), which can result in reduced BIOMASS levels in organisms fed with these plastics. The biodegradation process, facilitated by gut bacteria in mealworms, produces BIOMASS as a byproduct, which contains various bioactive compounds. Additionally, the type of feed and the developmental stage of Tenebrio molitor can also impact BIOMASS. BIOMASS is a crucial concept in understanding the relationship between living organisms, their environment, and the biodegradation of materials, with significant implications for waste management, biodegradation, and the potential use of insects as a food source. The material produced by mealworms, referred to as BIOMASS, can be converted into various materials, including feed, food, biomaterials, chitin, chitosan, fertilizers, and biofuels. Furthermore, BIOMASS can be used to measure the amount of nitrogen fixed by organisms and serves as a biological marker to measure the insects' growth and development, as well as a measure of biodegradation. Overall, BIOMASS is a vital component in the study of biological systems and has far-reaching applications in fields such as ecology, biology, and environmental science.&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass is the material that is incorporated into the body of mealworms during the biodegradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d7f6907ee7ce47b00537b1458fcc029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa2e818c436fabed80b9d3d720ebf491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein content is a measure of the amount of protein in Tenebrio molitor larvae, influenced by factors such as nutrition and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein content is a measure of the amount of protein in mealworms, which changes during experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein content is a nutritional component that is affected by the biodegradation of PE, with PE-fed larvae showing increased protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein content refers to the amount of protein in the biomass of mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The protein content refers to the amount of protein in the biomass and frass of mealworms, varying amongst different treatments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein content is a nutritional component of the mealworm larvae, determined using the Bradford method."&lt;SEP&gt;"Protein content is a measure of the amount of protein in the yellow mealworm samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb3edd44829125161ad624ea793ae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-246606838d14d58d03d733b6250a0460</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOHYDRATE CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbohydrate content is a nutritional component that is affected by the biodegradation of PE, with PE-fed larvae showing reduced carbohydrate content."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAT CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fat Content is a nutrient component of the barley bran, making up 4.5% of its composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat content is a nutritional component that is affected by the biodegradation of PE, with PE-fed larvae showing reduced fat content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat content refers to the amount of fat in the biomass of mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fat content is a measure of the amount of fat in Tenebrio molitor larvae, influenced by factors such as nutrition and biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SOD (Superoxide Dismutase) is an antioxidant enzyme that helps eliminate superoxide anion in organisms, with increased activity in mealworms fed with microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD is an antioxidant enzyme that can scavenge excess peroxidative free radicals, playing a role in protecting against oxidative stress damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD is an antioxidant enzyme that helps to alleviate oxidative stress in mealworm larvae during the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD, or superoxide dismutase, is an enzyme that plays a role in antioxidant systems and helps to scavenge free radicals."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD, or superoxide dismutase, is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in protecting tissues against ROS damage by converting O2- into H2O2 and O2."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD is an enzyme that is involved in the degradation of lignin and other complex organic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD refers to superoxide dismutase, an enzyme measured in the larvae to assess oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"SOD, or superoxide dismutase, is an enzyme that helps to protect against oxidative stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GST is an antioxidant enzyme that helps to alleviate oxidative stress in mealworm larvae during the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"GST, or glutathione S-transferase, is an enzyme that scavenges metabolites of lipid peroxidation and helps to protect against oxidative damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"GST, or glutathione-S-transferase, is an enzyme that scavenges the metabolites of lipid peroxidation and helps alleviate oxidative damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CAT, or catalase, is an enzyme that aids in the elimination of hydrogen peroxide by converting it into water and oxygen."&lt;SEP&gt;"CAT, or catalase, is an enzyme that helps to scavenge free radicals and protect against oxidative damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ROS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ROS (Reactive Oxygen Species) is a measure of oxidative stress in mealworms, which increases when ingesting microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS (Reactive Oxygen Species) is a metabolite that is being measured in the larvae, indicating its importance in the biological process."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS is a measure of oxidative stress in the larvae, and its levels are being evaluated in response to microplastic exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS, or reactive oxygen species, are a type of metabolite that can cause oxidative stress and damage to cellular structures and biomacromolecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS, or reactive oxygen species, are formed during the biodegradation of plastics and can induce oxidative stress in larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS, or reactive oxygen species, are molecules that are generated during oxidative stress and can cause damage to cells and tissues."&lt;SEP&gt;"ROS, or reactive oxygen species, is a measure of oxidative stress in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MDA (Malondialdehyde) is a measure of lipid peroxidation and oxidative damage in mealworms, which increases when ingesting microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA is a metabolite that indicates oxidative damage to membrane lipids, with higher contents found in PE-fed groups compared to the control group."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA refers to malondialdehyde, a metabolite measured in the larvae to assess oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA, or malondialdehyde, is a metabolite that is a product of lipid peroxidation and can be used as a marker of oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA, or malondialdehyde, is a metabolite that is generated during lipid peroxidation and is used as a marker of oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"MDA, or malondialdehyde, is a measure of oxidative stress in organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIOXIDANT SYSTEMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antioxidant systems are biological concepts that can be affected by the ingestion of PS polymers by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antioxidant systems are biological processes that help to protect against oxidative stress and damage caused by free radicals."&lt;SEP&gt;"The antioxidant systems of mealworms are damaged to some extent due to the biodegradation of PS polymers, highlighting the potential risks associated with this process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREE RADICALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Free radicals are molecules that are generated during oxidative stress and can cause damage to cells and tissues."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPID PEROXIDATION PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid peroxidation products are toxic metabolites that are generated during lipid peroxidation, including MDA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPEROXIDE DISMUTASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Superoxide dismutase is an enzyme involved in the degradation of reactive oxygen species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Superoxide dismutase is an enzyme that plays a role in antioxidant systems, helping to scavenge free radicals and protect against oxidative damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLUTATHIONE S-TRANSFERASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glutathione S-transferase is an enzyme that scavenges metabolites of lipid peroxidation and helps to protect against oxidative damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATALASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Catalase is a test used to biochemically characterize the bacterial isolates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catalase is an enzyme that can be produced by certain bacteria, including some species of Bacillus and Stenotrophomonas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catalase is an enzyme that helps to scavenge free radicals and protect against oxidative damage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catalase is an enzyme that is produced by some of the bacterial isolates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Catalase is an enzyme that is positive in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its ability to catalyze the decomposition of hydrogen peroxide."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-55bdcf1b4859e82ab15050837ab539dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDATIVE DAMAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidative damage is a biological process that occurs in Tenebrio molitor larvae when they biodegrade microplastics, resulting in negative physiological responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative damage is a physiological response that can occur in organisms that ingest microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative damage refers to the harm caused to cells and tissues by free radicals and other reactive molecules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSIOLOGICAL PERFORMANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physiological performance refers to the overall health and function of mealworm larvae, including growth, survival, and biomass production."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMASS PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomass production is a biological process that occurs during the biodegradation of EPS by insects such as Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass production refers to the production of biomass by mealworm larvae, including water, total carbohydrate, fat, and protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biomass production refers to the process of producing a large amount of biological material, such as edible insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WATER CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Water content is a measure of the amount of water in Tenebrio molitor larvae, influenced by factors such as nutrition and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water content is a physiological parameter used to assess the health and nutritional status of the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water content is an important factor in the survival of T. molitor larvae, with the water content in agar gel helping their higher survival rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Water content refers to the amount of water in the biomass of mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL CARBOHYDRATE CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Total carbohydrate content refers to the amount of carbohydrates in the biomass of mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMAL DECOMPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermal decomposition is a process that occurs in Styrofoam, resulting in the production of styrene and other metabolites."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermal decomposition is the process by which the thermal stability of materials is studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermal decomposition refers to the breakdown of molecules into smaller components using heat."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROCOSMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microcosms refer to small, controlled environments that mimic the conditions found in nature, such as the gut of mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNCTIONAL MICROORGANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Functional microorganisms refer to the microorganisms that play a role in the biodegradation of PE microplastics, including those found in the gut of mealworm larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CAD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CAD is an antioxidant enzyme that helps to alleviate oxidative stress in mealworm larvae during the biodegradation of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROENVIRONMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut microenvironment is the environment within the mealworm larvae's gut where biodegradation of polyethylene takes place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microenvironment refers to the environment inside the gut of an organism, including the presence of microorganisms, enzymes, and other factors that can affect the digestion and depolymerization of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIOXIDANT ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antioxidant enzymes are a group of enzymes that are being studied in the research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antioxidant enzymes, including SOD, GST, and CAD, are produced in mealworm larvae during the biodegradation of polyethylene, helping to alleviate oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antioxidant enzymes, such as SOD, GST, and CAT, are being measured in the larvae to evaluate their oxidative stress response."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf54b3c2c01c935a178261a31b8ed897&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
    </node>
