    <node id="&quot;EISENIA FETIDA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Eisenia fetida is a genus of earthworms that are being exposed to PS MPs, showing a remarkable ROS increase."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida is a species of earthworm that is capable of biodegrading microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida, also known as earthworms, are macroinvertebrates with poor plastic-degrading ability, showing increased ROS when exposed to PS MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida, also known as the earthworm, is a species of insect that is often used in studies of soil ecology and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida, also known as the earthworm, is a species of insect that has been found to be affected by low-density polyethylene microplastics in soils."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida is a species of earthworm that is affected by the gut toxicity of polystyrene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida is a species of earthworm that can interact with microplastics and is used in studies to understand the effects of microplastics on the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida is a species of earthworm that is affected by the toxicity of polystyrene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida is a genus of earthworms that can experience oxidative damage when exposed to microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida is a species of earthworm that can disintegrate bio-based polyactic acid microplastics into sub-micron microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Eisenia fetida, also known as the earthworm, is an organism that is being studied for its response to microplastics and other pollutants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-825c2784fa66ce67114e4173ed0702f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOIL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A natural environment where microorganisms that can degrade plastics can be found."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a complex ecosystem that supports a wide range of microorganisms and other organisms, and plays a crucial role in the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a physical feature that can contain microplastics and affect the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a natural environment where biodegradation of polystyrene can occur."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a type of environment where microorganisms, including those that can biodegrade plastics, can be found."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a physical feature that can be contaminated with pollutants and can be remediated through biodegradation, as discussed in the study by Bardi et al."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a type of location where microorganisms and soil invertebrates live and are capable of degrading organic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a physical feature that can contain microorganisms that biodegrade materials, such as polystyrene-graft-starch copolymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is the source from which the novel bacterial consortium was isolated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a physical feature that can be affected by microplastics and other toxic substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a natural resource that can be impacted by plastic pollution, which can affect its quality and fertility."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a physical feature that can be affected by the presence of plastic waste, including the potential for reduced fertility and increased pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a type of environment where microorganisms can break down organic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a physical property that can contain microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a component of the environment where plastics are biodegraded by microorganisms and other living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soil is a physical environment where microplastics can be found and can affect the physiology and behavior of organisms that live in it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5d8df2e13d3902379597b08eb0e08db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-043ac4479b542b2eb2620db8d408349b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67425e341a5b2c8102281581fa148554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a</data>
    </node>
