    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotic is a chemical property used to suppress the growth of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic is a substance that inhibits the growth of microorganisms, used to suppress gut microbiota in superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic refers to a substance that can inhibit the growth of microorganisms, which can be affected by biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances that are used to kill or inhibit the growth of microorganisms, and are often used in studies of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances that can affect the growth of microorganisms, including the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic is a type of substance that is being studied in the research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic resistance is not mentioned in the text, however, some plastics may contain additives with antibiotic properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic is a substance that can inhibit the growth of microorganisms, which can affect the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic is a substance that can suppress the growth of gut microbes in T. molitor larvae, used to study the role of gut microbes in PET biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are used to suppress the gut microbiome, demonstrating that the host digestive system can degrade PET independent of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic is mentioned as having an effect on the biodegradation of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic is a substance that is used to suppress the growth of microorganisms in the gut of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic is used to treat mealworms and suppress the growth of nitrogen-fixing bacteria in their guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotics are substances that are used to kill or inhibit the growth of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic is a type of chemical property that can be affected by the presence of microplastics in the environment."</data>
