    <node id="&quot;LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Low-density polyethylene is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain organisms, such as insect larvae, and is a key focus of study in the provided text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-density polyethylene is a type of plastic that is being studied for its biodegradation properties and potential impact on the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-density polyethylene is a type of plastic that is being studied for its biodegradation rates and effects on the life cycle of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;Low-Density Polyethylene, also referred to as LDPE, is a type of plastic that is being extensively studied for its biodegradation properties and potential environmental impact. It is a type of microplastic that can be ingested and metabolized by certain organisms, including the larvae of Tenebrio molitor, also known as mealworms, superworms, and Zophobas atratus larvae. Low-Density Polyethylene is biodegradable by various microorganisms, such as Pseudomonas sp. AKS2 biofilm, Corcyra cephalonica, and Pantoea, as well as certain species of insects, including dark- and yellow-mealworms, which can degrade it via gut microbe-independent depolymerization. Additionally, it can be biodegraded by bacteria, such as those from the species Zophobas aratus and Tenebrio obscurus. Low-Density Polyethylene is used in mulching films and has been found to affect earthworms in soils. The biodegradation of Low-Density Polyethylene by these organisms and microorganisms is an area of ongoing research, with various studies exploring its potential for biodegradation and its potential applications. Mealworms can consume Low-Density Polyethylene at an average rate of 0.00102 mg per day per mealworm, although it is less favorable for mealworm consumption compared to other plastics like polystyrene and polypropylene. Overall, Low-Density Polyethylene is a type of plastic that is biodegradable by certain species of insects and microorganisms, and its biodegradation is being extensively studied to understand its potential environmental impact and applications.&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-density polyethylene is a type of plastic that is commonly used in packaging and other applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Low-density polyethylene is a type of product that can be broken down by microorganisms through biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c4652e08c4ac6887914d0deebe761b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8917166a3e45f4bf51e2e04949f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bc3253e8d41785f994d1c6fcc2b6c47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21d8b17fc7993bee31f7e07e4db97cfa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e478d12101aa862a23f9dfc7ac8896b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af9ad6e808e93b61ec40d6ba4131fda7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08257b9745bccf6dfc5ca860da5a96bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b</data>
