    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBE-INDEPENDENT DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbe-independent depolymerization is a biological process by which microorganisms in the gut of insects such as dark mealworms break down plastics without the help of microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbe-independent depolymerization is a process by which certain microorganisms can break down plastics without the need for gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbe-independent depolymerization is a process by which certain organisms can break down plastics without the help of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbe-independent depolymerization is a process by which certain species of insects, including Tenebrio molitor, are able to break down plastics without the aid of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbe-independent depolymerization is a process by which certain microorganisms, such as Tenebrio molitor, break down plastics without the aid of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbe-independent depolymerization is a process by which insects break down plastics into simpler compounds without the help of microorganisms in their gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which LDPE is broken down by Tenebrio obscurus and Tenebrio molitor without the help of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbe-independent depolymerization is a biological process that involves the breakdown of plastics by microorganisms without the need for gut microbes."</data>
