    <node id="&quot;MINERALIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mineralization is a biological process by which mealworms convert plastics into inorganic compounds, resulting in the complete breakdown of the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization is the process by which microorganisms break down organic materials, such as polystyrene, into inorganic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization is the process by which microorganisms break down organic matter into inorganic compounds, such as carbon dioxide and water."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization is the process by which microorganisms convert organic compounds into inorganic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;MINERALIZATION is a biological process by which microorganisms, such as superworms, mealworms, and yellow mealworms, break down organic materials, including plastics, polystyrene, and other organic compounds, into inorganic compounds, such as carbon dioxide, water, and other simple compounds. This process is an important aspect of biodegradation, where organic matter is converted into inorganic matter, and it can be affected by consuming materials like polystyrene. MINERALIZATION occurs in various organisms and can be an effective method for degrading certain types of plastics, including PET and Styrofoam. The process involves the conversion of organic substances into inorganic substances and is a crucial step in the biodegradation of plastic waste. MINERALIZATION can also refer to the process by which microplastics and nanoplastics are converted into inorganic compounds, and it is the final step in the breakdown of organic matter, where the products of depolymerization are further broken down into simple compounds like CO2. Additionally, MINERALIZATION is used to determine the total content of protein in organic substances. Overall, MINERALIZATION is a vital process that helps to convert organic compounds into inorganic compounds, reducing the amount of plastic waste in the environment. It is a key aspect of plastic degradation and is being studied for its role in degrading polystyrene and other organic materials.&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization is the process of converting organic compounds into inorganic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization is the process by which organic substances are broken down into inorganic compounds, such as carbon dioxide and water."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization is a biological process that converts organic substances into inorganic substances, such as carbon dioxide and water."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization is the process by which organic matter is converted into inorganic matter, and it is being studied in the context of polystyrene degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1684575ed5f73a2ebe1adc7fbbb3b942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81b6237c84f002117fbfe7575d9cdd6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8cc3aa81b03290b589ccf0a1548ca0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3</data>
