    <node id="&quot;APOPTOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Apoptosis is a biological process that can occur in mealworms as a result of microplastic-induced oxidative stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis is a biological process that is affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis is a biological process that is affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) in mealworms, as indicated by the presence of lipids related to cell apoptosis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis is a process of programmed cell death, which is increased in polystyrene-fed insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis is the process of programmed cell death, which can be triggered by certain stimuli, such as exposure to microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis refers to the process of programmed cell death, and is often measured using various biological assays, including the Muse Annexin V &amp; Dead Cell Kit."&lt;SEP&gt;"Apoptosis refers to the process of programmed cell death, studied in the context of insect health status and the effects of polystyrene foam on the insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5caa980be616efa237401a957b69019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6cbb8ccec16f4756fa7a1fb365886d9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549</data>
    </node>
