    <node id="&quot;ENZYMATIC ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymatic activity is a biological function that is modified in mealworms fed a diet containing polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is a biological process that is affected by the different diets, with varying levels of activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is a measure of the ability of enzymes to break down plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the action of enzymes that break down polystyrene (PS) during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The enzymatic activity of gut bacteria in mealworm larvae changes depending on the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is related to the degradation of PS and is influenced by the presence of mannose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is the biological process by which the mealworm larvae break down the polystyrene into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the biological process by which Tenebrio molitor larvae break down PS into smaller organic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the ability of microorganisms to produce enzymes that break down complex materials, such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the ability of enzymes to catalyze specific chemical reactions, such as those involved in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is a measure of the ability of enzymes to catalyze chemical reactions, such as biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the ability of enzymes to catalyze specific chemical reactions, and is crucial for the biodegradation of polystyrene by Achromobacter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is modified in mealworms fed a diet containing polystyrene (PS), leading to changes in protein, nitrogen, and lipid populations."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity refers to the biological process by which enzymes break down substances, in this case, PS, with the presence of bran and water affecting the enzymatic activity and microbial activity in the insects' gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic activity is the 