      <data key="d1">"Oatmeal is a control feed used in the study, with a loss of 31.7% in substrate mass after 70 days of mealworm larvae feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a control feed used in the study, with a loss of 31.7% in substrate mass after 70 days of mealworm larvae feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of nutrient that is being used as a control group to feed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of feed given to Tenebrio molitor, resulting in significant differences in growth and development compared to other feed types."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of food that is used in the OAT diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of food used as a control diet for mealworms, providing a basis for comparison with other diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of food used as a diet for mealworms, resulting in a natural life cycle and lower mortality rates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of nutrient used as a diet for insects, resulting in the lowest counts of larvae at the last measurement, but also the highest number of pupae and adults emerging during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of food being used as a control in the study of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is used as a control food source for the mealworms in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a food source used in the study as a control, with mealworms showing a significant mass change when fed oatmeal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of food that is used as a control diet for the mealworms in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of food used to feed mealworms in studies, providing them with nutrients for growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a food source given to the larvae, served every 10 days and left for 24 hours before removal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a nutrient that is being used as a supplement to the PS diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of food that is being used to feed the T. molitor larvae in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oatmeal is a type of nutrient that is being used as a supplement to enhance the survival and growth of mealworms."</data>
