      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrosomonadales are an order of bacteria that contribute to the nitrification process, with their presence indicating an increase in nitrifying potential in the digestive system microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales are positively correlated with the PS diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of bacteria that are involved in nitrification and are found in the digestive tract of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of bacteria that includes the genus Nitrosomonas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of bacteria that is characteristic of the PS diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of bacteria that is found in the gut microbiome, with a mean abundance of 1.6%."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of microorganisms found in the microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of bacteria that includes the genus Nitrosomonas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrosomonadales is an order of bacteria that is involved in nitrification and is found in the digestive tract of T. molitor."</data>
