    <node id="&quot;ENTOMOPLASMATALES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Entomoplasmatales are an order of bacteria that are associated with various metabolic processes, including the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria mentioned in the study as a symbiont that can promote indirect reassimilation of NH3 and atmospheric nitrogen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that are involved in symbiotic relationships with insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that includes the genus Spiroplasma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order that includes families such as Spiroplasmataceae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that is characteristic of the PE-oxo diet and is often found in the digestive system of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that is found in the gut microbiome, with a mean abundance of 1.1%."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of microorganisms found in the microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is a type of bacteria that can fix nitrogen and is found in the gut of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that includes the genus Spiroplasma."&lt;SEP&gt;"Entomoplasmatales is an order of bacteria that is involved in symbiotic relationships with insects."</data>
