    <node id="&quot;CHRYSEOBACTERIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chryseobacterium is a bacterium that can be found in the gut microbiome of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chryseobacterium is a genus of bacteria that belongs to the order Flavobacteriales."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chryseobacterium is a genus of microorganisms that is associated with the PU diet and is a member of the Bacteroidetes phylum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chryseobacterium is a type of bacteria that can be associated with the degradation of polyurethane (PU)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chryseobacterium is a genus of bacteria that belongs to the order Flavobacteriales."</data>
