    <node id="&quot;ENTEROCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of bacteria"&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria that belongs to the order Lactobacillales."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is associated with PE diet in the gut of yellow and black mealworms, and its relative abundance increases in PS-fed superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria that is abundant in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor and may be involved in biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a type of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a genus of microorganisms that is associated with the PU diet and is a lactic acid bacterium that is known to be present in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a type of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of the Tenebrio species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria that is commonly found in the gut microbiomes of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a type of microorganism that can be found in the gut microbiome of insect larvae, including superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria that was found to have a significant difference in relative abundance between the PE and bran diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a type of microorganism that is present in the gut microbiome of mealworms and may play a role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria that has been identified in the gut of mealworms and plays a role in the biodegradation of styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a type of bacteria present in the gut of insect larvae that can degrade PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a type of bacteria that has been found in the gut microbiota of the three species of insect larvae and may play a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a type of bacteria that is found in the gut microbiome of all three species of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a type of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a bacterium that is associated with the production of esterases, indicating its role in the degradation of indoxacarb insecticide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterococcus is a genus of bacteria that belongs to the order Lactobacillales."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64e35cb810117768309e5f4db5d7e6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe</data>
