    <node id="&quot;SPIROPLASMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria that belongs to the order Entomoplasmatales."&lt;SEP&gt;Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria that belongs to the order Entomoplasmatales. It is a type of microorganism that is commonly found in the gut microbiomes of yellow mealworms and dark mealworms, particularly in the posterior gut of mealworms. Spiroplasma is a dominant genus in the gut microbiome of mealworms, including Tenebrio molitor, and is not harmful to them. It is also a dominant genus in polypropylene-fed groups, accounting for a significant relative abundance, and is associated with the biodegradation of plastics, including polyethylene and polypropylene. Spiroplasma is capable of living in anaerobic conditions and has been identified as a key player in the degradation of plastic polymers. Although it is known to be an insect pathogen, Spiroplasma does not cause harm to T. molitor larvae. Overall, Spiroplasma is a genus of bacteria that plays a significant role in the gut microbiome of mealworms and has the potential to contribute to the biodegradation of plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54f22136b514092aeeb2f431170b6ed6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222</data>
