    <node id="&quot;LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">Larvae are a developmental stage of insects, such as T. molitor, Tenebrio obscurus, Zophobas atratus, and mealworms, with specific energy requirements. They are a life stage where various enzymes have been measured, indicating their role in certain biological processes. Larvae are the early stages of insects that are being used to study the degradation of various materials, such as polystyrene, polypropylene, polyethylene, high-density polyethylene, polyethylene terephthalate, and polyurethane. They are capable of biodegrading certain materials, with the gut microbiome of larvae, particularly those of T. molitor, found to be capable of degrading polyethylene terephthalate, polystyrene, and other microplastics, with the help of nitrogen-fixing bacteria. Larvae are also capable of feeding on extracellular polymeric substances and are being used to study the biodegradation of various plastics under different conditions. 

During this stage, larvae undergo significant development and growth, and the type of feed provided to them can affect their development, leading to mortality, cannibalism, and changes in nutritional parameters. Physiological parameters such as survival rate, cannibal rate, and pupation rate are being studied in larvae to understand the effects of plastic diet on their growth and survival. Larvae are playing a significant role in biodegradation experiments and are being extensively studied for their ability to consume and degrade various types of plastics, including polyethylene, and their potential impact on food security. They are also capable of degrading vinyl plastics and are being used in experiments to study polypropylene consumption, microbial community analysis, and biodegradation of various materials.

Larvae are the immature stages of insects, including darkling beetles and yellow mealworms, that are capable of biodegrading plastics, and their ability to digest and biodegrade plastics makes them a crucial part of biodegradation research. They are being studied for their growth and survival patterns, growth and reserve dynamics, and ability to consume and break down polystyrene. The survival and development of larvae are being influenced by various factors such as feeding conditions and energy reserves, and they are being fed with different substances to study their growth and development. Overall, larvae are a critical life stage of insects, characterized by growth and development before pupation, and their study is essential for understanding their role in biodegradation</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f488d8d4434d57d1a775a22333caa04b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39598f698094d1663ca3438bc143bc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b3e57543d6b365fff3ef2b14ddb309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5134944e002326fa5ca136c470d99e2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6afbb58ebe9108893daf7e65d59fac39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91df729b04e3d570337e02872cf1c38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54e547b0e77432a65a8a9804c44c5d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3