    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas is a bacterium that is associated with the production of esterases, indicating its significance in the degradation of indoxacarb insecticide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is a genus of bacteria that includes many nitrogen-fixing species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is a genus of bacteria that includes strains with potential for PS biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is a type of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is a type of microorganism used in the incubation of PP films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas is another genus of bacteria known for its ability to degrade various organic compounds, potentially including plastics like polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;Pseudomonas is a genus of Gram-negative bacteria that is significantly associated with the degradation of various plastics and organic compounds. Pseudomonas is present in the gut of yellow mealworms and Tenebrio molitor larvae, where it has been found to have an increased relative abundance in the polypropylene (PP)-fed group and is dominant in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae fed with polypropylene. The genus is also over-represented in polystyrene (PS) samples and is capable of metabolizing styrene and degrading low-density polyethylene (LDPE), polyurethane (PU), and other chemicals. Pseudomonas has been isolated from Tenebrio molitor, where it has shown biodegradable activity against bioplastic, and is present in the gut microbiome of mealworms, where it is associated with the degradation of polyethylene microplastics. However, the abundance of Pseudomonas is decreased in the gut microbiota of mealworms fed with PVC. The genus includes species like Pseudomonas reinekei, which is involved in the degradation of chloroaromatic compounds. Pseudomonas is also known for its ability to produce enzymes such as laccase, which is involved in the degradation of synthetic textile dyes, and esterases, which are responsible for the degradation of indoxacarb insecticide and potentially polystyrene. Overall, Pseudomonas plays a significant role in the biodegradation of various plastics and organic compounds, including polystyrene, low-density polyethylene, polyurethane, and styrene, and is an important component of the gut microbiome of certain insect species, making it a key player in environmental cleanup and microbiome research.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6746a90a5be233f46211ddf406c02e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a21a8e638d3972014f836efe8aa62e3c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2122660fcfebecf752000198a16f222&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b68a8917166a3e45f4bf51e2e04949f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188daf7716cd1d683a79562bf4d6ab90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2aeb4d96b02258056c16688ea13a9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56</data>
