    <node id="&quot;LIPASES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipases are a type of enzyme produced by Achromobacter species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are a type of enzyme that breaks down lipids, a type of biomolecule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are a type of enzyme that can be used for the synthesis and degradation of polymers, offering a sustainable and efficient method."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes that have been found to degrade polystyrene, indicating their potential role in the degradation of this product."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are a type of enzyme that is involved in the degradation of polyurethane, particularly in the hydrolysis of PU bonds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes being investigated for their ability to biodegrade polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are enzymes that break specific bonds in polyurethane molecules and were measured in the gut of the mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are a type of enzyme that can break down PLA polymers via enzymatic hydrolysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases is an enzyme that is involved in the degradation of lignin and other complex organic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases are a type of extracellular enzyme produced by bacterial cells, capable of breaking down lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipases is an enzyme that is produced by Pseudomonas aeruginosa M8."</data>
