    <node id="&quot;PANTOEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria found in the digestive tracts of T. molitor adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria found in the larvae of T. molitor fed polyethylene diets, potentially participating in waste degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria that is enriched in the bran group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria that has been found to degrade plastics such as low-density polyethylene, indicating its potential role in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria that is found in the digestive tracts of T. molitor, and is capable of degrading PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria from which the species Mixta calida, Mixta gaviniae, Mixta intestinalis, and Mixta theicola were reclassified into the genus Mixta."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria that has been identified in the gut of mealworms and plays a role in the biodegradation of styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a genus of bacteria that includes many nitrogen-fixing species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pantoea is a type of bacteria that can degrade polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d47c76e5149ac059b1960b533c9e99a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0855091c2b50520d68971a532789a9a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d</data>
    </node>
