    <node id="&quot;ATMOSPHERIC NITROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Atmospheric nitrogen is a chemical compound mentioned in the study as a substance that can be fixed by nitrogenase."&lt;SEP&gt;"Atmospheric nitrogen is converted into a usable form by the nitrogen-fixing activity of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Atmospheric nitrogen is the nitrogen present in the air, used as a reference for measuring nitrogen isotope compositions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Atmospheric nitrogen is the nitrogen present in the air, which is fixed by gut bacteria and used by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Atmospheric nitrogen is a nutrient that can be fixed by certain microorganisms."</data>
