    <node id="&quot;BRANDON ET AL.&quot;&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Brandon et al. are researchers who published a study on the biodegradation of PE by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. are researchers whose previous reports are referenced in the methods and procedures for the collection and analysis of the residual polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. is a reference cited in the study, providing information on the biodegradation of polyethylene and plastic mixtures in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. refers to a research group that has studied the biodegradation of plastics by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. refers to a research group that has published studies on the biodegradation of polyethylene and polystyrene by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. is a group of researchers who have studied the biodegradation of EPS by insects such as Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. is a research group that has studied the chemical compositions of mealworm guts after consuming plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Brandon et al. is a research group that has studied the gut microbiome of insects and its relation to plastic degradation."</data>
