      <data key="d1">"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme involved in the degradation of certain compounds, with its expression levels varying in response to different substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme that has been detected in culturable gut bacterial flora isolated from diamondback moth, Plutella xylostella, and may play a role in indoxylcarb degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme that is overexpressed in G. mellonella larvae fed on beeswax, and is involved in the degradation of short-chain fatty acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme that is involved in the degradation of PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme that is involved in the degradation of lignin and other complex organic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme produced by Thermobifida fusca KWS for the hydrolysis of cyclic poly(ethylene terephthalate) trimers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme that is active toward PET oligomers and is involved in the degradation of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylesterase is an enzyme that is involved in the degradation of PET oligomers, and is found in the gut bacteria of larvae fed with PET."</data>
