      <data key="d1">"Chitin is a biological compound found in insects, such as mealworms, and can be extracted and used for various purposes, including as a fertilizer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a biological marker that can be found in the frass of mealworms and superworms, and may have growth-promoting effects on plants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a biological marker that can be found in worm frass, with potential applications in fertilization and plant growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component of superworm frass that can support rooting in plants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a product of Tenebrio molitor (TM) biomass that has various applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitinase is involved in the degradation of chitin waste by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component of the insect cuticle, detected in the frass of superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a component of the insect cuticle, detected in the fecula using 13C CP/MAS NMR."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a type of metabolite that is involved in degradation processes in insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chitin is a biological marker that can be found in melted skeletons and ingested by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
    </node>
