      <data key="d2">chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c68f3ddf96d927254424a036cd8b9acf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial community is a group of microorganisms that live in a given environment, such as a wastewater treatment plant, and play a crucial role in the treatment of wastewater."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wastewater treatment is a process that can remove pollutants, including micropollutants, from water."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wastewater treatment is a process that involves the management of sewage sludge and scum, with its operations and costs being relevant to the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wastewater treatment is the process of removing pollutants and contaminants from water, including the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wastewater treatment is a biological process that involves the removal of microplastics and other pollutants from wastewater."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wastewater treatment is a biological process that uses microorganisms to clean up pollutants in wastewater."</data>
