    <node id="&quot;PRIESTIA MEGATERIUM S1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium isolated from Tenebrio molitor, capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Priestia megaterium S1 is a microorganism that exhibits biodegradation capabilities over PE and PS beads."&lt;SEP&gt;"Priestia megaterium S1 is a polymer degrading gut microbe isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae fed on Styrofoam, capable of degrading PE and PS beads."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYROFOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrofoam is a type of plastic material that is commonly used in packaging and is biodegradable by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;STYROFOAM is a type of plastic material, specifically a trade name for polystyrene (PS) foam, a type of expanded polystyrene. It is commonly used as a packaging material and for insulating building elevations, known for being a durable single-use plastic. Recent studies have explored its potential biodegradation by certain insects, such as mealworms, including the species Tenebrio molitor L., and superworms, which can consume and degrade it. The degradation process can be facilitated by the gut microbiota of these insects, with a retention time of 12-15 hours in their gut. This biodegradation process can potentially allow for the safe use of STYROFOAM in animal or human feeding. STYROFOAM can be ingested by mealworms, affecting their nutritional composition and potentially serving as an energy source. The material can also be biodepolymerized by Tenebrio molitor and biodegraded by mealworms, with a significant weight loss at 360-480 °C. Additionally, STYROFOAM has been used as a sole diet for mealworms in various studies to examine its biodegradation potential and effects on the insects' nutritional composition. The biodegradation of STYROFOAM by microorganisms in the gut of the larvae has also been observed, resulting in a significant decrease in molecular weight after degradation. Overall, STYROFOAM is a type of plastic product that can be degraded by certain insects, making it a potential candidate for sustainable waste management solutions. Furthermore, research has shown that mealworms, including the species Tenebrio molitor, have the ability to fix nitrogen while consuming STYROFOAM, and the presence of gut nitrogen-fixing bacteria is associated with the consumption of STYROFOAM by mealworms.&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrofoam is a type of polystyrene foam that is widely used for packaging and insulation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea4f92fecc6ac55379b7db07587354ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c8f677b3b4d06e07d3a58446375133fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1498160e7767dd16008724d09b2ac64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df4c8c66bfbbfc37ed842f53d2b8796c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2961e2aad708e7b78a585260097b4d2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d6a80044bea074bdbcb68f489aa8af0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16S RRNA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16S rRNA is a biological marker used to identify and classify microorganisms in the gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a gene used as a marker for bacterial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a genetic marker used to characterize and identify microorganisms, including Priestia megaterium S1."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a type of RNA that can be used to analyze the bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a genetic marker used to analyze the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a type of genetic material used for phylogenetic analysis and identification of bacterial strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA is a type of gene used to analyze the bacterial diversity in the larval gut of yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31b36e69e51416db099951b925beff9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BARLEY BRAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Barley bran is a nutrient source provided to the Tenebrio molitor larvae in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Barley bran is a nutrient source used to feed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Barley bran is a nutrient-rich substance used to feed mealworms, containing protein and lipid."&lt;SEP&gt;"Barley bran is a type of feed consumed by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Barley bran is a nutrient that is used to supplement the diet of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3d7160b00e54118a03f0273d60bfe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3646a65acc7cbdc1d20742888b17613a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"pH is a chemical property that affects the growth of bacteria, with an ideal range for the culturing of bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a measure of the acidity or basicity of a solution, affecting the growth and activity of microorganisms like Priestia megaterium S1."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a measure of the acidity or basicity of a solution, with a pH of 6.5 being optimal for Priestia megaterium S1 growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a physical property that affects the growth of PM S1, with optimal growth at pH 7.0."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a measure of the acidity or basicity of a solution, with a range of 7.2 to 7.6 being suitable for Blood Agar."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a measure of the acidity or basicity of the frass, with values of 7.95 for white EPS frass and 7.74 for grey EPS frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a physical property that affects the growth of bacteria, with different species having optimal pH ranges."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a chemical property that is affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a measure of the acidity or basicity of a solution, being measured in the insects' frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is a physical characteristic used to control the environment of the Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"pH is an important factor in the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms, although the optimal pH range is not specified in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7df3b1ec42b9ac5c08513c3b568a399&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TEMPERATURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Temperature is a physical property being controlled in the experiment, with its effects on the larvae's nutritional values and fatty acid profiles being analyzed."&lt;SEP&gt;Temperature is a physical property that affects the growth, development, and behavior of various organisms, including microorganisms like Priestia megaterium S1 and insects such as Tenebrio molitor larvae, also known as mealworms. It is a measure of the thermal energy of a system and has a significant impact on the biodegradation process, including the degradation of materials like polystyrene. Temperature influences the eating habits and mobility of mealworms, with colder temperatures resulting in slower movement and eating. For Priestia megaterium S1, a temperature of 28°C is optimal for growth, while for mealworms, temperatures between 25-28°C are optimal for growth, development, and biodegradation efficiency. Temperature is a critical factor in controlling the environment of Tenebrio molitor larvae and is often controlled in experimental setups, with set points ranging from 24-28°C. Different species of microorganisms and insects have optimal growth temperatures, and temperature affects the rate of biodegradation, with optimal biodegradation occurring at 25°C. Overall, Temperature plays a crucial role in the growth, activity, and survival of various organisms, as well as the degradation of materials, and its control is essential in experimental setups to study its effects on microplastic pollution, biodegradation, and other biological processes.&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature is a physical property that is maintained at 37 °C throughout the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature is a physical property that affects the growth of microorganisms in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Temperature is a physical property that affects the biodegradation of plastics in soil and other environments."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6d7e47d05442ff6cd0cf042db9974f2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6b4ab01931acbc7aa9c77cd03531c57e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5cbd81fc528c18f42514a2a74d4921e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HDPE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HDPE (high-density polyethylene) is a type of plastic that is biodegraded by some organisms, resulting in the formation of microplastics and potentially nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"HDPE is a type of plastic that undergoes biodegradation, similar to LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;HDPE, or High-Density Polyethylene, is a type of plastic material that is being studied for its biodegradation properties and potential environmental impact. It is a type of polyethylene with long linear chains, minimal branching, and high crystallinity, which affects its degradability and suitability for various applications. HDPE is commonly used in packaging and other applications, but it is difficult to degrade in the natural environment due to its physicochemical characteristics, including high molecular weight and hydrophobicity. However, HDPE can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, such as Priestia megaterium S1, PM, the strain PELW2042, and Achromobacter xylosoxidans, which can cause changes in its chemical structure and molecular weight over time. Additionally, HDPE can be biodegraded by larvae of certain insect species, including Tenebrio molitor, Tenebrio obscurus, and mealworms, with mealworms having an average consumption rate of 0.00281 mg per day per mealworm. The biodegradability of HDPE is influenced by its physical properties, such as molecular weight and crystallinity, and it is generally considered to be less biodegradable than LDPE, leading to higher toxicity in invertebrates. HDPE has a high degree of crystallinity, linear chains, and low level of short chain branching, resulting in strong intermolecular forces, and it has higher crystallinity and density than LDPE, contributing to its different properties and applications. Despite its resistance to biodegradation, HDPE is being studied for its potential to be broken down by various microorganisms and insect species, with the goal of reducing its environmental impact and improving its sustainability. Overall, HDPE is a complex material with unique properties and challenges, and further research is needed to fully understand its biodegradation and environmental fate.&lt;SEP&gt;"HDPE, or high-density polyethylene, is a type of plastic that can be degraded by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-970b4f5f0c494fbc90aab36156ecc044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-602bba09eb2c3