    <node id="&quot;PETROLEUM-BASED PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Petroleum-Based Plastics are a type of plastic that is derived from petroleum."&lt;SEP&gt;"Petroleum-based plastics are a type of plastic material that is widely used and contributes to plastic pollution due to its slow biodegradation rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Petroleum-based plastics are a type of plastic that includes polystyrene and is known to be resistant to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Petroleum-based plastics are a type of plastic that is recalcitrant and difficult to degrade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Petroleum-based plastics, such as PS, PE, and PVC, are biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Petroleum-based plastics, such as polyethylene, polyvinyl chloride, and polypropylene, are widely used in various industries and daily life, but their degradation is a significant environmental concern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Petroleum-based plastics are a type of plastic that is widely used and includes PE, PP, PVC, PUR, PET, and PS."</data>
