    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Mealworm, also known as Tenebrio molitor, is an insect that plays a significant role in the biodegradation of plastics. The mealworm is capable of hosting microorganisms that can biodegrade plastics, and its gut microbiome is used to degrade various types of plastics, including polyethylene, polystyrene, and expanded foam plastics. Mealworms have been found to consume and degrade rigid microplastics, and their larvae are capable of biodegrading polyethylene. The insect's gut microbiome plays a crucial role in the biodegradation process, and its characteristics, such as feeding habits and morphological identification, make it an ideal subject for study. Mealworms are being used as a degradation reactor in recalcitrant microplastic waste management and are being fed with different diets, including synthetic polymers and natural food, to study their survival and development. Additionally, mealworms are being used as an insect model to study the impact of plastics on central carbon metabolism and the effects of plastics on metabolism and microbiota. Overall, mealworms have the capacity to biodegrade certain types of plastics, and their unique characteristics make them a valuable tool in the study of biodegradation and plastic waste management.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-110013d54a5fd492446b1fe049a60fe9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d03c0a2dce3f57876d209a83a2e82a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8518832c2d3e002c8acf71795e306144&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdf2753a9a78b282c1ca2c0539e3203d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3d7160b00e54118a03f0273d60bfe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365</data>
    </node>
