    <node id="&quot;FTIR SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNIQUE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR Spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of organic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR Spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of substances, in this case, LDPE beads."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR Spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the chemical structure of PS beads before and after treatment with PM S1."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a biochemical measure used to analyze the molecular structure of a substance, such as LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the chemical structure of PS beads before and after treatment with PM S1."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a biochemical measure used to analyze the chemical composition of microplastics before and after metabolism by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy, or Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy, is a technique being used to analyze the chemical alterations at the surface of PVC fragments."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a method used to analyze the chemical composition of evolved gaseous compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the gaseous compounds produced during the thermal decomposition of the control PS and the fecula."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of materials, including the waste consumed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a biochemical measure used to analyze the surface morphology of PS/CS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy was used to characterize the functional groups of the PS and CS feedstocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a biochemical measure used to identify the primary functional groups of virgin PE-MPs compared to frass residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the structural characteristics of plastic debris in the marine environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be41a05c5e519995f6622e2258511b70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939fc2ea222a49f84f9bdc11f9801367&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb00229bf45a3bd9b8a17e10a1c93d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SEM ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"SEM analysis is a biochemical measure used to analyze the surface structure and texture of a substance, such as LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM analysis is a technique used to analyze the surface morphology of the polyurethane foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"SEM analysis is a technology used to study the surface morphology of PS/CS samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3d2baf02fdfbafa95ded13de61aaaa1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillaceae is a bacterial family that is significantly more abundant in PS samples than in CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillaceae is a family of bacteria that includes Virgibacillus sp. and Pseudogracilbacillus, which appeared to be overrepresented in PS samples compared to CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillaceae is a family of bacteria that includes genera such as Bacillus, Metabacillus, and Cytobacillus, which are related to the mealworm gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillaceae is the family to which PM S1 belongs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillaceae is a family of bacteria that is present in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillaceae is a family that includes species such as Bacillus alkalinitrilicus and Bacillus velezensis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillaceae is a family of bacteria that is enriched in the bran group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillaceae is a family of bacteria that is present in the anterior gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillaceae is a family of bacteria that includes Bacillus amyloliquefaciens."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;16 S RRNA GENE SEQUENCING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16 s rRNA gene sequencing is a genetic concept used to determine the phylogenetic relationship between different species of bacteria, such as mealworm gut bacteria and Prestia megaterium S1 (ON024787)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16a478461d1471ca083f90b3f8e7456e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PM refers to a microorganism that is capable of degrading plastic materials, such as LDPE, HDPE, and PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3646a65acc7cbdc1d20742888b17613a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STURM TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sturm test is a method used to determine the biodegradation of plastic materials by measuring the amount of CO2 generated."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3646a65acc7cbdc1d20742888b17613a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CO2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CO2 is a gas that is produced during the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;CO2, or carbon dioxide, is a metabolite and byproduct that is produced during the biodegradation of various plastic materials, including polyethylene, polystyrene, polyurethane, and PET, by different organisms such as mealworms, Tenebrio molitor, microorganisms, and superworms. The production of CO2 is an indicator of energy production and is important for understanding the degradation process of these plastics. CO2 is also a compound that is formed during the mineralization of polystyrene and is released as a gas during the biodegradation process. Additionally, CO2 is produced by the gut microbiome during respiration and is a product of the degradation of Styrofoam by superworms, as measured in respirometry tests. The biodegradation of plastics by yellow mealworms, T. molitor, and T. obscurus also results in the production of CO2. Overall, CO2 is a key metabolite that is produced during the biodegradation of plastics, with implications for biodegradation and waste management.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fbbfcf279533f78737706f5751ee5a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4304c39ef3427872131caf77e7cdb438&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-237dcdbb783e27ec19d2ebc6b854b744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3646a65acc7cbdc1d20742888b17613a</data>
    </node>
