    <node id="&quot;SOY PROTEIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Soy protein is a nutrient source used to feed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soy protein is a nutrient-rich co-diet used for the growth of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soy protein is a type of nutrient that can be used as a co-diet with PS to enhance its consumption by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soy protein is a nutritious feed supplement that can enhance the degradation rate of plastics by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soy protein is a nutrient supplement that increases the rate of PS degradation when fed to mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soy protein is a type of nutrient that is being used as a feed supplement for the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soy protein is another nutritional supplement used to support the growth and plastic degradation abilities of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soy protein is another source of nutrition that can be added to the diet of mealworms to facilitate faster rates of polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Soy protein is a type of nutrient that is mentioned as a comparison to oatmeal in terms of its effect on mealworm survival and growth."</data>
