      <data key="d1">"16S rRNA Sequencing is a technique used to identify and characterize microorganisms based on their genetic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA sequencing is a molecular technique used to identify the bacterial isolates."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA sequencing is a technique used to analyze the gut microbial composition of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA sequencing is a technique used to analyze the community of microorganisms in a sample, including the gut microbiome of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S rRNA sequencing is a biological process used to identify the taxonomic species of the isolated microorganisms."</data>
