    <node id="&quot;CARBON SOURCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon source is a nutrient required for the growth of microorganisms, including strains NyZ450 and NyZ451."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon source is a nutrient required for the growth of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carbon source is a nutrient that affects the growth of PM S1, with LDPE, HDPE, and PS used as carbon sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon source is a nutrient that is required by microorganisms, such as Klebsiella oxytoca, to survive and carry out their metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon source refers to the substance that provides carbon for microbial growth and respiration, such as polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The carbon source is a type of nutrient that can be used by microorganisms, including the mealworm gut microbiome, to support growth and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon source is a nutrient that is utilized by the larvae and gut bacteria for energy and growth, particularly in the degradation of polypropylene (PP)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon source is a type of nutrient that is provided by microplastics, but is insufficient for the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae."</data>
