    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus is a bacterium that is associated with the production of esterases, indicating its significance in the degradation of indoxacarb insecticide."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus is a genus of bacteria that can decompose micro-sized polyethylene (PE) efficiently."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus is a genus of bacteria that has been found to degrade polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;Bacillus is a genus of bacteria that includes various species capable of degrading different types of plastic waste, such as polyethylene (PE), polypropylene (PP), polystyrene (PS), and high-density polyethylene (HDPE). The genus Bacillus has been found to have styrene-degrading abilities and is known for its ability to degrade polystyrene, with many species contributing to this process. Bacillus is commonly found in the digestive tracts of certain insects, including Tenebrio molitor (mealworms) and termites, where it plays a role in the biodegradation of plastics, including styrofoam. The genus Bacillus has been identified as a key player in the degradation of various plastics, with some species producing enzymes like esterase, which is associated with high impact polystyrene degradation. Additionally, Bacillus has been studied for its potential in degrading plastics, including polypropylene, and has been used in the incubation of PP films. Some species of Bacillus, such as strain PELW2042, have been specifically identified as having the ability to biodegrade HDPE. The abundance of Bacillus has been found to increase in PS-fed larvae and decrease in the gut microbiota of mealworms fed with PVC. Overall, Bacillus is a genus of microorganisms that exhibits high abundance in the gut of insects fed with certain plastics and is capable of producing enzymes that contribute to the degradation of various types of plastic waste.&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus is a genus of bacteria that has been found to be capable of biodegrading polyethylene mulching films."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681a7143730d41e569d0d76a926eb069&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6eb7955dc484d5f656e1be7b406abb3a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81f09d7c1a5d91a7a0b4766ca0e47f56</data>
    </node>
