      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The 16S rRNA gene sequence is used to identify the isolate S1 and its relationship to other bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOFILM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A biofilm is a complex community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface, in this case, the PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a biological concept that refers to the colonization of PM S1 on the surface of LDPE, HDPE, and PS beads."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that can form on the surface of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface and can contribute to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that form on the surface of plastic and enhance its degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm refers to the complex community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface and work together to break down organic substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a complex community of microorganisms that adhere to surfaces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that adheres to the surface of HDPE film, indicating the ability of bacteria to use insoluble materials efficiently."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface, such as PS, and can play a role in the degradation of the material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a type of biological structure that can be formed by certain bacteria, including some species of Bacillus and Stenotrophomonas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm refers to the community of microorganisms that forms on the surface of materials, contributing to the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface and play a role in the degradation of PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface, in this case, polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface, playing a role in biodegradation and other biological processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface, such as the polyethylene-degrading bacterium Rhodococcus ruber."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a complex community of microorganisms that can create a protective environment for themselves and degrade synthetic products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a biological concept that refers to the formation of a complex community of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface, in this case, the surface of polystyrene plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a biological concept that refers to a community of microorganisms that adhere to a surface, such as polystyrene film."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biofilm is a layer of microorganisms that attaches to a surface."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7432cb0d6c74fd2dd80b065fbad26b4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af57b5211422531c03b0cbcfded1b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d4e1982efefa47339205e972562b51f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc75b7e672a7f7c036713dfa2675d79a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c6dfb08bb454e8ff642e7975ba7af10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOD TEST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The BOD test is a biochemical measure that assesses the oxygen demand of microorganisms, with PM S1 showing a BOD of 7.4 mg/l for LDPE, 7.2 mg/l for HDPE, and 6.7 mg/l for PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2fd075a78abe1dca64ddea928d3f94b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBON DIOXIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbon dioxide is a byproduct of the biodegradation of EPS by gut bacteria in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a byproduct of the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a metabolite that is produced during the decomposition of the fecula."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a product of the biodegradation of Styrofoam, resulting from the mineralization of the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a byproduct of the plastic degradation process by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a metabolite produced by the biodegradation of EPS by insects such as Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a product of the mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms and their gut microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbon dioxide is a chemical compound that is produced during the combustion of the mealworm powder in the isotopic ratio mass spectrometer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb3edd44829125161ad624ea793ae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLONIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Colonization is the process by which bacteria, such as Rhodococcus ruber, establish themselves on a surface."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonization is the process by which microorganisms establish themselves on a surface, in this case, the surface of plastic beads."&lt;SEP&gt;"Colonization refers to the process by which microorganisms establish themselves on surfaces, and it is influenced by the ability of the microorganisms to produce enzymes that break down organic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-262bed73e929944e03b9f72769b8196c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aad5e97885ea1116956513db244b8fb6</data>
