      <data key="d0">"CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Circular bioeconomy is a concept that refers to the production and consumption of bioproducts in a way that reduces waste and promotes sustainability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a882603f777986db9d8fc65cea91dce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOSURFACTANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biosurfactant is a biochemical measure that enhances the rate of hydrocarbon degradation, and is produced by some of the identified bacterial species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biosurfactant is a biological marker that is produced by certain microorganisms and can be used to assess their ability to degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biosurfactant is a substance that enhances the biodegradation of hydrocarbons and other xenobiotics, including PS, by increasing their bioavailability."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a882603f777986db9d8fc65cea91dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8b07ee5dc7a7af59a93d03311efe60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROALGAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microalgae are a type of microorganism that have been studied for their potential to produce biopolymers, which could be used as a sustainable alternative to traditional plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microalgae are a type of microorganism used for bioenergy production, with potential applications in carbon capture."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microalgae are microorganisms used for bioenergy production with carbon capture via graphene oxide quantum dots."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8e18d03240e025c60621d616f1de85b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYANOBACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cyanobacteria are a type of microorganism that have been found to produce biopolymers, which could be used as a sustainable alternative to traditional plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cyanobacteria is a phylum of bacteria that is decreased in abundance in the gut of mealworms fed PS and CS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOPOLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biopolymers are a type of polymer that is produced by living organisms, such as microalgae and cyanobacteria, and could be used as a sustainable alternative to traditional plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85d18d5d86ed1c061dc44d69e9c09ffc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastics are a group of materials that are being studied in the research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are a type of material that has been shown to be biodegradable by Tenebrio molitor, with studies investigating the effects of polymer size on biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are a type of product that is degraded by mealworms, and its degradation is mediated by enzymes such as CES and GSTs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics, including HIPS, EPS, LDPE, LLDPE, and PP, are the materials being degraded by the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics, including PE, PP, PVC, PET, and PUR, are materials that can be biodegraded by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are the materials being analyzed, including polystyrene, polyurethane, and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are frequently ending up in landfills and oceans, causing environmental pollution, and conventional methods to tackle plastic pollution are not sufficient."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics, including polyethylene and polystyrene, are the subject of biodegradation in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are a type of material that is being studied for its biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic or semi-synthetic organic solids that can be molded or shaped."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are a type of material that is widely used and has become a major environmental concern due to its prevalence and impact on the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics, including PP, PU, and EVA, are the materials being consumed by the yellow mealworms, and their degradation is being studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are a type of product that can be broken down by microorganisms through biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastics are synthetic materials that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms and are a major contributor to environmental pollution."</data>
