    <node id="&quot;DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diet has been found to affect the composition of the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor, with some diets promoting the growth of microorganisms that are capable of degrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet is a nutrient source used to feed the larvae, consisting of polymers and wheat bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the food sources available to T. molitor larvae, including PS foam, bran, and soy protein."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the food and nutrients that an organism consumes, which can be affected by biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet is a factor that affects the composition of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the food consumed by an organism, in this case, mealworms, and can affect their development and ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet is the food that mealworms eat, and it can affect the bacterial community in their gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet is the food source that T. molitor larvae use to biodegrade PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet is a factor that affects the biodegradation of PE polymers by T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the food that the larvae were fed, and it had an effect on the gut microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet is a nutritional component that affects the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the different feeding conditions being tested, including control, Diet 1, Diet 2, and Diet 3, with varying ratios of bran to PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the food consumed by the insects, which can vary in composition, including the ratio of bran to PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diet refers to the food that an organism eats, and in the case of Tenebrio molitor, it can affect its development and ability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
