      <data key="d1">"HDPE is a type of plastic that is widely used and has a higher density than LDPE and MDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"HDPE is a type of plastic that mealworms can consume, with several marks and holes caused by the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-Density Polyethylene (HDPE) is a type of plastic that is commonly used in packaging and other applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microoccus luteus strain CGK112 can form biofilms and degrade HDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-density polyethylene (HDPE) is a type of plastic that has been found to be degraded by certain microorganisms, such as Micrococcus luteus."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-density polyethylene (HDPE) is a type of plastic mentioned as being biodegradable by the larvae of T. molitor and Z. atratus."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-Density Polyethylene is a type of plastic that mealworms can consume, with a relatively low compatibility as a feeding source."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-density polyethylene (HDPE) is a type of polyethylene that is consumed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-density polyethylene is one of the types of plastics used in the study, commonly found in commercial plastic bags."&lt;SEP&gt;"High-density polyethylene (HDPE) is a chemical compound that can be colonized and degraded by Aspergillus niger."</data>
