    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOW-DENSITY POLYETHYLENE (LDPE)&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b387da8298c55673284dca93ea82fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af801199dfd68205bddcbe0bcda26eef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d9491734042920c5911740665415835&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a882603f777986db9d8fc65cea91dce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d575c206eb616c4c970fd48fe3349247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb16cd27b6682965375050748ee77862</data>
      <data key="d1">Low-Density Polyethylene (LDPE) is a type of plastic that is widely used and has various applications, including packaging and the production of foam products. LDPE is commonly found in commercial plastic bags and is one of the major sources of plastic waste and microplastics. However, LDPE has been found to be biodegradable by certain microorganisms, such as Pseudomonas species, Aspergillus clavatus, Tenebrio obscurus, and Tenebrio molitor. Additionally, mealworms, including yellow mealworms, and the larvae of T. molitor and Z. atratus, can consume and biodegrade LDPE. The biodegradation of LDPE by these microorganisms and insects has been the subject of several studies, which have investigated the effects of LDPE on the metabolism and survival rate of mealworms. While LDPE has been found to have a relatively low compatibility as a feeding source for mealworms, it can still be degraded by these organisms, resulting in holes and scratches on the plastic surface. Overall, Low-Density Polyethylene (LDPE) is a type of plastic that is being studied for its biodegradation properties and its potential to be broken down by certain microorganisms and insects, which could help to reduce plastic waste and microplastics in the environment.</data>
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
    </node>
