    <node id="&quot;CITROBACTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of bacteria"&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a bacterium associated with PE and PP diets in superworms and mealworms, indicating its potential role in plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria that is associated with the degradation of polyethylene and polypropylene in superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria that is strongly associated with both PE and PS degradation in T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a type of bacteria found in the gut microbiome of the Tenebrio species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria that can cause infections in humans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been found to be present in the gut of mealworms and has nitrogen-fixing abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been found to have nitrogen-fixing abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter is a genus of bacteria that includes many nitrogen-fixing species."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec1a5b2913dd6782ff1e0533dd57325f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa10245aaff722ac7d69e73bed8afe74</data>
