    <node id="&quot;LARVAL GROWTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larval Growth is a biological process that is affected by polystyrene diet in yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval growth is a biological process affected by plastic ingestion in insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval growth is a biological process by which T. molitor larvae increase in size and develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval growth is the biological process by which the larvae develop and grow in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval growth is the process by which Tenebrio molitor larvae develop and increase in size, supported by nutrition from wheat bran and microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval growth refers to the process of yellow mealworms growing and developing."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval growth is the process by which Tenebrio molitor larvae develop and increase in size."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval growth refers to the process of development and increase in size of the yellow mealworms."</data>
