    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBIAL COMMUNITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbial communities are biological concepts investigated in the study to understand plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial communities refer to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of an organism, such as mealworms or Indianmeal moth larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial communities are microorganisms that live in the gut of insects such as Tenebrio molitor and play a significant role in the biodegradation of EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial communities refer to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of Tenebrio species and play a key role in the depolymerization of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial communities are diverse and play a crucial role in the biodegradation of PP by T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbial communities are composed of microorganisms that live in the gut and play a role in biodegradation."</data>
