    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupation is a biological process that is affected by the ingestion of microplastics in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a biological process that occurs in the life cycle of superworms and yellow mealworms, and can be affected by plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a stage in the life cycle of insects, where they transform into pupae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a life stage of mealworms that can be affected by the ingestion of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is the process by which mealworms form pupae, with its rate and timing being affected by different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a life stage of T. molitor larvae that is affected by their diet and nutritional status."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is the biological process by which Tenebrio molitor larvae transform into pupae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a biological process that occurs in the life cycle of superworms and yellow mealworms, and is used as an indicator of health and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a stage in the life cycle of larvae, which is affected by the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a type of life stage that is being referenced in the experiment, with mealworms undergoing pupation before emerging as adult beetles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a life stage of an insect, which was observed in A. diaperinus after feeding on polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a biological process where larvae transform into pupae, a non-feeding stage that precedes adulthood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a life stage of T. molitor that occurs after the larval stage and is influenced by the amount of reserves accumulated by the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation is a life stage of an organism, during which it undergoes transformation into a new form, such as from a larva to a pupa."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a1fbf409e74e27aa2b223e54f2e0def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a38c714e7f1f701ec1149e25910e16e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Development is a biological concept that refers to the process by which living organisms grow and mature, and is affected by endocrine-disrupting substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development is a biological concept that refers to the process of growth and maturation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development is a biological process that occurs in superworms and yellow mealworms, and can be affected by plastic consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development refers to the process of change from one stage to another in the life cycle of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development is a biological process that is affected by polystyrene diet in yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development refers to the process by which an organism, such as the T. molitor larvae, grows and matures from one life stage to another."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development is the process by which organisms grow and mature, influenced by gut bacteria in the case of the velvetbean caterpillar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development is a biological process that was studied in the mealworms, including their prepupal and pupation periods."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development is the process by which Tenebrio molitor mature and reach adulthood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development is a biological concept that refers to the process of growth and maturation in an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Development refers to the process of growth and differentiation of an organism, from one life stage to another."</data>
