      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larval guts are the location where polyethylene and polystyrene plastics undergo oxidation and depolymerization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DSC-TGA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DSC-TGA (Differential Scanning Calorimetry-Thermogravimetric Analysis) is a technique used to analyze the thermal stability of the plastics and their degradation products."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA is a biochemical measurement technique used to examine the thermal properties and decomposition rates of frass and original mask materials, providing evidence of biodegradation and new compound production."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA is a technique used to assess the thermal stability of materials, including plastics and frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA is a technique used to examine the thermal stabilities of foam plastic and frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"DSC-TGA is a technique used to analyze the thermal properties of the plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9a869d17d470cb9ca00328986147a3f</data>
    </node>
