    <node id="&quot;BRAN DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bran diet is a type of food that can be fed to mealworms, and can be supplemented with microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran diet is a type of diet that serves as a control for the experiment, used to compare the effects of plastic diets on superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A bran diet is used as a control diet for the mealworms, providing a natural source of nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran diet is a diet that affects the composition and function of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran diet is a nutrient used to feed mealworms, with its composition and effect on mealworm growth being important factors in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran diet is a type of diet that is used as a control in the experiment to compare with the polyurethane diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran diet is a type of diet that is used as a control in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bran diet is a type of diet that was used in the study to explore the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The bran diet is a type of diet that is used to feed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran diet is a type of diet that can be fed to Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae."</data>
