    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OTUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OTUs (Operational Taxonomic Units) are a way of categorizing microorganisms based on their genetic similarity, and are used to analyze the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs (Operational Taxonomic Units) refer to the individual units of microbial classification used in the analysis of gut microbial communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs refers to operational taxonomic units, used to assess the diversity of microorganisms in the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs, or operational taxonomic units, are a biological concept used to measure the diversity of the bacterial community in the gut of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs, or operational taxonomic units, refer to the distinct types of bacteria or fungi present in the gut communities of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs, or operational taxonomic units, are a way of categorizing and comparing different microorganisms based on their genetic characteristics."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs, or operational taxonomic units, are a way of categorizing microorganisms based on their genetic similarity."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs refer to the operational taxonomic units used to cluster the microorganisms present in the gut of the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs (Operational Taxonomic Units) is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms in the yellow mealworms' gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"OTUs are operational taxonomic units, used to study the diversity of microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHAO INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chao index is a measure of diversity, used to study the diversity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chao index is a biological concept used to measure the richness of the bacterial community in the gut of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Chao index is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms in the yellow mealworms' gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GPC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GPC analysis is a biochemical measure that is used to characterize the molecular weight distribution of plastic foams."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a biochemical measure used to determine the molecular weights and molecular weight distribution of the polystyrene microplastics (MPs)."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a technique used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers, such as polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis, or gel permeation chromatography, is a biochemical measure used to analyze the molecular weights of plastics such as PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis, or gel permeation chromatography, is a biological process used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis, or gel permeation chromatography, is a technology used to study the molecular weight of the PS residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a method used to analyze the molecular weight distribution of polymers, such as polyethylene terephthalate (PET)."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a biochemical measure used to analyze the composition and characteristics of frass produced by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a technique used to analyze the molecular weight of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a biochemical measure used to analyze the molecular weight of PS residuals after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a type of biochemical measure that is being used to analyze the degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a method used to characterize the depolymerization and biodegradation of ingested PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a biochemical measure used to characterize the polymer depolymerization during biodegradation of the ingested plastics by insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a tool used to analyze the size distribution of plastic particles."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a method used to analyze the molecular weight of plastics, and it is used to study the biodegradation of plastics by mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"GPC analysis is a method used to analyze the molecular weight of plastics, and it is used to study the biodegradation of plastics by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1f0f043d44950fae05e8207a298d4a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-490fdb90ad8a65d35f3c2cd42a8c4c8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0881f766e34a5d97ee711cd2edd793f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASCOMYCOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGI"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ascomycota is a class of fungi that includes Eurotiomycetes, Sordariomycetes, and other classes, which appeared to be overrepresented in PS samples compared to CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ascomycota is a phylum of fungi that is predominant in both PS and CT samples, but more abundant in CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ascomycota is a predominant phylum in bran-fed groups of both larvae species and PS-fed superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ascomycota is a type of fungi that showed a significant increase in the bran-fed group and is associated with plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ascomycota is one of the most representative fungal phyla involved in the degradation of various polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASIDIOMYCOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGI"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Basidiomycota is a class of fungi that is almost totally absent in CT samples, but present in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basidiomycota is a phylum of fungi encountered at a high frequency in PS samples, potentially involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basidiomycota is a phylum of fungi that is less abundant than Ascomycota, but still present in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basidiomycota is strongly associated with plastics diets in yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Basidiomycota is one of the most representative fungal phyla involved in the degradation of various polymers, and its relative abundance increases in all plastics-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93d5b1c190fdca6b5e456b1513515be4</data>
    </node>
