    <node id="&quot;GUT BACTERIAL COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut bacterial community refers to the collection of microorganisms present in the gut of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut bacterial community of T. molitor larvae is composed of various bacterial species that contribute to PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut bacterial community refers to the collection of bacteria that live in the gut of superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut bacterial community of Tenebrio molitor larvae is composed of various bacteria, including Spiroplasma, Acinetobacter, and Pseudomonas."</data>
