    <node id="&quot;PEDIOCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pediococcus is a genus of bacteria found in the gut of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediococcus is a genus of microorganisms that is associated with the PU diet and is a lactic acid bacterium that contributes to the health of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediococcus is a genus of bacteria that exhibits high abundance in the PS- and CS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediococcus is a type of lactic acid bacteria that may contribute to the health of the gut microbiome environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediococcus is a type of microorganism that is present in the gut microbiome of mealworms and may play a role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pediococcus is a type of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."</data>
