      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weissella is a genus of bacteria found in the gut of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella is a genus that is enriched in the CS-fed group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella is a genus of bacteria that was found to have a significant difference in relative abundance between the PE and bran diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella is a genus of bacteria that has been identified in the gut of mealworms and plays a role in the biodegradation of styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella is a genus of bacteria present in the gut of yellow mealworms, which disappeared in the PP-fed group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weissella is a genus that disappeared in the PP-fed group, although it was reported as a gut-associated bacterium in mealworms."</data>
