    <node id="&quot;PENICILLIUM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Penicillium is a fungus that has been reported to increase in abundance in PS-fed lesser mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penicillium is a genus of fungi that appeared to be overrepresented in PS samples compared to CT samples, with a Log2-fold change of 16.3."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penicillium is a genus of fungi that includes species capable of degrading plastics, such as polyethylene and polystyrene, which may indicate a potential role in plastic breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penicillium is a genus of fungi that is significantly over-represented in PS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Penicillium is a genus of fungi that has been found to be capable of biodegrading thermally treated low-density polyethylene."</data>
