    <node id="&quot;INSECT LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">Insect larvae are a life stage of insects, such as Tenebrio molitor, Galleria mellonella, and Zophobas atratus, that are capable of biodegrading plastics. They have been found to possess microorganisms in their gut that can degrade certain types of plastics, including polystyrene (PS). Insect larvae, including mealworms and superworms, can survive on a diet of plastics and contribute to their biodegradation. They are also capable of damaging and biodegrading certain plastics, and some species, such as the yellow mealworm larva, can achieve rapid biodegradation of plastics. Furthermore, insect larvae can secrete emulsifiers to mediate plastic biodegradation, potentially playing a significant role in the biodegradation of plastics. The gut microbiome of insect larvae has been studied to investigate the effects of plastic feedstocks on their growth and microbiome. Overall, insect larvae are organisms that have gut microbes with PS-degrading activity, and their ability to biodegrade plastics makes them a subject of interest in studies aimed at understanding the effects of microplastics on the environment and exploring their potential in plastic biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e3058d086d89f1ce9baa29cbc29bb48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b27c93b39534612a0492f52ce1f3cd8e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEEDSTOCKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feedstocks are the different diets being used to feed the larvae, including CB, PS, and CS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Feedstocks refer to the nutrients that are provided to the insect larvae in the study, including bran, PE, and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Feedstocks are the substances being consumed by the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b3e57543d6b365fff3ef2b14ddb309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">The MICROBIOME is a biological concept that refers to the community of microorganisms that live in and around an organism, including insects such as Tenebrio molitor larvae. This complex and diverse community of microorganisms plays a crucial role in the degradation of various substances, including polystyrene, polyethylene, and plastics. The MICROBIOME is involved in biodegradation and other biological processes, and its composition can be affected by factors such as diet. It is thought to play a role in the health and development of the organism it inhabits, and its study is important in understanding the complex relationships between microorganisms and their environments. The MICROBIOME is present in various environments, including the gut of insects, where it plays a crucial role in their physiology and development. In particular, the MICROBIOME of insects has been shown to be capable of metabolizing styrene and degrading plastics, such as PE mulching films and LDPE. The MICROBIOME is also involved in plastic degradation activity and is assessed in the context of Tenebrio molitor fed with polystyrene waste. The MICROBIOME can be analyzed using 16S rRNA gene sequencing, which helps to understand its composition and activity. Different diets can affect the composition and activity of the MICROBIOME, highlighting the importance of considering the specific environment and conditions in which the MICROBIOME is present. Overall, the MICROBIOME is essential for the proper functioning of ecosystems and has significant implications for our understanding of environmental processes.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33180d5b7e1ebfedf8de59ba1a2a2d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbb6f13dbe3de759712fa3a0c9780470&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-126ff1ea4b1c89f82a750386be59f926&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57e056cd3b06b37d22117fc75e3a4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e356bad5f8c2dd9188b38c0d9462b9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f45bee9c7111e3b95e966d23c3a6223d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3815960770483b9c0a1579ca8442e3a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755b