    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL COMMUNITIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial communities are groups of microorganisms that work together to break down complex materials, such as plastics, and are found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities are involved in dark fermentation of enzymatic hydrolysates and hydrogen production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities refer to the groups of microorganisms that live in the gut of an organism, such as Tenebrio molitor, and play a role in biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities refer to the groups of microorganisms that live in the gut of the larvae, and their composition and function were analyzed in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities refer to groups of microorganisms that work together to break down organic matter, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial communities are the communities of microorganisms present in the gut of yellow mealworms."</data>
