    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS ARATUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zophobas aratus is a genus of insects, specifically the superworm, that is capable of biodegrading polypropylene via gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas aratus is an insect species that can biodegrade foam plastics, with changes in gut digestive enzymes activities and microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas aratus, also known as the superworm, is an insect species that is capable of degrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas aratus, also known as superworms, are insects that can biodegrade polypropylene through a gut-microbe-dependent process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas aratus, also known as the superworm, is a microorganism capable of biodegrading low-density polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas aratus, also known as the superworm, is a species of insect that has been found to biodegrade plastics, including polystyrene and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas aratus, also known as the superworm, is an insect that can biodegrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3569d74f8a4c9d0851777a5a66284a00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f830cfd93570c7a9762518aa356ab69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ac276660dd76d0ef97a8a0b1a59664c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5073433ee060ce75e140a6626619108b</data>
