    <node id="&quot;XENOBIOTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Xenobiotics are a type of organic compound that is foreign to the environment and can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xenobiotics are foreign substances that are degraded by mealworms, and their degradation is mediated by enzymes such as CES and GSTs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xenobiotics are foreign substances that can be degraded by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xenobiotics are foreign substances that can be degraded by certain enzymes, including cytochrome P450."&lt;SEP&gt;"xenobiotics are foreign substances that are not naturally produced by an organism, and their degradation is an important process in the metabolism of plants and microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Xenobiotics are foreign substances that can be degraded by microorganisms."</data>
