    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular Weight is a physical property of the PS MPs that affects the SPCR of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight is a measure of the size of polymer chains, and it is used to study the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;Molecular Weight is a measure of the size of molecules, which can be affected by various factors such as depolymerization and biodegradation. It refers to the total mass of a molecule and is a physical property of substances, including polyethylene (PE), polystyrene (PS), and polypropylene (PP), that affects their thermal degradation and other characteristics. Molecular Weight is an important property in understanding the structure and behavior of materials, and it is used to study the chemical properties of plastics, including their degradation and biodegradation. In the context of biodegradation, Molecular Weight can decrease over time as a result of biodegradation, and decreases in Molecular Weight have been observed during the degradation of plastics, such as PE and PS, by microorganisms. However, the relationship between Molecular Weight and biodegradation is complex, as lower Molecular Weights can result in higher biodegradation rates, while higher Molecular Weights can make it more difficult for microorganisms to break them down. Molecular Weight is a key measure in understanding the size of molecules, which can affect their behavior and interactions, and is essential in understanding the biodegradation of plastics and their impact on the environment. It is used to analyze the properties of PE polymers and to track changes in the Molecular Weight of plastics during biodegradation. Additionally, Molecular Weight is used to fractionate the supernatant into different fractions and to compare the control PS and the fecula. Different types of Molecular Weight, including number-average Molecular Weight (Mn), weight-average Molecular Weight (Mw), and z-average Molecular Weight (Mz), can be analyzed to understand the properties of microplastics. Overall, Molecular Weight is a crucial property in understanding the biodegradation of plastics, and its characterization is important for understanding the size of molecules and their behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight is a physical property of PS polymers that can affect their biodegradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight is a physical property of polystyrene that affects its biodegradation in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight is a physical property of the PS polymers, which affects their biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2169963c4d6dae9b98da331d39eaa72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31ad3152e855d5b8085e1e61af57515d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54049db5a67a6464f459ccc427765140&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf662c8e784d14a3a4dba2e89041aa4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9bd8cf0d5102bbca724e0773be0eeae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f23046f647dab4d4caebd663db9aecde&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a228b2d8328bdce2419d34f8f59bc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89