    <node id="&quot;HIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HIPS is a type of plastic being degraded by the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS is a type of plastic that is amorphous and has a high cumulative consumption by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS is a type of plastic that is being used as a control in the biodegradability experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS is a type of plastic that is degraded by mealworms, and its degradation is mediated by enzymes such as CES and GSTs."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS, or high-impact polystyrene, is a type of plastic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS, or high-impact polystyrene, is a type of plastic that can be degraded by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"HIPS is a type of plastic that may be degraded by certain microorganisms, such as those in the Enterobacteriaceae family."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38f2f3673b813b3a817c014229c9565</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotics can suppress gut microbiota and inhibit polystyrene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;Antibiotics are substances that are used to treat bacterial infections by killing or inhibiting the growth of microorganisms. In the context of mealworms and other larvae, antibiotics are being used to treat these organisms and study their effect on the gut microbiome. Specifically, antibiotics can suppress the activity of microorganisms involved in plastic biodegradation, highlighting the importance of the gut microbiome in this process. By using antibiotics, researchers can eliminate the gut microbial microbiota of mealworms and other larvae, such as superworms, which impairs their capability to degrade plastics, including polystyrene (PS) and polyethylene terephthalate (PET). Antibiotics can also disrupt the symbiotic relationship between mealworms and nitrogen-fixing bacteria, thereby impairing the mealworm's ability to fix nitrogen from the atmosphere. Furthermore, antibiotics can have an adverse effect on the gut microbiota of mealworms and their ability to biodepolymerize plastic waste. The use of antibiotics in these studies allows researchers to investigate the role of gut microbes in plastic degradation and the impact of antibiotics on the behavior of larvae, such as the greater wax moth and mealworms. Various types of antibiotics, including aminoglycosides, macrolides, amphenicol, tetracycline, and β-lactam antibiotics, are used to suppress gut bacteria in the larvae. Overall, antibiotics play a crucial role in understanding the complex relationships between microorganisms, mealworms, and plastic degradation, and their use in these studies has significant implications for our understanding of the impact of antibiotics on ecosystems.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-497648a1cf8e41fac896250ae1eebbb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5</data>
    </node>
