    <node id="&quot;DEGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEGs refer to Differentially Expressed Genes, which are genes that have a significant change in expression level under different conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"DEGs, or differentially expressed genes, were used to identify potentially relevant metabolic pathways and functional enzymes involved in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ACHROIA GRISELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achroia grisella are insects that have the ability to digest and biodegrade plastic products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achroia grisella is a species of insect that has been found to biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achroia grisella is a type of insect that can efficiently biodegrade polyethylene waste."&lt;SEP&gt;Achroia Grisella, also known as the lesser waxworm or lesser waxmoth, is a species of moth whose larvae are capable of efficiently biodegrading high-density polyethylene (HDPE) waste and other plastics. This species of insect has been found to have the ability to break down and modify the backbone of various plastics, earning them the reputation of being "plastic-eating" worms. Achroia Grisella's capacity for plastic degradation is being studied, and they are often compared to other insects, such as Tenebrio molitor, in terms of biodegradation. The larvae of Achroia Grisella are particularly notable for their ability to degrade polyethylene (PE), and the species as a whole is being researched for its potential to biodegrade polyethylene waste. Overall, Achroia Grisella is a species of insect that has demonstrated a significant ability to biodegrade plastics, including polyethylene, and is an important area of study in the field of biodegradation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-323c02b97d9365a25761a155d358b17a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b08485bef3ee3db21e59e159ad4c3e20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566d464a7713ef7ca266f3d5f24a1a59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77</data>
