    <node id="&quot;KEGG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KEGG is a database being used to annotate the genes with KEGG pathways."&lt;SEP&gt;"KEGG stands for Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes, which is a database that provides information on gene functions and their interactions."&lt;SEP&gt;"KEGG, or Kyoto Encyclopedia of Genes and Genomes, is a database of biological pathways and genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"KEGG is a database of genes and genomes that is used to identify the pathways involved in the degradation of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"KEGG is a database that provides information on metabolic pathways, including those involved in the biodegradation of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"KEGG is a database used for functional annotation of unigenes and metabolites."</data>
