      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BLASTX is a bioinformatics tool used to compare a query sequence to a database of known sequences to identify similarities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GO stands for Gene Ontology, which is a framework for annotating genes and their products with terms that describe their functions and locations."&lt;SEP&gt;"GO, or gene ontology, refers to the functional annotation of genes and their products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f545e57b1a2b3da8601b4d23e1260c94</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RT-PCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"RT-PCR is a biological concept used to analyze the expression levels of enzymes involved in the degradation of PS and lignin."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR is a biological process used to validate the expression of genes."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR is a laboratory technique used to validate the expression levels of related PS- and CS-degrading enzymes in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR stands for Real-Time Polymerase Chain Reaction, which is a laboratory technique used to detect and quantify specific DNA sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR, or real-time polymerase chain reaction, is a technique used to amplify and quantify DNA sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR is a laboratory technique used to analyze the expression of nifH genes in the gut microbiota of Styrofoam-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"RT-PCR, or reverse transcription polymerase chain reaction, is a laboratory technique used to amplify specific RNA sequences."</data>
