    <node id="&quot;ANOVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"STATISTICAL METHOD"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ANOVA is a biological process used for statistical analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical concept used to evaluate the differences in the data."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical method used to analyze data."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA stands for Analysis of Variance, which is a statistical technique used to compare means among groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA, or analysis of variance, is a statistical technique used to analyze data."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA, or analysis of variance, is a statistical method used to compare the means of different groups in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is the statistical method used to analyze the data."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical technique used to compare means of different groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical method used for analyzing variance."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA, or analysis of variance, is a statistical method used to compare means among groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anova is a statistical process used to compare the mean values of the growth and development parameters of the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA, or analysis of variance, is a statistical process being used to analyze the data."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA is a statistical method being used to analyze the differences in PE consumption and changes in molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"ANOVA, or analysis of variance, is a statistical method used to assess the significant differences in the extraction rates, plastic removal, and Mw, Mp, and Ms values."</data>
