    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLY(ETHYLENE TEREPHTHALATE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Poly(Ethylene Terephthalate) (PET) is a type of plastic that can be degraded by certain bacteria and enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(ethylene terephthalate) is a type of plastic that is degraded by Ideonella sakaiensis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(Ethylene Terephthalate) is a type of plastic that can be degraded and assimilated by a bacterium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(ethylene terephthalate) is a type of plastic that can be degraded and assimilated by a certain bacterium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(ethylene terephthalate) is a chemical property that can be degraded and assimilated by microorganisms, such as Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(ethylene terephthalate) is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Poly(ethylene terephthalate) is a type of plastic mentioned as one of the six major polymers."</data>
