    <node id="&quot;FATTY ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty acids are a type of nutrient analyzed in the study, with their levels being used as a source of energy during starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;Fatty acids are a type of complex organic molecule and biomolecule that play a crucial role in various biological processes. They are a source of energy for mealworms, particularly during starvation, and are also involved in the metabolism of plants and microorganisms. Fatty acids are metabolites produced during biodegradation and are involved in the degradation of polystyrene. They are nutrients that can be converted to α,ω-dicarboxylic acids by certain microorganisms and are important for mealworm growth and development. Fatty acids are also a type of bioactive compound generated during the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor larvae. They are components of the lipids extracted from mealworms and can be analyzed by gas chromatography. The profiles of fatty acids in mealworms can vary depending on their diet, and they are also found in the feeds used in experiments, such as wheat bran and dried whey. Fatty acids are a type of nutrient that is being studied for its effects on the gut microbiome and are important for human health. They are involved in energy metabolism in insects and can be produced through the metabolism of polystyrene. Additionally, fatty acids, including monounsaturated fatty acids (MUFAs) and saturated fatty acids (SFAs), are metabolites that indicate the presence of bacteria capable of decomposing urea and contribute to the degradation of polystyrene. Overall, fatty acids are a vital nutrient that plays a significant role in the biology of mealworms and other organisms, and their profiles can be adjusted by changing the feed.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33180d5b7e1ebfedf8de59ba1a2a2d04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eed90a978852274ead3771418cd60bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df24ea37743c236d369911024fc20bfc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4712059883b356b4aea23cb7ef1514&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9d01d291012bd548fc067e250ec39fba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0e30f29e9016acae216566f53e60cea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f141d484320c21ec01b892a9b7d56486&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ddf4b13293dd3d8d0887af10fc52c98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-728d6b0b96814c5c3c7b93042e9b9856&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38f2f3673b813b3a817c014229c9565</data>
