    <node id="&quot;FATTY ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fatty acid biosynthesis gene modules are enriched in the gut microbiome of yellow mealworms fed with PVC, suggesting an increase in energy metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acid is a metabolite that may be produced during PET biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acid is a type of molecule that undergoes degradation in mealworms, with different types of fatty acids being produced or degraded in the presence of different substrates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acid is a type of biomolecule that is oxidized to provide energy during starvation in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acid refers to a type of molecule that is involved in energy storage and other biological processes, which can be affected by biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are a type of metabolite that can be produced during the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acid is a type of nutrient found in the insects, with varying composition depending on the diet, with oleic acid being the most abundant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acid is a type of metabolite that is involved in the degradation of PET and is an important component of the cell membrane structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acids are a type of lipid that is found in the biomass of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acid is a type of metabolite found in bacteria, with different species having distinct fatty acid profiles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fatty acid is a component of fat that is being analyzed in the experiment using gas chromatography with flame ionization detector."</data>
