    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEESWAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beeswax is a mixture of several chemical compounds consisting mainly of esters of various long-chain alcohols and fatty acids, used by honey bees to raise their larvae and store honey and pollen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a nutrient that affects the expression of genes related to carboxylesterase and lipase in G. mellonella larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a nutrient that is used to feed G. mellonella larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a type of natural product that can be metabolized by the hologenome of Galleria Mellonella, indicating its potential for biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a type of lipid that can be biodegraded by certain insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a type of lipid produced by honeybees."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a type of food used to feed G. mellonella larvae before the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a type of long-chain hydrocarbon that can be metabolized by the hologenome of Galleria mellonella."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a type of nutrient that is being used as a control feed for the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beeswax is a type of lipid that can be metabolized by certain microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipase is an enzyme encoded by the PueA gene, which plays a role in the degradation of polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme involved in polyurethane degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme produced by Rhizopus delemar that can degrade polyesters."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that is overexpressed in G. mellonella larvae fed on beeswax, and is involved in the degradation of lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that hydrolyzes p-nitrophenyl laurate, and its activity is determined spectrophotometrically."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that is capable of breaking down lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme involved in lignin and plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme involved in the degradation of lipids and other fatty acid-containing compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme involved in the hydrolysis of products to generate long-chain fatty acids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme produced by Candida antarctica that acts synergistically with cutinase from Humicola insolens for PET hydrolysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that is involved in the breakdown of lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that is involved in the hydrolysis of lipids, and is upregulated in T. molitor larvae during PET biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that breaks down lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that has been found to be involved in the degradation of various organic compounds, including polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipase is an enzyme that is active in the digestive tract, indicating its role in the breakdown of lipids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2741fab96df80d452d2d4cc651730521&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf1f7b81bc271c665d7776cc3114a92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b1c9087e78bc6ba94c2b63fd88d2ca66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67425e341a5b2c8102281581fa148554&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f2fd4b2e978e6745e0dde602114a826</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;G. MELLONELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"G. mellonella (Galleria mellonella) is a type of insect that can biodegrade plastics, including PE, and is used in research studies."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a genus of insect that is capable of degrading plastics, and its larvae are used to study the effects of beeswax on gene expression."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is an insect whose gut environment is capable of degrading plastic, with the insect host and its gut microbiome collaborating to break down the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a genus of microorganisms that can biodegrade plastics, with a different biodegradation process compared to T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a genus of insects, specifically superworms, that are used in the study to analyze their gut microbial community and ability to consume Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a species of larvae used in the experiment, fed with beeswax and later with Styrofoam blocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a microorganism mentioned in the study as a wax moth."&lt;SEP&gt;"G. mellonella is a type of microorganism that is capable of biodegrading LDPE, as mentioned in the text."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NAT is an enzyme that is involved in the acetylation of isoniazid, and is mediated by the gene n-acetyltransferase."&lt;SEP&gt;"NAT, or n-acetyltransferase, is an enzyme that catalyzes the transfer of acetyl groups to substrates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CES is an enzyme that is involved in the hydrolysis of isoniazid, and is mediated by the gene carboxylesterase."&lt;SEP&gt;"CES, or carboxylesterase, is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of ester bonds."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GSTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GSTs are a family of enzymes that are involved in the detoxification of xenobiotics, and are upregulated in mealworms fed on plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"GSTs, or glutathione S-transferases, are enzymes that catalyze the conjugation of glutathione with electrophilic substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPASE 1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipase 1 is an enzyme that is overexpressed in G. mellonella larvae fed on beeswax, and is involved in the degradation of lipids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIPASE 3&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
