      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrocarbons are a class of chemical compounds that are being degraded by the identified bacterial species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons are a type of chemical compound that is found in beeswax, and is involved in the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons are compounds that are formed during the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons are a type of chemical compound that can be degraded by certain bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons is a chemical property that is observed in the FTIR analysis of polyethylene (PE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydrocarbons are a type of chemical compound that is present in polypropylene."</data>
