    <node id="&quot;HOLOGENOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hologenome refers to the collective genome of a host organism and its associated microorganisms, and is an important concept in understanding the complex interactions between hosts and their microbiomes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hologenome refers to the collective genome of an organism and its associated microorganisms, which can influence the organism's metabolism and biodegradation capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The hologenome refers to the combined genome of an organism and its associated microorganisms, such as the gut microbiome of Galleria mellonella."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hologenome refers to the collective genome of an organism and its associated microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
