      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORTHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Orthology refers to the study of the evolutionary relationships between genes in different organisms, and is an important concept in understanding gene function and evolution."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47ee82f655853704e6653d8146973278</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zophobas atratus larvae are a type of insect that has been found to be capable of breaking down plastic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae, also known as superworms, are capable of biodegrading certain types of plastics, including polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae, also known as superworms, have been reported to eat plastics, including polyethylene and polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae are insects that have the ability to digest and biodegrade plastic products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae are a type of insect that may be affected by microplastic biodegradation, similar to Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas atratus larvae have been found to biodegrade polystyrene and low-density polyethylene, producing microplastics and altering their gut microbiota."</data>
