      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saline solution is a chemical used to extract and preserve the gut bacteria from the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline solution is a substance used for removing alcohol and killing mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline solution is a substance used to suspend the gut cells of the worms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline solution is a mixture of NaCl and distilled water, used in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline solution is used for the extraction of gut tissue from Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline solution is prepared by mixing 0.85% (w/v) sodium chloride and distilled water."</data>
