    <node id="&quot;PCR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) is a biological process used to amplify DNA sequences, which helped in identifying the species of the lesser waxworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction) is a laboratory technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences, including the 16S ribosomal RNA gene and the alkB gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is a process that was used to amplify the alkB gene in Klebsiella oxytoca strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR, or polymerase chain reaction, is a molecular biology technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences, such as the 16S ribosomal RNA gene in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is a process used to amplify the DNA content."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is a biological process used to amplify DNA sequences in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR, or polymerase chain reaction, is a laboratory technique used to amplify DNA sequences."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR, or polymerase chain reaction, is a laboratory technique used to amplify the DNA of the polystyrene-degrading bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR stands for polymerase chain reaction, a biological process used to amplify the V3 region of bacterial 16S rRNA gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is a technique used to amplify the DNA of the microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR is a technique used to amplify the genetic material of the microorganisms in the gut core microbiome of the yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCR, or polymerase chain reaction, is a laboratory technique used to amplify specific DNA sequences."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-568e2e90ce0d3bbb4e21079f4252f5de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-36b964b1825429cad2c7d13c1ea8827e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b74e88d1f94354055e078b38af6a180&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c341ee1e0a5f54e33ca3379aa9d01c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33649582d350bc1da7dbca1a65092127&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83f95e0134b38f78f2624da01ab0f79&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5eb6a8326b4977801e2f7694a2c750&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aface14c9ee7dd5ccd25e7094ed5c1c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE EMULSION&quot;">
