      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phylogenetic Analysis is a process used to infer the evolutionary relationship between different species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is a biological process used to study the evolutionary relationships among different bacteria, including Klebsiella oxytoca."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to study the evolutionary relationships among organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is the process of studying the evolutionary relationships between different organisms, including the bacterial strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is a method used to study the evolutionary relationships between organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is the study of the evolutionary relationships between different organisms, which can be used to identify and classify microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Phylogenetic analysis is used to evaluate the relationships among bacterial cells."</data>
