      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"16S ribosomal RNA is a biological concept that refers to a specific region of the ribosomal RNA molecule used to identify and classify microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The 16S ribosomal RNA gene is a gene used for molecular identification of bacteria, including Klebsiella oxytoca."&lt;SEP&gt;"16S ribosomal RNA is a genetic concept that refers to a type of RNA used to identify and classify microorganisms, including the gut bacteria of T. molitor larvae and adults."</data>
