    <node id="&quot;ALKB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"AlkB is a gene in Pseudomonas, identified as the key enzyme in alkane biodegradation during polyethylene breakdown."&lt;SEP&gt;"AlkB is a gene responsible for the degradation of polystyrene and is found in Klebsiella oxytoca strains."&lt;SEP&gt;"AlkB is a gene that was amplified by PCR in Klebsiella oxytoca strains, and its sequence was analyzed to confirm its identity."&lt;SEP&gt;"AlkB is a gene that is cloned into a recombinant cell to enhance polyethylene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"AlkB is a type of hydroxylating enzyme that is involved in the biodegradation of HDPE, performing initial hydroxylation at the PE terminal ω-carbon."&lt;SEP&gt;"AlkB is an enzyme that has been found to be involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene."</data>
