    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROORGANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microorganisms are the microorganisms that live in the gut of mealworms and play a role in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a role in the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by plastic-eating mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms, including those found in mealworms, play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polymeric materials."&lt;SEP&gt;Gut Microorganisms are microorganisms that live in the gut of various organisms, including insects such as Tenebrio molitor, mealworms, and other invertebrates. They play a crucial role in various biological processes, including the digestion process, and are capable of biodegrading certain materials, including polyethylene and polystyrene. Gut Microorganisms found in the digestive system of animals, such as Tenebrio molitor larvae and mealworms, aid in the degradation of plastics and play a crucial role in the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene. They have efficient biodegradation ability and can break down plastic waste, particularly polystyrene. Gut Microorganisms are essential for the biodegradation of plastics by insects and other organisms, and their role in the digestive system of animals is vital for the degradation of various materials. Specifically, they play a crucial role in the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene by mealworms, as indicated in research, and are also involved in the biodegradation of low-density polyethylene (LDPE) in the larvae of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus. Overall, Gut Microorganisms are vital for the degradation of plastics, particularly polystyrene, and their role in the digestive system of insects and other organisms is crucial for the biodegradation of plastic waste.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627e3f1b0fb440795f73c4fa33093c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1dd9a0647afad70038c8052c24eb5a67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39598f698094d1663ca3438bc143bc90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8cede90fd3b3eee0bd12d582eaa7d54c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c7bcc9530f9dc72038f774f6f084ab6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38a07d29ecfa06f82d97e69f5cd2c801&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db0003a7244c51697d0129eb84b8e28e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cdc0cc71ed5e76f044e4db50f81ad2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc31a0931fceb1446bc6ec4d0c587f7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56604c68c2f6221f63a4afa5d457e8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-412d934721b214c2cd0565531172171c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20a69982e6abe36c2a0d4a70b78720ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eada60ee606520104bb515c4896d6b0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908b8bfa7e446694958cf9bd0cfbc583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b8cc3aa81b03290b589ccf0a1548ca0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3</data>
