    <node id="&quot;RHODOCOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rhodococcus is a bacterium that has been reported to have styrene-degrading abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria that can metabolize styrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria that contains multiple alkB homologous genes with varying substrate ranges and induction styles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria that includes species capable of producing biofilms and degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria that is involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria that has been found to biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria that is known for its ability to degrade various organic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus that exhibits higher abundances in both PS- and CS-fed groups than in CB-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of microorganisms that includes species capable of biodegrading polystyrene and other plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria that was found to have a significant difference in relative abundance between the bran and PE diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus is a genus of bacteria that has been found to degrade polypropylene."</data>
