    <node id="&quot;AMINO ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amino acids are a group of nutrients that are essential for the growth and development of the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are a type of compound found in the bodies of mealworms, which can be synthesized by microorganisms in the microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are essential nutrients that are found in Tenebrio molitor L., making it a good source of nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids, such as threonine, valine, histidine, and lysine, are essential nutrients found in Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are a type of nutrient that is synthesized by microorganisms and is important for the growth and development of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are the building blocks of proteins and are produced by the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae through nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are nutrients that may be produced by fungi in the gut of A. diaperinus, which may be related to their ability to degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids refer to a type of biomolecule that is observed in the 1H NMR spectra of degraded PP polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Amino acids are a type of metabolite that is formed during the biodegradation of LDPE, as shown by the ¹H NMR spectra."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd90c8f9754a78aabdbd7053e1adf90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-302543e7a2fdb3596cc8a10e7072ec01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81a3bc3c202af119c80775d5bf23d8b2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32f340b7166025be3c56178a94ae480d</data>
    </node>
