    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL POLLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental pollution is a concept that refers to the contamination of the environment by pollutants, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is a concept that refers to the harm caused by human activities to the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is a major problem that can be addressed through the use of edible insects as a sustainable food source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the harm caused to the environment by the accumulation of polystyrene (PS) and other plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is the contamination of the environment by human activities, including plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is a consequence of plastics ending up in landfills and oceans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is an ecological concept that is being studied as a major problem caused by plastic production and usage."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by plastic materials, including polystyrene, and its impact on ecosystems and human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is the contamination of the environment by pollutants, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is the contamination of the environment by pollutants, such as plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is a major problem caused by the accumulation of polystyrene waste, and can be mitigated by biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by plastic waste, affecting the health and survival of wildlife and humans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by human activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by harmful substances, such as plastics, which can have negative impacts on ecosystems and human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment with harmful substances, including microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by pollutants, such as microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is a major concern that is related to the biodegradation of plastics and other materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is a major concern related to the production and disposal of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is an ecological concept that is being studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is the contamination of the environment by pollutants, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental pollution is the contamination of the environment by human activities, including the generation of plastic waste."</data>
