    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMEOSTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Homeostasis is a biological concept that is provided by the host to microorganisms that coexist within it."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeostasis is a biological concept that refers to the ability of the body to maintain a stable internal environment, and is affected by endocrine-disrupting substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeostasis is a biological concept that refers to the maintenance of a stable internal environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeostasis is a biological process that is affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Homeostasis is a biological process that is affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) in mealworms, as indicated by changes in metabolites involved in biochemical processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7734a37a076c4f934de059042daf10cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproduction is a biological concept that refers to the process by which living organisms produce offspring, and is affected by endocrine-disrupting substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reproduction is a biological concept that refers to the process of producing offspring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reproduction is a biological process that occurs in organisms as they produce offspring."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reproduction is the process by which T. molitor produces offspring, which is influenced by the energy density threshold and the reproduction buffer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7e755eeac14110dcfdcfc32e51f30b89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2934b88523093a8bba74cc29a0c775e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
