      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T-Bili is a biochemical measure that is below the measurement range in some groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-Bili is a measure of total bilirubin in the serum biochemical analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-Bili, or total bilirubin, is a measure of the amount of bilirubin in the blood, with a measured value of LOD."&lt;SEP&gt;"T-Bili, or total bilirubin, is a metabolite that is used as a marker of liver function."</data>
