      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glucose is a measure of blood sugar levels in the serum biochemical analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a type of sugar that serves as a primary source of energy for the body, with a measured value of 224.80±7.17 mg/dL."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a nutrient used as a control to test the effect of supernatant on respiration."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a type of sugar used as a control in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a type of carbohydrate that is present in the hemolymph and plays a crucial role in maintaining organ function, particularly the nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a type of sugar that can be fermented by certain bacteria, including some species of Bacillus and Stenotrophomonas."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a metabolite that is associated with the degradation of polystyrene, with its presence indicating the potential for metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glucose is a nutrient that is utilized by Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its ability to grow on this carbon source."</data>
