    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL MICROBIOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal microbiota are microorganisms that are being studied for their changes in response to expanded polystyrene ingestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms living in the intestine of mealworms, contributing to the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms living in the digestive tract of the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiota refers to the microorganisms present in the gut of mealworms, which play a significant role in EPS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live within the digestive tract of organisms, such as Tenebrio molitor."</data>
