    <node id="&quot;HISTOLOGICAL FINDINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Histological findings refer to the results of studies on the microscopic structure of tissues and organs, and can provide insights into the effects of different factors on health and disease."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Toxicity is a biological concept related to the adverse effects of certain substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity is a biological response to exposure to microplastics, which can cause harm to organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity is a concern when considering the use of insects that degrade Styrofoam as a food source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects of a substance on an organism, and can be influenced by factors such as dose and duration of exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects of plastic on the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the ability of a substance to cause harm or damage to living organisms, such as the T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects of microplastics on the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects of certain substances, such as EVA, on the yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects of a substance, such as microplastics, on living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the potential harm caused by a substance to living organisms, including humans and the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity is a concept used in the study to describe the negative effects of certain substances on the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity is a physiological response that occurs in organisms when they are exposed to toxic substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Toxicity refers to the harmful effects of polystyrene on T. molitor larvae, which can be quantified using the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6cc0afd02f25b584d6e3a755fc7272b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ce7cf71b094ef4329d3da3b628438bec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a097963ab8ec0ad6b1d51685fc359027&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a31a12c930b59b872c94dda484d0db4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-383865d9c2a2b8a7cabd754f1193b8f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENOTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Genotoxicity refers to the ability of a substance to damage DNA and cause genetic mutations, and can be influenced by factors such as dose and duration of exposure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genotoxicity refers to the ability of a substance to damage genetic material, which can lead to harmful health effects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Genotoxicity refers to the harm caused to an organism's genetic material by microplastics and other pollutants."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a53d37e7ff6850fc55177f325e49861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef</data>
    </node>
