    <node id="&quot;ZOPHOBAS MORIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zophobas morio is a synonym for Zophobas atratus, a species of darkling beetle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is a type of insect that can feed on and degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas morio is a species of beetle that has been extensively studied for its unique characteristics and potential applications. It is known to be a species of insect that can degrade polystyrene, as well as other plastic packaging materials, including polyurethane (PU) and expanded polystyrene (EPS). The bacterium P. aeruginosa was isolated from Zophobas morio, highlighting its potential as a source of beneficial microorganisms. Additionally, Zophobas morio, also known as superworms, have been found to have antioxidant properties and have been studied for their nutritional value as a food source. Research has shown that feeding Zophobas morio with Styrofoam can affect their nutritional composition, making them a potential candidate for sustainable bioremediation and waste management. The larvae of Zophobas morio have been observed consuming plastics, and the species has been found to biodegrade plastics at a higher rate than some other insects, such as mealworms. Zophobas morio is related to Tenebrio and has been observed to penetrate packaging materials, making it a valuable species for further research. Overall, Zophobas morio is a species of insect with significant potential for applications in biodegradation, sustainable bioremediation, and as a food source, with ongoing research exploring its capabilities and properties.&lt;SEP&gt;"Zophobas morio is the species to which superworms belong."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4fc215d3abb38f76b4ee0d22c4f1eb11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db672d5836dfe372ee7c47ee4dd6fbd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d5261cecf34dd62f3f6ee6f6c3e7834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba22196a59b67cbf67af7d76a039af1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-97444337eddb4e9e3d88bde93ce02aef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6264a99190316d0aeed63b5d6485999e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4b03ca32b0efbf0ca6a3c8761c0d03d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-119b3f144b4ec234392cca17031bd7a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32e10966ec80ea585746639b6be7e04e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d7ae4d155085781614411da5564816&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXIGUOBACTERIUM SP. STRAIN YT2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the guts of mealworms, capable of forming biofilm on PS film and degrading PS pieces."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a PS-degrading bacterial strain isolated from the guts of mealworms, capable of removing PS by 7.4% in a 60-day period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain that can degrade PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain that can degrade polystyrene, removing 7.4% of its mass over a 60-day period."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a strain of bacteria that can degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a type of bacteria that lives in the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor and enables them to break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterium that can degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain that has been isolated from the intestine of the mealworm and has been found to have PS-degrading activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a plastic-degrading bacterium isolated from the mealworm's gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a type of bacteria that lives in the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor and helps to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2 is a bacterial strain that can degrade polystyrene and form a biofilm on its surface."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df4c8c66bfbbfc37ed842f53d2b8796c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e67971bdf45c447f2409fddb80e0d8a</data>
    </node>
