    <node id="&quot;CYTOTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cytotoxicity is a biological response measured in the in vitro assays to assess the toxicity of the insect homogenates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytotoxicity refers to the ability of a substance to be toxic to cells, and is an important consideration in the development of insect-based food products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytotoxicity refers to the ability of a substance to be toxic to cells, studied in the context of insect extracts and their potential applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytotoxicity refers to the ability of a substance to be toxic to cells, which is being studied in the context of mealworm and superworm extracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytotoxicity refers to the ability of a substance to be toxic to cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytotoxicity is a physiological response that can occur in organisms as a result of exposure to microplastics and nanoparticles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cytotoxicity is a type of toxin that is being measured in the edible insects."</data>
