    <node id="&quot;SUSTAINABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sustainability is a concept that involves the use of resources in a way that minimizes harm to the environment and human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sustainability is a concept that is being studied in the research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sustainability is an ecological concept that estimates the sustainability of the biodiesel production process, with its environmental impact and economic viability being evaluated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sustainability refers to the ability to maintain or support a process or system over time, with implications for the potential of insect-based food products to promote sustainable food systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sustainability is the concept of reducing plastic waste through biodegradation by Tenebrio molitor and Exiguobacterium sp. strain YT2."</data>
