    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER ASBURIAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter asburiae is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae is a bacterial strain that can degrade LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae is a bacterium capable of degrading polyethylene, and was isolated from the gut microbiome of plastic-eating waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae is a type of bacteria that can be found in the gut microbiota of certain insects, including mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae is a type of bacterium that can biodegrade plastics, including PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter asburiae is a bacterium that can enhance resistance to Aeromonas veronii infection in common carp."</data>
