    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of bacteria that includes strain PELW2042, which has the ability to biodegrade HDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a bacterial strain capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a bacterial strain that can degrade LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that has been found to be present in the gut of insects that break down plastic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that includes strain NyZ451, which is capable of degrading PE mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a genus of microorganisms that includes Bacillus sp. PELW2042."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of microorganism that is capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a species of bacteria that is capable of degrading PS, and was found to form tunnels, cracks, and cellular aggregates on PS sheets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a genus of bacteria that may be involved in PP degradation in the gut of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a genus of microorganisms that is involved in the degradation of lignocellulose and PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that is associated with the degradation of low molecular weight polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacterium that can biodegrade plastics, including PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a bacterium that has been investigated for its role in degrading polystyrene, highlighting its potential in environmental cleanup efforts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that has been found to biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a genus of bacteria that includes species capable of biodegrading polyethylene mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that has been found to be capable of degrading polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that is capable of degrading polypropylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that can biodegrade polypropylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that can biodegrade polyethylene mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacillus sp. is a type of bacteria that has been reported to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b77d05458a2050e3057c427cf81e24ef&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a8c5ce99d234a2ac272a8b4b8135e53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49ebafd73759fc2bf3d4a642ccad96e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecf2c478d08c7bc8e491f630aa289881&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02761f0aee6116a25ce05444f6ce8242&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf</data>
