      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moisture Content is a physical characteristic used to measure the moisture content of the insects and frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture content is a measure of the amount of water in the yellow mealworm samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture content is a parameter monitored in the experimental setup, affecting the growth and activity of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture content is a physical characteristic of the insects, determined using a moisture analyzer, which is crucial for calculating the nutrient composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moisture content is an influencing factor in the biodepolymerization of plastic waste and polystyrene."</data>
