    <node id="&quot;LIPIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of biomolecule that may play a role in the degradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a component of mealworms used to produce biodiesel, with their content and conversion being important factors in the production process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a nutrient that can be converted to biodiesel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a type of biomolecule that can be extracted from larvae and used to produce biodiesel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a type of biomolecule that can be found in mealworms and superworms, and their content can be affected by consuming polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a type of metabolite that is produced during the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a type of biomolecule that can be produced by mealworms as a result of degrading polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a type of nutrient that is being analyzed in the mealworms, with decreased levels found in groups fed with polystyrene compared to the control group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a type of biomolecule that are produced by mealworms during the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS), and they are an important source of energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are metabolites extracted from the mealworms, and their composition and structure are important for understanding the degradation process of Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a type of biomolecule that is affected by the type of polystyrene mealworms consume, with decreased levels indicating potential starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipids are a type of nutrient being measured in the bodies of mealworms fed different materials."</data>
