    <node id="&quot;FECULA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fecula is a metabolite produced by mealworms after they ingest Styrofoam, indicating the degradation of Styrofoam by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is a metabolite produced by the mealworms during the decomposition of Styrofoam, with its carbon content being measured over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is a metabolite that can be produced by mealworms as a result of consuming polystyrene, and it can be used as an indicator of energy production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is the metabolite produced by the mealworms as they degrade the Styrofoam, and its composition and structure are important for understanding the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is the residual material that is egested by the mealworms after they have degraded the Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula refers to the residues of polystyrene (PS) that have been egested through the gut of mealworms, containing new components produced during digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is a metabolite produced by the biodegradation of EPS by insects such as Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is a metabolite that is produced by mealworms during the degradation of EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fecula is a substance produced by mealworms that is used to analyze the degradation of Styrofoam."</data>
