      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Z. morio is a species of insect that is being studied for its ability to digest and degrade Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Z. morio is a species of superworm that is being compared to mealworms in terms of their ability to consume polystyrene and their potential effects on cell cytotoxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Z. morio is a type of insect that has been studied for its potential cytotoxic properties and its ability to be fed a diet of polystyrene foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Z. morio is an insect that can digest polystyrene, and its intestinal microbiota contains bacteria that can decompose polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Z. morio is an insect that has microorganisms in its digestive tract that can degrade polystyrene."</data>
