      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alphitobius diaperinus is a microbe that has been studied for its growth and metabolic rate in relation to temperature."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is a species of beetle that has been studied for its nutritional value as a food source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is a species of beetle that has been studied in the context of biodegradation and metabolic responses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is an insect species whose gut microbiota was studied in relation to poly styrene feeding."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is a species of mealworm that is used as a source of nutrient composition and is also capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is a species of beetle, specifically a tenebrioid beetle, that is being studied for its potential to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is a species of insect that is capable of feeding on and degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is a species of insect, specifically a lesser mealworm, that is used in the experiment to study the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alphitobius diaperinus is an insect species that has been found to be capable of feeding on and degrading polystyrene."</data>
