      <data key="d1">"Larval stage is a life stage of T. molitor, characterized by growth and development before pupation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval stage is a life stage of mealworms that is affected by the ingestion of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval stage refers to the different developmental stages of the mealworms, including young larval stage (YLS), middle larval stage (MLS), and old larval stage (OLS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval stage of mealworms is the stage at which they are capable of biodepolymerizing plastic waste and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval stage of Tenebrio molitor is a critical period of growth and development, influenced by the type of feed provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval stage is the stage of development of the mealworms that is capable of breaking down EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval stage is a developmental stage of the lesser waxworm where it prefers to eat."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval stage is one of the life stages of the yellow mealworm, during which it is capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval stage is the immature stage of insects, including mealworms, that is being studied for its ability to consume and break down PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196a7570e6cac531e94c1680c54f5491&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f21478b87845df31740b3dab37d197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KUMHO TIRE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kumho Tire is a company that provided the micro-PS (MPS) material used in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BOB'S RED MILL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bob's Red Mill is a company that provided the wheat bran used as a food source for the mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COTED DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coted diet is a type of diet where the micro-PS (MPS) is coated with bran, used in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUBBER SUCTION BULB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOOL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rubber suction bulb is a tool used to remove the frass from the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MESH SIEVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOOL"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mesh sieve is a tool used to separate the micro-PS (MPS) from the frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YOUNG LARVAL STAGE (YLS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Young larval stage (YLS) is the first stage of the mealworms' development, characterized by a weight of -3 mg ind^-1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIDDLE LARVAL STAGE (MLS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Middle larval stage (MLS) is the second stage of the mealworms' development, characterized by a weight of -20 mg ind^-1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLD LARVAL STAGE (OLS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Old larval stage (OLS) is the third stage of the mealworms' development, characterized by a weight of -80 mg ind^-1."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUMULATIVE CONSUMPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cumulative consumption is the process of measuring the total amount of micro-PS (MPS) consumed by the mealworms over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVORSHIP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Survivorship is the process of measuring the survival rate of the mealworms over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1283355f048671359adcde7d3137af9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MPS is a nutrient that affects the survival and growth of mealworms, with varying effects at different larval stages."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPS is a type of toxin that can cause harm to mealworms, including weight loss and higher mortality."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPS refers to a type of chemical property that is ingested by mealworms and can cause harm to their growth and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPS refers to the microplastic particles being fed to the mealworms, with varying effects on their consumption and degradation abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPs, or microplastics, are small plastic particles that can be biodegraded by larvae, with a size range of &gt;1 μm."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPs are microplastic particles that can be ingested by Tenebrio larvae, causing oxidative stress and ecotoxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPs are microplastics that are used in the study to investigate the biodegradation of aged MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"MPs refer to microplastic particles that are produced during the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"YLS is a reference to a group in a study on the effects of microplastics on mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"YLS is the young larval stage of mealworms, where they are more susceptible to the effects of different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"YLS refers to the young larval stage of the mealworms, which has the lowest consumption and degradation abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MLS is a reference to a group in a study on the effects of microplastics on mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"MLS is the middle larval stage of mealworms, where they show varying responses to different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"MLS refers to the middle larval stage of the mealworms, which has moderate consumption and degradation abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"OLS is a reference to a group in a study on the effects of microplastics on mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"OLS is the old larval stage of mealworms, where they are less affected by the negative effects of MPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"OLS refers to the old larval stage of the mealworms, which has the highest consumption and degradation abilities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYL GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboxyl groups are a functional group that can be modified through oxidation, leading to the degradation of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxyl groups are a type of functional group that is formed during the biodegradation of HDPE, indicating the progression of biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6675480dfd01dcb533166d01b8e5482e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C—N STRETCH VIBRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C—N stretch vibration is a chemical property that can be used to analyze the modification of functional groups in microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METAMORPHOSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metamorphosis is a biological process undergone by the insects, with different rates depending on the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metamorphosis is a physiological response of mealworms to microplastic consumption, which can be affected by the larval age and consumption rate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metamorphosis is the process by which mealworms transform into pupae, with its rate and timing being affected by different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metamorphosis is the biological process by which Tenebrio molitor transforms from one life stage to another, influenced by nutritional factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02f21478b87845df31740b3dab37d197&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORTALITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mortality is a biological process affecting the insects, with different rates depending on the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortality is a health measure that can be affected by the ingestion of microplastics in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortality is a health measure that reflects the number of mealworms that die in response to different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortality is a measure of the number of yellow mealworms that died during the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortality is a health measure used to assess the impact of plastic ingestion on the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortality is a measure of the number of Tenebrio molitor that die, which can be affected by the type of feed provided."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mortality refers to the death rate of insects in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-531058c4540bd4e6a50d141db01d4d11&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbf28f07f3e46b29e447aae784667c29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddb3edd44829125161ad624ea793ae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVING PERIOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HEALTH MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surviving period is a health measure that reflects the length of time mealworms survive in response to different diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FITTED DEATH RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fitted death rate is a biochemical measure that reflects the rate at which mealworms die in response to different diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPATION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupation rate is a biological marker that reflects the number of mealworms that form pupae in response to different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation rate is a physiological parameter measured in the larvae, indicating the percentage of larvae that pupate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation rate is the physiological response of the larvae to the feedstock, measured as the percentage of larvae that pupate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation rate refers to the percentage of larvae that successfully pupate and form adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupation rate is a measure of the percentage of mealworms that successfully pupate, which is affected by their diet, including the consumption of plastics with or without bran."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e557113f1cfd2472fa9c51d1cdc3069a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPATION DISTRIBUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupation distribution is a biological process that reflects the timing and pattern of pupation in response to different diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAL WEIGHT DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larval weight development is a biological process that reflects the growth and development of mealworms over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH PATTERN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth pattern is a biological process that reflects the change in larval weight over time in response to different diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SENESCENCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Senescence is a biological process that reflects the decline in physical condition and function of mealworms as they age."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy is a crucial component for the survival and development of organisms, and is obtained from food sources and stored in reserves."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy is a measure of the amount of energy that is available to an organism for growth, maintenance, and reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy is a necessary component for the survival and growth of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy is a nutrient that is essential for the survival of the larvae, and the diet had an effect on the availability of energy."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy is a nutritional component that is accumulated as a reserve throughout the larval stage of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy is a physiological response that is obtained by mealworms from the digestion of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy is a physical property that is produced during bioenergy production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy is a nutrient analyzed in the study, with mealworms showing significant changes in their energy levels when fed different materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-352650a946ab941cec3f7b9813faeee1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTHORACICOTROPIC HORMONE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"HORMONE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prothoracicotropic hormone is a hormone that is involved in the regulation of pupation in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-84558838faaf585c61e883356c52c0e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JUVENILE HORMONE&quot;">
