    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environment refers to the ecological concept that is affected by the presence of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The environment refers to the natural world, including ecosystems, soil, water, and air, which can be impacted by plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The environment is the ecosystem that is affected by plastic waste and can benefit from the consumption of plastics by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environment refers to the external surroundings in which organisms live, and it is influenced by the ability of microorganisms to biodegrade organic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The environment is the ecosystem that is affected by the degradation and assimilation of poly (ethylene terephthalate) by the bacterium."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Environment is the setting where plastic degradation and pollution are being studied, including factors such as temperature and composting conditions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d7f6907ee7ce47b00537b1458fcc029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05fb1b56e288f49324a636e1365b5406&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe</data>
    </node>
