    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE TEREPHTHALATE (PET)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PET is a type of plastic that is widely used and has a different structure than PE and PP."&lt;SEP&gt;Polyethylene Terephthalate (PET) is a synthetic polymer, commonly known as polyester in the textile industry, with a molecular weight of around 20.00 kDa. It is a type of plastic that is widely used in packaging materials and other applications. PET is a mass-produced fossil-based plastic polymer that contributes to catastrophic levels of plastic pollution. Despite being known to be resistant to biodegradation, PET can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, fungal enzymes, and insects, such as the larvae of T. molitor and Z. atratus, as well as Black Soldier Fly larvae, which can affect its central carbon metabolism. Additionally, PET can be broken down and recycled by PET depolymerase. However, its degradation rate is slow, and it is almost unsusceptible to biodegradation under normal conditions. PET is also used in the production of storage jars and is compared to other plastics like polypropylene (PP). Its widespread use has significant implications for plastic waste management and biotechnology, and it can cause physiological stress responses in macroinvertebrates. Overall, Polyethylene Terephthalate (PET) is a complex plastic polymer with varying degrees of biodegradability, depending on the conditions and organisms involved.&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate (PET) is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, such as the yellow mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate (PET) is a type of petro-based polymer mentioned as a potential area of future research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate (PET) is a type of petro-based polymer that may be studied in future research on plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f3365d0b08e5e77183d813ce6a1049&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-02e6f7bbb2c1ef92c57b423020b0cc5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2359b10600f30376fe077f5e942cc999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d575c206eb616c4c970fd48fe3349247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa5755e6c9a5eeae3f595d901dff422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78f3828bbe45c2c38004a29d55dcbf40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a</data>
    </node>
