    <node id="&quot;ENZYME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymes are biological molecules that can catalyze chemical reactions, including the breakdown of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes are biological molecules that catalyze chemical reactions, including those involved in biodegradation, and can serve as markers for biodegradation activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes are involved in the biodegradation of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes, such as those produced by microorganisms in the gut of larvae, are involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes are biological molecules that catalyze specific chemical reactions, such as the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes are biological molecules that catalyze chemical reactions, including the degradation of plant biomass and synthetic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymes are biological molecules that catalyze chemical reactions, and are involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms."</data>
