      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wei-Min Wu is a corresponding author of the study, affiliated with Stanford University."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher and author of the study on biodegradation of polyethylene terephthalate by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher who co-authored a study on the biodegradation of microplastics by Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher who contributed to the study on PET biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher who has studied the biodegradation of plastics by insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is an author of the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher involved in the study of biodegradation of polyethylene by Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher who has contributed to the study of polystyrene (PS) degradation by strain YT2."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is an author of the study on mealworms and plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher who has contributed to the study of polyethylene biodegradation and is a corresponding author."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is an author who was involved in the conceptualization, methodology, supervision, validation, and writing of the research on polypropylene (PP) biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher who studied the biodegradation of LDPE by Tenebrio obscurus and Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wei-Min Wu is a researcher and corresponding author of the study on biodegradation of commercial plastics."</data>
