    <node id="&quot;PET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PET (polyethylene terephthalate) is a type of plastic that is found in some animal-based traditional medicinal materials, indicating the presence of microplastics in these materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of material that has not been tested for biodegradation by T. obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of plastic that affects the metabolism and microbiota of insect models."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of plastic that has a positive metabolic interaction with BSF larvae, indicating its potential for degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of plastic used in the study to expose the insect larva."&lt;SEP&gt;PET, also known as polyethylene terephthalate, is a type of plastic material that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, including the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae. The larvae of T. molitor, also known as mealworms, can ingest and digest PET, providing energy for their survival and growth. PET is susceptible to microbial degradation and enzymatic attack due to its hydrolysable ester backbones. The biodegradation of PET by T. molitor larvae is affected by the molecular weight of the plastic, with different molecular weights being tested for their effect on the biodegradation process. Additionally, PET can be hydrolyzed by enzymes such as lipase, cutinase, carboxylesterase, and alkane 1-monoxygenase. The degradation products of PET can be utilized by the gut microbiota and the larval host. PET is being studied for its biodegradation properties, and it is used as a primary diet for T. molitor larvae in biodegradation tests. The biodegradation of PET by microorganisms, including T. molitor larvae, is a subject of ongoing research, with potential implications for the management of plastic waste. Overall, PET is a type of plastic polymer that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae and other microorganisms, and its biodegradation is influenced by various factors, including molecular weight and enzymatic activity.&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of plastic that is hydrolyzable and has been studied for its biodegradation, with factors such as surface hydrophobicity and molecular weight distribution affecting its degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of plastic that is mentioned as a potential target for biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PET is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by the larvae of Tenebrio molitor and other insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96c76e51cdc8235f685cdc9efc87b6a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84a8f1c256b1141b6bd2b404e817dfb7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d290a6a81802d3048c35d2a2fb1252c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df5e2448d1e9703b511b85725469467e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-74e2601f950d62c093ceb86612b2374f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e81871d41a32fbdcbbd4f699efae3d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-694aaaa7c2839ea048d46b6a2bb13748&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5338aa2127367c868a3e7331e1f66225&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
