    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AGAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agar is a biological reagent used as an adhesive to make agar-PET gel to feed the larvae, serving as a nutrient source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient source being used in the experiment, mixed with PET to feed the T. molitor larvae, and helps in their survival and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient source used to feed insects in laboratory experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a chemical used as a growth medium for microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient component of Blood Agar, serving as a gelling agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient used in the preparation of agar medium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a chemical compound used in the preparation of the LB agar medium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient used to support the growth of microorganisms, including T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient source used as a control group in the experiment to compare with PP degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient source used to feed Tenebrio molitor larvae in addition to polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient used as a control diet for the T. molitor larvae, compared to the PET-agar gel."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a type of nutrient used as an adhesive in biodegradation tests, specifically for mixing with PE powders to allow larvae to ingest and biodegrade them."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient used in the cultivation of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a nutrient used to mix with PE microplastics during incubation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is a chemical compound used in the preparation of LB medium."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agar is used to prepare agar plates for growth media."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a32ea55d79e87933e26b4165db47b1fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fca6acde6809ed3c727d7bffdbfd1ada&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-152e743d95b64fab136afadf0304d459&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T. MOLITOR LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T. molitor larvae are affected by changes in reserve dynamics and have difficulty completing their life cycle when fed with polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae are the early stages of development of the T. molitor insect, and are being studied in terms of their growth and reserve dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae, also known as mealworms, are capable of biodegrading high-purity PS with various molecular weights."&lt;SEP&gt;T. molitor larvae, also known as mealworms, are the larvae of the mealworm beetle. They are a species of insects that have the ability to depolymerize and biodegrade various types of plastics, including low-density polyethylene (LDPE), polystyrene (PS), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), polypropylene (PP), and expanded polystyrene (EPS). The gut microbiome of T. molitor larvae plays a crucial role in the degradation process, although their ability to depolymerize certain plastics, such as PET, can be independent of gut microbes. T. molitor larvae are being used in the study of biodegradation of plastics, specifically for breaking down polymers like PS, LDPE, and PP. They are being fed with different diets to test their capacity to ingest and biodegrade various types of plastics. T. molitor larvae exhibit oxidative stress responses to plastic microplastics and have a dietary adaptive regulatory mechanism to survive and reproduce in environments with nutrient restrictions. The digestive gene expression of T. molitor larvae is being examined, and their gut microbial community is being analyzed for its potential role in the biodegradation process. Overall, T. molitor larvae are a significant subject of study in the field of biodegradation of plastics, and their ability to consume and biodegrade plastic polymers makes them a valuable tool in the efforts to address plastic pollution. They are capable of producing various degradation products when biodegrading microplastics, such as PE and PS. T. molitor larvae have been compared to other species, such as Z. atratus larvae, in terms of their consumption rates of different plastics, with T. molitor larvae having a lower PP consumption rate. Their consumption and survival rates are also being analyzed in relation to microplastic ingestion, providing valuable insights into their potential for biodegradation and their potential applications in addressing plastic pollution.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-846559469c70e081884fea2f9a4b7317&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a14229bceb339a4ca1baf0772b47ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5238515b2316265fb5cb6c6295c54e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5a7fb8d6a76ecfbfc810f952bfba090&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a3e42eecd3967a9e53cfadc926363ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70eb294c60e73338ed59a2eddf057c1e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e98fb757cb68ae45626058d9c3a15cb4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b673e7590aa1d03b7721694ed73cd74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c5fc4d4324334254706d6d5f9312276&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0efd7a9e4443dc5d3dfe588c7f7efc13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca86254d65e47c4049e193cf2098b964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5</data>
    </node>
