    <node id="&quot;WB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Abbreviation for Wheat Bran"&lt;SEP&gt;"WB is a nutrient source used to feed Tenebrio molitor larvae, used as a comparison to polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"WB is a type of nutrient used to feed the T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"WB is a product that is used as a normal feed and has a high protein content."&lt;SEP&gt;"WB is a type of diet that is high in protein and is used as a control group in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"WB is a type of feedstock being used as a control."&lt;SEP&gt;"WB is a type of diet that is being used to compare with plastic diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"WB refers to a control diet used in the study, without polyethylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"WB, or wheat bran, is a type of nutrient-rich feedstock that is used to supplement the diet of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."</data>
