    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation Rate is a measure of the rate at which mealworms break down EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation rate is a biochemical measure used to assess the rate at which polypropylene is broken down by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation rate is a measure of how quickly PET polymers are broken down."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation rate is a measure of the rate at which microorganisms, such as insect larvae, break down organic materials like polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation rate is a measure of how quickly microorganisms can break down organic materials, such as polyethylene terephthalate (PET) polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation rate is a biochemical measure used to quantify the rate at which EPS is degraded by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation rate is a measure of the rate at which microorganisms break down organic materials, such as plastic."</data>
