      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gentamicin sulfate is a specific antibiotic used to suppress gut bacteria in the T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used in the suppression tests to understand its effect on the biodegradation of EPS and LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used to suppress gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used to suppress the gut microbiome of the mealworms, allowing for the study of the mealworm's role in plastic degradation without microbial influence."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is a type of antibiotic that is not used in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used to suppress the growth of microorganisms in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used to suppress gut microbes in T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used to suppress gut microbiota in T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae, in order to examine its effect on PP degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic being used to suppress the gut bacteria of the insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gentamicin sulfate is an antibiotic used in the experiment."</data>
