    <node id="&quot;ACINETOBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacter sp. is a PS-degrading bacteria, strongly associated with PS degradation in the gut microbiome of T. castaneum larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a bacterium that is dominant in the gut microbiomes of PET-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that includes strain NyZ450, which is capable of degrading PE mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a genus of bacteria that may be involved in PP degradation, particularly in the degradation of medium MW PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that is associated with the degradation of medium molecular weight polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a genus of bacteria that includes species capable of biodegrading polyethylene mulching films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that is associated with PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that can biodegrade polyethylene mulching films."</data>
