    <node id="&quot;CITROBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrobacter sp. is a bacterial strain that has been associated with the biodegradation of polyethylene plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter sp. is a bacterium that is dominant in the gut microbiomes of PET-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter sp. is a bacterium associated with PE and PS degradation, capable of utilizing oxygen and more abundant in plastic-only diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter sp. is a bacterium that is strongly associated with the degradation of both polyethylene and polystyrene in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter sp. is a type of microorganism that is more abundant in plastic-only diets and is associated with the degradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that has been found to be involved in the degradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter sp. is a species of bacteria that is associated with the biodegradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter sp. is a type of bacteria that has been found to be associated with the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP) in the gut microbiome of Zophobas atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter sp. is a type of gut microbe that is strongly associated with the PP-fed gut microbiome of Z. atratus larvae."</data>
