    <node id="&quot;MICROBIOTA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbiota is a biological concept that refers to the community of microorganisms that live in a particular environment, including the digestive tracts of T. molitor larvae and adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms living in the digestive tract of T. molitor, which plays a role in PS biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that are present in the gut of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the intestines of mealworms and contribute to polystyrene degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in a particular environment, such as the gut of invertebrates, and can play a role in degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the digestive tract of Tenebrio molitor and have been found to have the ability to degrade PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota is the community of microorganisms that live in the digestive system and vary depending on the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in a particular environment, such as the gut of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in a particular environment, such as the gut of an insect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live within an organism or ecosystem."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the insect gut and contribute to the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms that live in a particular environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota refers to the community of microorganisms, including nitrogen-fixing bacteria, that live in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiota is a community of microorganisms that plays a crucial role in biodegradation and other biological processes."</data>
