    <node id="&quot;ASSIMILATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Assimilation is a biological process by which mealworms incorporate the carbon from the plastics they consume into their biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assimilation is the process by which microorganisms incorporate PET-derived molecules into their biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Assimilation is the process by which the bacterium incorporates the broken-down components of poly (ethylene terephthalate) into its own biomass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d7f6907ee7ce47b00537b1458fcc029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut refers to the digestive system of an organism, and in the case of mealworms, it is where the gut microorganisms live."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut is the part of the mealworm's body where nitrogen-fixing bacteria are found."&lt;SEP&gt;GUT, referring to the digestive system of various organisms, including Tenebrio molitor larvae and mealworms, is a physical characteristic that functions as a bioreactor, facilitating the biodegradation of various polymers such as polyethylene, polypropylene, polystyrene (PS), and polyethylene terephthalate (PET). The GUT is home to symbiotic microbiota, including gut bacteria, that aid in digestion and biodegradation processes. In the case of Tenebrio molitor larvae and mealworms, the GUT is where the breakdown of these polymers takes place, involving microbes and extracellular enzymes, with a retention time of 12-15 hours for polystyrene degradation. The GUT is also a vital organ in insects, including Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, that is involved in digestion and immunity. Furthermore, the GUT is where metabolites are being analyzed, and its bacteria are being studied. Overall, GUT plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of various polymers, and its unique characteristics make it an important area of study in understanding the biodegradation processes of different organisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90367ecb21e0f14b2e548acf307a2628&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b3e57543d6b365fff3ef2b14ddb309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d57e056cd3b06b37d22117fc75e3a4df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbc20d6948e6ca1157ecd7f80a183952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdf2753a9a78b282c1ca2c0539e3203d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d</data>
    </node>
