    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MINERALIZATION PROCESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mineralization process is a series of biological reactions that convert organic substances, such as polystyrene, into inorganic substances, such as carbon dioxide and water."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization process is the process by which the products of depolymerization are further broken down into CO2 and other simple compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization process refers to the process by which organic matter is converted into inorganic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mineralization process refers to the conversion of organic compounds into inorganic compounds by the gut microbiome of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization process refers to the series of steps by which microorganisms break down organic materials, such as polystyrene, into inorganic compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mineralization process refers to the process by which organic matter is converted into inorganic matter."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21c07a838ff0a489c73c8319e5011134&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54215690a971d0637c3a6fa61d10f685&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f35f87c2ff7792eb41bdd8debdb5f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2b715dc0bf578795b387fe1255d07f22</data>
