      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae of Tenebrio molitor are microorganisms that have been studied for their ability to biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larvae of Tenebrio molitor is a life stage of the insect that can biodegrade expanded polystyrene and low-density polyethylene foams."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae of Tenebrio molitor are a life stage of the yellow mealworm that can digest and biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae of Tenebrio molitor, also known as mealworms, are capable of ingesting and biodegrading microplastics."</data>
