    <node id="&quot;METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolism is a biological process aimed at generating necessary substrates for basic cellular processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is a biological process that is affected by microplastic exposure, leading to changes in an organism's energy production and utilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is a biological process that is affected by the different diets, with varying levels of activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is the process by which mealworms break down and utilize microplastics, with varying effects depending on the type of microplastic and region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is the process by which organisms break down and utilize nutrients, and has been found to play a key role in the biodegradation of plastics by certain species of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is the process by which organisms convert energy and nutrients into the components that make up their cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is the process by which organisms, such as the wax moth and the mealworm, convert nutrients into energy and synthesize new biomass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is a biological process undergone by the insects, with different rates depending on the diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The proteins synthesized from the genetic code are involved in various metabolic processes, which are essential for the maintenance of life."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is the process by which organisms convert energy and nutrients into the components that make up living cells."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolism is the process by which organisms convert energy and nutrients into the components that make up living cells."</data>
