    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBE-DEPENDENT DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbe-dependent depolymerization is a biological process by which microorganisms in the gut of insects such as yellow mealworms and superworms break down plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbe-dependent depolymerization is a process by which certain species of insects, including Tenebrio molitor, are able to break down plastics with the aid of gut microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microbe-dependent depolymerization is a biological process that involves the breakdown of plastics by microorganisms with the help of gut microbes."</data>
