    <node id="&quot;PLESIOPHTHALMUS DAVIDIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plesiophthalmus davidis are insects that have the ability to digest and biodegrade plastic products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis is a species of insect larvae that has been found to biodegrade plastics, specifically PE and PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis is a species of insect larvae that is capable of biodegrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis is a species of insect that has been found to have a gut microbial flora that biodegrades polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis is an insect that can biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis is a species of insect that is mentioned as a comparison to Tenebrio molitor in terms of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plesiophthalmus davidis is a species of insects that have a gut microbial flora capable of biodegrading polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f15cc70e99a3287ced1a6cbb6c8d76a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microbes are microorganisms that live in the gut of insects such as mealworms and have the ability to digest and biodegrade plastic products."&lt;SEP&gt;Gut Microbes are microorganisms that live in the gut of various organisms, including insects such as Tenebrio molitor larvae, mealworms, superworms, and yellow mealworms. They play a crucial role in various physiological processes and are essential for the overall health and development of the organism. Gut Microbes are responsible for degrading various substances, including plastics, polystyrene (PS), polyethylene terephthalate (PET), and natural lignocellulosic polymers. They contribute to the biodegradation of synthetic plastics, such as low-density polyethylene (LDPE), and aid in the depolymerization process. The natural diet of these organisms, such as lignocellulose, may be related to their ability to degrade certain plastics. Gut Microbes are also involved in the biodegradation of aged microplastics (MPs) and have PS-degrading activity. They are affected by antibiotic treatment, which highlights the importance of these microorganisms in the biodegradation process. Overall, Gut Microbes are a vital component of the ecosystem, and their ability to degrade plastics and other substances makes them a crucial area of study in the field of environmental science. While the role of Gut Microbes in the biodegradation of certain plastics, such as LDPE, may be independent or less dependent on them, they play a significant role in the biodegradation of various substances, making them a key area of research.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-79c11bccb4ef9bd152bdae9b5c2c5c8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16328c3c685f35501c3639525e997d2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10474cc69c90eb0c245c8f55d1ec2834&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-013f364e92a266c0e922cb0582f7a997&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88f3ed3eec20cee61421cc094dde89f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1ab39969c669dba42f162e8497c23f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21bee96879472a1c6df454d862dc9e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a193cc62c03cb6460b0434df42d8c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b74f16813537103549cdcb6770abaea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-705bf68703e5d236b2ffabb7ecb3de5e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b12468cce513394dbebb8b4ce27f62d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f</data>
    </node>
