    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYLACTIC ACID (PLA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polylactic Acid (PLA) is a biodegradable plastic that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor, with a higher biodegradation rate than polyvinyl chloride and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a type of biodegradable polymer that requires specific conditions for degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a type of plastic polymer that can be biodegraded by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a type of plastic that can be degraded by certain insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by T. molitor, among other microorganisms and insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic acid (PLA) is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms, with a range of properties and applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polylactic Acid (PLA) is a type of plastic that affects the central carbon metabolism of insect models, with Mealworm and Wax Moth larvae showing increased metabolic activity when exposed to it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff933f404b1e6da13d6c1319bc7432c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44bfda02e6c219cb097ec88543433798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0c513c586aa89e48e9570525bfc5366&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f1aa99e321e9e3b94552e6c6f8e00f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENTAMICIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ANTIBIOTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">Gentamicin is an antibiotic used to treat bacterial infections, and its presence affects the digestion of various plastics by certain insect larvae. In the context of scientific research, Gentamicin is utilized to understand the activity of gut bacteria and its effect on the depolymerization of plastics, such as polystyrene (PS), polyethylene (PE), and polypropylene (PP). Gentamicin has been used in studies to inhibit the growth of gut microbes in various larvae, including Tenebrio molitor, Tenebrio obscurus, and Zophobas atratus, which in turn affects the degradation of plastics. The antibiotic is effective in suppressing the growth of gut bacteria in these larvae, resulting in the loss of ability to depolymerize and mineralize plastics. Specifically, Gentamicin has been used to inhibit the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms, highlighting the importance of gut microflora in the degradation process. Additionally, Gentamicin has been used to eliminate gut microbes of larvae and to reduce the effectiveness of their gut bacteria in biodegrading extracellular polymeric substances (EPS). In some studies, Gentamicin has been used to inhibit the biodegradation of PS, but not low-density polyethylene (LDPE). Gentamicin's role in these studies has provided significant insights into the importance of gut microflora in the degradation of plastics, and its use has helped to advance our understanding of the complex relationships between microbes, plastics, and the environment. Furthermore, Gentamicin is used to suppress gut microbes in the larvae of T. molitor and T. obscurus, affecting the biodegradation of LDPE, and to study its effect on LDPE depolymerization. Overall, Gentamicin is a valuable tool in understanding the role of gut bacteria in the biodegradation of plastics and has been used in various experiments to suppress the growth of certain microorganisms and study its effects on the depolymerization of plastics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-697bf99ecf19f99243f3b5a4ef5b334c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68041096d198a27b4ed526281746b7f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207d77d551e893eda6578be68ca3d0db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4df787efdb36123e3f2a76b5402278ec&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5dc0ba5d8a1abfb746af0dedb7d575b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68c274a59cd5db4cd675bca51f11adb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85c9587b55f24a8ae5ba6b478dbb98e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4443da1fe36ec7133cd5add18d1957a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d5a9fbe4803ded646c6a5e4d23ca93a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06ba9ca61fb4f42582bbf7bd00ff0005&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8b7b5a840af17cee78d71347e532d51&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5613b129e38cb777855c04f228fe7e9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c42631c88da011b836666dae04cfa11a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HUMIDITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Humidity is a factor that affects the mealworms' eating habits and mobility, with variable humidity in the at-home setting."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is a physical property derived using the gravimetric method."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is a physical property that affects the behavior and growth of organisms, such as the mealworm beetle."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is a physical property that can affect the survival and plastic consumption of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is a physical property that can influence the growth and activity of microorganisms, such as those found in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is an environmental parameter that can influence the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is a physical property that affects the growth and development of mealworms, with a humidity of 70-80% and 80% used in the experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is a physical property that is being controlled in the experiment, with a set point of 80%."&lt;SEP&gt;"Humidity is a physical property that is maintained between 30% to 40% throughout the experiment."</data>
