    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROFLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microflora is a biological concept that refers to the collective microorganisms present in a particular environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microflora refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microflora refers to the microorganisms present in the intestines of the Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microflora of T. molitor gut microorganisms have efficient biodegradation ability, making them interesting for further research."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microflora refers to the community of microorganisms present in the insect gut, with its composition and activity affecting the degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microflora refers to the community of microorganisms that live within the gut of mealworms and play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84f576487c8d473c1524eb1141730a12&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3891caf14683493be3d8709ced467492</data>
    </node>
