    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROFLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut microflora can be collected using rinsing of extracted gut tissue or collecting intestinal tissue for DNA extraction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microflora is a biological concept that refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the intestines of mice."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microflora refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the digestive system of an organism, such as an insect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microflora plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms, as evidenced by the loss of degradation ability when mealworms are fed the antibiotic gentamicin."</data>
