    <node id="&quot;ACINETOBACTER SP. STRAIN NYZ450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterial isolate that can degrade polyethylene mulching films when co-cultured with Bacillus sp. strain NyZ451."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterial strain that can degrade LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterial strain that can grow as a co-culture on polyethylene as a sole carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterial strain that is capable of biodegrading polyethylene mulching films in co-culture with Bacillus sp. strain NYZ451."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterial strain that degrades PE, with a GenBank accession number MT459299 for its 16S rRNA gene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Acinetobacter sp. strain NyZ450 is a bacterial strain that has been isolated from the intestine of the mealworm and has been found to have PE-degrading activity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b42ef7860e1f056d47955d0d13a15cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c39e41f4f36c9c6854fa71508c35a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24ba7d6b1b5275089cbabe56bc33b92e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d97be338c51b4c4354e2d0f8de9c9dc8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-567c36cf69b624a7ec0d891d3bd15163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116</data>
    </node>
