    <node id="&quot;MASS LOSS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mass loss is a biochemical measure being used to study the effects of different materials on mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a biological measure used to assess the degradation of plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a measure of the amount of plastic consumed by mealworms during experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a physical property used to measure the amount of microplastics ingested by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a physiological parameter measured in the larvae, indicating the amount of mass lost during the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the decrease in mass of the plastics over time, used as a measure of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a physiological response that is being studied in mealworms that are being fed different types of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a physical characteristic of the plastic waste that mealworms digest, with its measurement and calculation being important factors in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the decrease in mass of the LDPE substrate after being in contact with the Greater Wax Moth Larvae or mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a measure of the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a physiological response being measured in the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss refers to the decrease in mass of the mealworms over the duration of the experiment, which is affected by the type of plastic consumed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a physiological response analyzed in the study, with mealworms showing significant changes in their mass when fed different materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass loss is a measure of the amount of PS that is broken down by mealworms over time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6d515521d6d2b72e82154cc544d26cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d47d39d364c5c66ef3fc32ef741ca63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e9eb740edf53e540b468122b302cb82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78cd8d4684fa9e0519635dba9f124a08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d575c206eb616c4c970fd48fe3349247&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a11793261251544a542146bc9bf0c5dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c7abab621f928edec1e33d1fe2afd4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
