    <node id="&quot;PS FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS foam is a product that is being fed to the larvae, and the nitrogen-fixing bacteria can only provide a limited amount of protein to the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of plastic that can be ingested and digested by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of plastic that is consumed by mealworms, which can digest and assimilate the carbon from it."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is the type of plastic used in the study, provided as a feed for the mealworms and as a material for microbial cultures."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of plastic that is used as a food source for insects in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of plastic that is consumed by superworms and yellow mealworms, with a morphology that changes over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of plastic that is being consumed and biodegraded by the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of plastic used in the study to test biodegradation by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is another type of microplastic that is consumed by T. molitor larvae, with different effects on their growth and survival compared to PE film."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS foam is a type of product that can be biodegraded by T. obscurus larvae through gut-microbe dependent depolymerization."</data>
