    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS degradation is a biological process that occurs in the gut of mealworms, and is affected by the presence of bran and gentamicin."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS degradation is the process by which T. molitor larvae break down PS foam, and it is influenced by factors such as diet and temperature."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS degradation is the process by which polystyrene is broken down, and it is influenced by enzymatic activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS degradation is a biological process that refers to the breakdown of polystyrene materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS degradation refers to the process by which mealworms break down polystyrene into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS degradation is the process by which PS is broken down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS degradation refers to the process of breaking down polystyrene."</data>
