    <node id="&quot;FTIR ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR Analysis is a biological process that is being used to study the changes in the functional groups of PU Foam after biodegradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR Analysis is a method used for analyzing the changes in the functional groups of PU Foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a biological process used to analyze the degradation of PS by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of a substance, in this case, polystyrene and its biodegradation products."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of materials, such as the frass samples from the larvae of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a technology used to analyze the surface changes of polystyrene during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a technique used to analyze the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a technology used to study the surface morphology and functional groups of PS/CS samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a method used to analyze the chemical structure of polymers, such as polyethylene terephthalate (PET)."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a biochemical measure used to examine the chemical modifications of plastics, such as PE and PS, after degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a biochemical measure that is used to analyze the chemical composition of polyethylene (PE) and its degradation products."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a biochemical measure used to analyze the physiochemical properties of substances, including the biodegradation of polyethylene (HDPE) waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a technique used to characterize the oxidation and chemical modification of polyethylene polymers after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a method used to study the biodegradation of PS, showing chemical changes and incorporation of oxygen in the PS polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a biochemical measure used to study the degradation of polystyrene foam by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a technique used to study the degradation of PS by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a biological function used to determine the changes in the functional groups of plastics after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analysis is a biochemical measure used to provide evidence of oxidation and depolymerization of LDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df4c8c66bfbbfc37ed842f53d2b8796c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd73d3cca5434181ee9dd1ad1b8f8ab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9aa972c0f1c2838103f61cd8ae101a8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39596f0742e3d89f278017df88b8065b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eecad183fc5700f3d7e0a266e293de1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MWD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MWD is a biochemical measure that is used to characterize the molecular weight distribution of PS residues extracted from frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD is a measure of the molecular weight distribution of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD is a type of biochemical measure that is being used to analyze the degradation of PS, representing the molecular weight distribution of the PS residues."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD refers to the molecular weight distribution of a polymer, which can shift during the degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD, or molecular weight distribution, is a measure of the range of molecular weights present in a polymer, such as polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD, or molecular weight distribution, is a measure used to analyze the degradation of PS by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD is a measure of the molecular weight distribution of a polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"MWD is a measure of the molecular weight distribution of the LDPE molecules before and after biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc7f923e7edaa7bcfa79c0f7a9896e00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d3b3c7bbc61318a9728caff13ac5b04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cbedc06292e5cf07fbca1958d8587e6</data>
    </node>
