      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboxylic acid groups are a type of functional group present in the biodegradation products of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acid groups are a type of functional group that can be detected in the FTIR spectra of frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acid groups are a type of functional group that is associated with the FTIR spectra of PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acid groups are a type of functional group that is formed during the degradation of polystyrene, which can influence the chemical composition of the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acid groups are a type of functional group that are formed during the biodegradation of polystyrene, resulting in the incorporation of oxygen into the PS polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acid groups are a type of functional group that is present in the biodegraded LDPE, as shown by the FTIR spectra."</data>
