    <node id="&quot;LIFE CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Life Cycle is a biological concept that is completed by polystyrene-fed larvae of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle refers to the different stages of an organism's life, from birth to death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle refers to the different stages of growth and development of an organism, such as the larvae of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle of yellow mealworms is affected by their ability to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle of the yellow mealworms is affected by their ability to biodegrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle refers to the stages of development and growth of an organism, including the biodegradation of plastics by mealworms and other microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle refers to the stages of growth and development of an organism, from egg to adult."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle refers to the stages of development and growth of an organism, including superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The life cycle of A. grisea larvae is completed when they develop into pupae and moth, which can take around 6.8 and 10.7 days respectively."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle is a biological process being studied in the experiment, with its different stages being analyzed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle is the concept of the different stages of development of Tenebrio molitor, from larvae to adult."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle refers to the different stages of an organism's life, from birth to death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle is a biological concept that refers to the stages of growth and development in an organism from birth to death."&lt;SEP&gt;"Life cycle is the series of stages that an organism goes through from birth to death."</data>
