    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FTIR ANALYSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"FTIR analyses are a method used to examine the composition of mealworm fecula and compare it to the polystyrene feedstock."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analyses are a technique used to verify the formation of new functional groups during the degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"FTIR analyses is a technique used to study the formation of newly oxidative functional groups in polyethylene polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSUMPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Consumption is the process by which mealworms eat and digest PS, leading to its degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumption refers to the process of the larvae eating and digesting the PP foam."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm gut is a biological system that can break down plastics, including polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm gut is a microorganism that is studied in the context of gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm gut is a physical characteristic that is capable of degrading and mineralizing Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm gut refers to the digestive system of mealworms, where the degradation of PS takes place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut is a physical structure that can harbor microorganisms that contribute to EPS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut is the organ where the gut microbiome resides and where plastic degradation primarily occurs."&lt;SEP&gt;"The internal environment of the mealworm where microorganisms that can degrade plastics can be found."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut is a complex ecosystem that contains microorganisms and extracellular enzymes, which play a crucial role in the degradation of polyurethane."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm gut is the location where the plastic degradation takes place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut is the location where the degradation of plastics takes place, and it is home to a diverse community of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut of mealworms is the primary location where biodegradation of plastics occurs, involving a complex community of microbes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm gut is the digestive system of mealworms, which contains microorganisms that aid in the biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut is the environment where polystyrene biodegradation occurs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm gut is a physical characteristic of the mealworms that provides an ecological niche for the microbial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm gut is a physical characteristic of mealworms that is used for digestion and absorption of nutrients."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c28d5d503e85e3e6ad15cee35d50e98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89c37eb3e3a5b6ab731f5dbe280aa054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53ab7dd83bf51674598c6a5bdd146b90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457d054c08a16428ed81526fc2ddce41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1684575ed5f73a2ebe1adc7fbbb3b942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a4c43611ebe237c15c5f9201a9f8dbee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2c62bcfb28547d6b2336f142d27a326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
