    <node id="&quot;ERWINIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Erwinia is a genus of bacteria found in the digestive tracts of T. molitor adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is a genus of bacteria that is found in the digestive tracts of T. molitor, and is capable of degrading PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is a genus of bacteria that is prevalent in the gut of mealworms, with no significant differences in relative abundance between diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is a type of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is a genus of microorganisms that includes several species, such as Erwinia pirillorinigrans, Erwinia tasmaniensis, and Erwinia uzeniensis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Erwinia is a genus of microorganisms that is related to the genus Mixta."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff28716c2f25b8550595e1f473add0c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5318125e74217718b470b7721d1d6365&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-576a8e18f3d6ea8c7d4a5f2cd554423c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACTOBACILLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactobacillaceae is a family of bacteria that can be enriched in the intestines of animals fed with T. molitor, suggesting a beneficial effect on gut health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a family of bacteria that is present in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a family that includes species such as Lactobacillus crispatus, Lactobacillus graminis, and Lactobacillus salivarius."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a family of bacteria that is found in high abundance in the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a family of bacteria that is dominant in the gut-bacterial community of the bran-fed group, with a relative abundance of 47.87%."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a family of bacteria that is affected by the presence of MPs in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillaceae is a family of bacteria that is present in the gut microbial community of Tenebrio molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73db2a18ccd822d0da3ef61e68d3a6f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7367fc6115c08ae427a6e9e91eaa1de3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5251cc2ed910c3785b2c7242b7cbc11e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LEUCONOSTOCACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Leuconostocaceae is a family of bacteria that is found in high abundance in the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leuconostocaceae is a family of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Leuconostocaceae is a family of bacteria that is present in the gut of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04683827a8d88bc2fa28ae73ccc0714f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62</data>
