      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weights are a biochemical measure used to analyze the degradation of PS by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights are a physical property of plastics like LDPE, LLDPE, and HDPE that can affect their biodegradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights, including Mm, Mw, and Ms, are being used to examine the performance of depolymerization and biodegradation of PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights are a biochemical measure used to characterize the polymer depolymerization during biodegradation of the ingested plastics by insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weights are a measure of the size of molecules, used in this study to verify the biodegradation of polystyrene and polyethylene."</data>
