    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT DISTRIBUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight distribution is a biochemical measure that refers to the range of molecular weights of a polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a biochemical measure used to analyze the degradation of PS by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a measure of the range of molecular weights of microplastics, which can be affected by the metabolism of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a physical property of polypropylene that affects its biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a physical property of polymers that affects their biodegradation, with a wider distribution making it more difficult for microorganisms to break down."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a measure of the size of polystyrene molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a biochemical measure used to compare the molecular weight of LDPE feedstocks and frass of T. molitor and T. obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a measure of the range of molecular weights in a polymer."</data>
