    <node id="&quot;MEALWORMS (TENEBRIO MOLITOR)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) are insects capable of degrading polystyrene (PS), with their gut microbiome playing a significant role in the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are larvae that can break down plastics, including EPS, and have a significant role in EPS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms (Tenebrio molitor) are the microorganisms used in the study to biodegrade polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are insects that have been shown to degrade polystyrene through enzymatic activities."</data>
