    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLIGOMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oligomers are a type of chemical that can be released from plastic wastes and harm the environment and human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oligomers are complex compounds that are formed during the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oligomers are small molecules that are composed of a few monomer units, including those from polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oligomers are susceptible to biodegradation, similar to styrene monomers, but polystyrene is more resistant to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oligomers are small molecules that are formed during the biodegradation of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oligomers are molecules that are composed of a few monomer units and are involved in the degradation of polystyrene."</data>
