    <node id="&quot;BACTERIAL STRAINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacterial strains are microorganisms that are capable of biodegrading plastics, such as polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial strains are microorganisms that are isolated from the guts of waxworms and can biodegrade PE films."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial strains are microorganisms that can break down polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial strains refer to the specific types of bacteria that are part of the gut microbiome of mealworms, contributing to the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial strains are types of microorganisms that can effectively degrade plastics, isolated from the intestinal flora of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial strains from the guts of plastic-eating waxworms have been found to biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial strains have been found to biodegrade polyethylene and other plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial strains from the guts of waxworms can biodegrade polystyrene, indicating their potential in biodegradation processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03f4c282fe2323dc6e310501af888c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f26c2702cadbaabe34c0d0e5cd2ec9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15323ef47e29f2927f95274e49f4e5bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27</data>
    </node>
