    <node id="&quot;LACTOBACILLUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria present in the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor, involved in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a type of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria that is commonly found in the gut microbiomes of insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria that was significantly associated with the PE + bran diet compared to the bran diet and the PE diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a type of bacteria that has been found to be significantly associated with the degradation of polyethylene in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a type of microorganism that is present in the gut microbiome of mealworms and may play a role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a genus of bacteria that has been identified in the gut of mealworms and plays a role in the biodegradation of styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactobacillus is a type of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."</data>
