    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT GAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight gain is a physiological response of mealworms to consuming plastics, which may be due to the adaptation of mealworms to new food sources."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight gain is a physiological response that is measured in T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight gain is a physiological response that is affected by the feed conditions, with mealworms fed PS plus soy protein or bran showing increased weight gain compared to those fed PS alone."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight gain is a type of physiological response that is being measured in the experiment, with mealworms fed bran experiencing a 32.0 ± 1.5% weight gain."&lt;SEP&gt;"Weight gain is a physiological response of the larvae to the consumption of PS and nutrition-rich codiet."</data>
