      <data key="d1">"NaOH is a chemical compound mentioned in the text, but its role is not explicitly stated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Sodium hydroxide is used to collect CO2, which is then precipitated with BaCl2 to form BaCO3."&lt;SEP&gt;"NaOH is a chemical property used to remove CO2 from the air in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"NaOH is a chemical used to stop the reaction in the lipase activity analysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"NaOH is a chemical substance used in the Kjeldahl method for distillation."&lt;SEP&gt;"NaOH is a chemical used to trap CO2."</data>
