    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC-EATING MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic-Eating Mealworms are a type of mealworm that is capable of biodegrading plastics, including polystyrene and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-Eating Mealworms are insects that are capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-Eating Mealworms are insects that can digest and degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are a type of insect that can biodegrade plastics, including polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are a type of microorganism that is capable of degrading certain types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are a type of mealworm that is capable of biodegrading plastics, including polystyrene and other types of plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are a type of microbe that is capable of eating and biodegrading plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are insects that can eat and biodegrade polystyrene, with the help of gut microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms refer to the ability of Tenebrio molitor to degrade and consume plastics, including polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are a type of insect that can biodegrade polystyrene and other plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are a type of mealworm that is capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are a type of insect that has been found to be capable of biodegrading certain types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are capable of biodegrading and mineralizing polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating mealworms are a type of mealworm that is capable of eating and degrading polystyrene."</data>
