    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial Biodegradation is a biological process by which microorganisms break down substances, such as plastics, into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial biodegradation is a process by which microorganisms break down organic matter, and in this case, polystyrene, into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic materials, such as plastics, into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic materials, such as plastics, into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic substances, such as polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic compounds, such as polystyrene, into simpler substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30b68116bde3b0e31c29adbd05cadaaa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene Biodegradation is a biological process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which the mealworms and the bacteria in their gut break down the polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms, such as Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation refers to the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is a biological process by which microorganisms such as Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is a biological process that occurs in mealworms, leading to the breakdown of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is a biological process that occurs when insects such as Tenebrio molitor break down polystyrene into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which mealworms break down EPS into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms, such as those found in mealworms, break down polystyrene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene plastics into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which polystyrene is broken down by microorganisms such as Tenebrio obscurus and Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which the larvae and their gut bacteria break down PS into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is a process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polystyrene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene biodegradation refers to the breakdown of polystyrene by microorganisms, such as mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5ea4395a1eb1886507c72cdf33db169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a0e22d97687eaef3d31a60f7da6e668&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87427955fe47fc204be31f4d99036055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3351564dbd6a0ee6a8b97f6687378ffc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4da90774e2e5cb1fea30fd5aa390760&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-069f8447676509ffdd0028e9c05fb9ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cb5478046e8b80ff49694ccdb8f92fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc744f6fa5a9ea876a0423d37eedfc87</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyethylene Biodegradation is a biological process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene, a type of plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms, such as Tenebrio molitor, break down polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation refers to the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is a biological process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is the process by which A. grisea larvae break down PE into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is the process by which PE is broken down by mealworm species."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene plastics into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene biodegradation is a process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene into smaller components."</data>
