      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut Microbiome of Tenebrio Molitor is a biological concept that refers to the community of microorganisms living in the gut of Tenebrio Molitor, which plays a role in biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the gut of the mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor is a biological concept mentioned in the study as a potential source of microorganisms for biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the digestive system of the yellow mealworm."</data>
