    <node id="&quot;BIOREMEDIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bioremediation is a biological concept that refers to the use of living organisms to remove pollutants from the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a biological process that refers to the use of microorganisms to clean up pollutants, such as plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a biological process that uses living organisms to degrade and remove pollutants from the environment, with potential applications in waste management and sustainable bioremediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using living organisms to biodegrade pollutants, including plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a process that uses microorganisms to break down pollutants in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a process that uses microorganisms to break down hazardous chemicals and clean up polluted environments."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the use of living organisms or their enzymes to remove pollutants from the environment, and has been proposed as a solution to plastic waste pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the use of microorganisms to clean up pollutants in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a biological process that uses microorganisms to remove pollutants from the environment, as discussed in the study by Volkering et al."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the use of microorganisms to clean up pollutants in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using microorganisms to clean up pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a process that uses living organisms to remove pollutants from the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using living organisms to degrade or remove pollutants from the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using living organisms or their enzymes to remove pollutants from the environment, in this case, nanoplastic particles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using microorganisms to clean up environmental pollutants, and Achromobacter's ability to biodegrade polystyrene makes it a potential candidate for this process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using microorganisms to clean up pollutants in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using microorganisms to degrade pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation refers to the process of using microorganisms to clean up environmental pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is the process of using microorganisms to clean up pollutants, such as plastics, in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioremediation is a biological process that uses microorganisms to clean up pollutants in the environment."</data>
