    <node id="&quot;PYROLYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyrolysis is a chemical reaction that can be used to break down microplastics and is a key focus of study in the provided text."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a chemical reaction that involves the breakdown of materials, such as plastics, into simpler components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a chemical reaction that involves the decomposition of plastic waste into smaller components under high temperatures and a catalyst."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a process that involves the thermal decomposition of materials, such as plastics, to produce petro-chemical feedstock."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is the process by which LDPE microplastics undergo decomposition, resulting in a chain scission process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a type of chemical process that involves the thermal decomposition of organic matter, and has been found to produce bio-oil."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a process that occurs during TGA, where the sample undergoes a reaction that produces combustible gases and biochar."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrolysis is a process that involves the thermal decomposition of materials, including plastics, in the absence of oxygen."</data>
