    <node id="&quot;POLYURETHANE FOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyurethane foam is a type of plastic material that can be degraded by certain insect larvae, including superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane foam is a type of plastic polymer used in various applications, including automobile seats and coatings."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane foam is a type of plastic that can be degraded by certain microorganisms or enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane foam is a type of plastic that was utilized by mealworms in the experiment, with a significant change in surface structure after digestion."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane foam, referred to as PU, is the material being tested for biodegradation by the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane foam is a type of plastic that is used in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyurethane foam, also known as PU, is a type of plastic that can be degraded by superworms and yellow mealworms."</data>
