    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTH LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wax moth larvae are a type of macro-organism that can biodegrade polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae are insects that can biodegrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae are the larvae of the wax moth and can biodegrade plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae are microorganisms that digest plastic waste and produce biodiesel, with their growth and development being important factors in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae are the larvae of the wax moth, used in experiments to study the degradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae, specifically Galleria mellonella, are another type of macro-organism that has been found to consume and potentially biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moth larvae have been found to be capable of degrading microplastics."</data>
