      <data key="d1">"Macro-organisms are a type of organism that can biodegrade polyethylene and polystyrene, including mealworms and wax moth larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macro-organisms are large organisms that can biodegrade plastics, such as mealworms and wax moth larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macro-organisms refer to large organisms such as mealworms and wax moth larvae that are capable of consuming and biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Macro-organisms, such as larvae, are involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene, but their role is not fully understood."</data>
