    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANAEROBIC CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Anaerobic conditions are a biological concept that refers to the absence of oxygen, which is necessary for certain microorganisms to degrade certain pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions are conditions in which there is no oxygen present, which can affect the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions are a physical characteristic of the environment in which the bacteria degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions are an environmental condition under which certain bacteria, including those within the Enterobacter genus, can degrade polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions refer to an environment that lacks oxygen, which can affect the growth and activity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions refer to an environment without oxygen, where microorganisms can still thrive and degrade organic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions refer to an environment without oxygen, which affects the biodegradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions refer to an environment without oxygen, which affects the growth and activity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions refer to an environment without oxygen, which is necessary for LG3 to degrade PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions refer to an environment without oxygen, which is relevant to the biodegradation of plastics by certain bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions refer to an environment without oxygen, which is used to study the degradation of PS by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Anaerobic conditions refer to the absence of oxygen, which is used to culture the bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-345c72af5aa26d5c4e06d7df5d8a1c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dc6c2706bd609f920aa61d5ef2310db6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AEROBIC CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aerobic conditions are a physical characteristic of the environment in which the bacteria degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions are an environmental condition under which certain bacteria, including those within the Enterobacter genus, can degrade polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions are conditions in which oxygen is present, which can affect the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to an environment that contains oxygen, which can affect the growth and activity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to an environment with oxygen, where microorganisms can thrive and degrade organic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to an environment with oxygen, which also affects the biodegradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to an environment with oxygen, which is relevant to the biodegradation of plastics by certain bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to an environment with oxygen, which is used to study the degradation of PS by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aerobic conditions refer to the presence of oxygen, which is used to culture the bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91523cdd8f510a966e9b301a0adb96b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d80979bb7e58b10bb558705b5d96fa99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eafea2357c59ac6712f4d9ab41ac5d14&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-050a4c71685bf71165985a79f528ed58</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMER DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymer degradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polymers into smaller units."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer degradation is the process by which polymers are broken down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer degradation is the process by which polymers, such as plastics, are broken down into smaller components."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eb14281b4a095b6c531146d40b5110a1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYMATIC DEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzymatic Degradation is the process by which enzymes break down plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic degradation is the process by which enzymes break down plastics into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic degradation is the process by which enzymes break down organic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic degradation is a biological process by which enzymes break down organic substances, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic degradation refers to the process by which enzymes break down complex molecules into simpler ones, in this case, plant biomass and synthetic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic degradation is a type of biodegradation process that involves the use of enzymes to break down polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic degradation is a process by which enzymes break down plastics and other materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic degradation is a process by which enzymes break down synthetic plastics, and it is an important mechanism for the degradation of plastic pollutants."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enzymatic degradation is the process by which enzymes break down organic compounds, such as polystyrene, into simpler substances."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44e006d8af33633a06dac6789334329d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59dab99372af01b60a073d8eac17870f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63813cc5cb4812528045bd8f1ced4313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40407fe311340b08da856202f38b459c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-908b8bfa7e446694958cf9bd0cfbc583&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c31fc195067eeb8acb7f98417bd6744&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bb7b0638c9c59e134df0491b542efdf</data>
