      <data key="d1">"Black Soldier Fly (BSF) is an insect model used to study the impact of plastics on central carbon metabolism, exhibiting unique metabolic pathways when exposed to different plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black Soldier Fly is a type of insect larva used in the study to determine the metabolic effect of exposure to plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black Soldier Fly is a type of microorganism used as a fertilizer and for biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black soldier fly is an insect that can be used to produce frass, which can be used as a fertilizer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black Soldier Fly, or BSF, is another insect species used in the study, also for evaluating the impact of plastic on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Black soldier fly, also known as Hermetia illucens, is a genus of insect that can be reared on organic waste streams."</data>
