    <node id="&quot;PS MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROPLASTICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS microplastics are a type of microplastic that can be ingested by mealworms, leading to a mass loss of 57.5%, 34.4%, and 51.4% for mealworms from Guangzhou, Tai'an, and Shenzhen, respectively."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS microplastics undergo depolymerization and degradation by mealworms, resulting in a change in molecular weight distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS microplastics are small-sized polystyrene particles used in microbial cultures, with defined size and molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS microplastics are a type of microplastic that undergoes biodegradation by T. molitor larvae, resulting in the formation of 1,3-di-tert-butyl-2,5-dimethylbenzene and other compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS microplastics are a type of plastic that is ingested by mealworm larvae, affecting their growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PVC MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROPLASTICS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PVC microplastics are a type of microplastic that can be ingested by mealworms, leading to a mass loss of 48.4%, 34.0%, and 57.0% for mealworms from Guangzhou, Tai'an, and Shenzhen, respectively."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC microplastics are a type of microplastic that undergoes decomposition in two stages, dechlorination and chain scission period."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC microplastics are a type of plastic that is ingested by mealworm larvae, affecting their growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDPE MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"LDPE microplastics are a type of microplastic that can be ingested by mealworms, leading to a mass loss of 36.9%, 22.0%, and 29.7% for mealworms from Guangzhou, Tai'an, and Shenzhen, respectively."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE microplastics undergo pyrolysis in one stage, resulting in a chain scission process with main products being alkenes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241</data>
    </node>
