    <node id="&quot;CHAIN SCISSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chain scission is a chemical reaction that can occur during the degradation of plastics, resulting in the breaking of polymer chains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chain scission is the process by which the molecular weight of PS is reduced, resulting in the formation of smaller molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Chain scission is the second stage of decomposition of PVC microplastics, occurring at a maximum rate at 432 °C."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-99f8bb992751f8875d9449507e9c46ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0caad5c42a4b470a8c41ac3fb68c1f64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e50d86c5a0ab8e4188ede9ae519d241</data>
