    <node id="&quot;MICROPLASTIC POLLUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENVIRONMENTAL ISSUE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microplastic pollution is a significant environmental issue, with plastic wastes causing harm to marine and terrestrial animals, plants, and humans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution is a type of pollution that affects the environment and marine ecosystems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution refers to the contamination of the environment by small plastic particles, which can harm animals and humans."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution refers to the accumulation of microplastics in the environment, which can harm ecosystems and human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution is an ecological issue with adverse impacts on the immune and reproductive systems."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution refers to the contamination of the environment with small plastic particles, which can harm ecosystems and human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution refers to the pollution caused by small plastic particles in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution refers to the presence of small plastic particles in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastic pollution is an environmental issue that affects the survival, development, metabolism, and feeding activity of freshwater invertebrates."</data>
