    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL FLORA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal flora is closely related to the eating habits of yellow mealworms, with significant differences in the main intestinal flora after ingesting different types of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal flora refers to the community of microorganisms that live in the intestines of an organism, such as Tenebrio molitor, and play a crucial role in its health and ability to degrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal flora refers to the microorganisms that can be found in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal flora refers to the microorganisms present in the gut of yellow mealworms, which are capable of degrading plastics and are isolated from the intestinal flora of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal flora refers to the microorganisms present in the intestines of various organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Intestinal flora refers to the microorganisms that live in the intestine of an insect, such as Plesiophthalminus davidis, and can play a role in degrading plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdb235a6eddd0a0e69be356e83362fc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c808bc1867233246c6ad41186de9452&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a8521d10cd6a04d8ba536be9f9dec8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OATS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oats are a food source provided to mealworms to enhance their growth conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats are a type of nutrient that can be used to feed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats are a type of food that can be used to rear mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats are being used as a bedding material in the experiment and are also being consumed by the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats are used as a bedding material in the experiment and can affect the EPS consumption rate of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats are a type of food used to feed mealworms in the control group of the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oats are used as a control diet for the mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3235cc6102d988875f1dda974a56038&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d76ad321e1c68d5f139cdb94d5bf42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c11c77665793ac79aecfb19a89dd1f52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3c4d027474e8769f550ce290c9391ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2fb515eae7af2b662d5d600120e7001&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
