    <node id="&quot;POLYETHYLENE TEREPHTHALATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyethylene Terephthalate (PET) is a commonly used plastic that contributes to the majority of plastic wastes and can be biodegraded by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene Terephthalate, also known as PET, is a type of plastic, making up 6.9% of plastic production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic polymer that is widely used, making up a significant portion of thermoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that can be taken up by industrial snails."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that is being studied for its biodegradation, with certain microorganisms capable of breaking down the material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic polymer that is resistant to biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate (PET) is a type of plastic product that is being studied for its degradation by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that is mentioned as a material that Tenebrio molitor can degrade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that is being studied for its biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of polymer that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic polymer, commonly used in packaging materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene Terephthalate, or PET, is a type of plastic used in the study to evaluate its impact on insect metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that is widely used and can be degraded by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of polymer that is widely used and has a wide range of applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that is commonly used in packaging and other applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene terephthalate is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b0664a95aeeb896dcab096b098c3b54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-566afea8a2a89bd188f68d0afa1bb173&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dafca19c0156f11127587dba3673503&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-411368ddb6a73777c1dd4c683bd389c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cbdeaa1a437ba819412de45788aa119c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa3bd7c611ad935dba56fd3d7300cbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c638e6375f0847be0d1116f4846e5e1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6aab9d327fcd7d10b5d4fbb22c03292a</data>
