    <node id="&quot;ENVIRONMENTAL REMEDIATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Environmental remediation involves the use of microorganisms and other methods to restore environments polluted with plastics like polypropylene (PP)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental remediation is a potential application of the biodegradation of polyethylene by larvae, but it is unlikely due to the high energy requirements and low value of the products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental remediation refers to the process of cleaning up polluted environments, including those harmed by plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"The use of microorganisms to clean up pollutants, including plastics, in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental remediation refers to the process of removing or reducing pollutants, such as PS, from the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental remediation is the process of removing or reducing pollutants from the environment, with biodegradation being a key mechanism for remediation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental remediation is the process of removing pollutants and toxins from the environment to restore it to a healthy state."&lt;SEP&gt;"Environmental remediation is the process of removing pollutants, including plastics, from the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-71372e333b39cee7eea0c53f89bec5c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eca628f2d85c664191a5205194ec475&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a54f7d9e0a43fb94e2fc35f93656fc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-918d0788c95399a6714bd40c688594de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7106a16c81492914e4ba58e248689714</data>
    </node>
