      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-2 is a product used as a feedstock for the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of LDPE feedstock used in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of LDPE film that is colorless and without additives."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of LDPE foam that is consumed and depolymerized by Tenebrio molitor larvae, with a different depolymerization pattern compared to PE-1."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of low-density polyethylene (LDPE) foam with a higher average molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of plastic foam being tested for biodegradation by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is another type of low-density polyethylene (LDPE) polymer being tested for depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of LDPE foam used as a control sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of LDPE polymer that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of LDPE polymer that is being studied for its biodegradation properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of LDPE that is used to test the consumption and biodegradation by T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of plastic that undergoes biodegradation, similar to LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of polymer that can be depolymerized by T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is a type of polymer that is being compared to LDPE in terms of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-2 is another type of LDPE foam."</data>
