    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC TREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotic treatment is a biological process that is used to evaluate the effect of antibiotics on the depolymerization of plastic foams."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic treatment is a process being used to test the effect of gentamicin on the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic treatment is a process that is being used to study the effect of antibiotics on the degradation of feedstocks by larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic treatment is the process of using antibiotics to suppress gut microbes in T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic treatment refers to the use of antibiotics to treat the larvae, which affects the microbial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic treatment is a process that involves the use of antibiotics to suppress gut microbiota."</data>
