    <node id="&quot;MORGANELLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS OF MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A genus of bacteria"&lt;SEP&gt;"Morganella is a genus of bacteria that increased in relative abundance in the gut of yellow mealworms after feeding on masks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Morganella is a genus of bacteria that is found in high relative abundance in the inner-fed group of yellow mealworms and is associated with the diet of the inner layer of the surgical mask."&lt;SEP&gt;"Morganella is a type of bacteria that is found in the gut of insects and has been found to be associated with the breakdown of plastic polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Morganella is a type of bacteria that is present in the gut microbiome of T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."</data>
