      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Depolymerization patterns refer to the different ways in which the larvae break down PP, including broad depolymerization and limited extent depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depolymerization patterns refer to the ways in which plastics are broken down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depolymerization patterns refer to the ways in which polymers are broken down into smaller molecules."</data>
