      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hemicellulose is a biological marker involved in the degradation pathway of lignocellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemicellulose is a type of nutritional component found in the feedstocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemicellulose is a type of polysaccharide that can be degraded by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"hemicellulose is a type of complex carbohydrate that is a key component of plant cell walls, and its degradation is an important process in the metabolism of plants and microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hemicellulose is a type of nutrient that can be degraded by certain microorganisms."</data>
