    <node id="&quot;CITROBACTER FREUNDII&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrobacter freundii is a bacterium known to degrade long-chain polymers, linear hydrocarbons, and cyclic hydrocarbons, and is significantly associated with the gut microbiome in PS- and PE-fed mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter freundii is a type of bacterium that has been identified as contributing to the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrobacter freundii is one of the unique gut microorganisms associated with PS biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KLEBSIELLA AEROGENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Klebsiella aerogenes is a bacterium associated with hydrocarbon degradation and bioremediation, and is one of the most prevalent strains identified in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella aerogenes is a type of bacterium that has been identified as contributing to the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella aerogenes is a bacterium that has been found to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella aerogenes is one of the unique gut microorganisms associated with PS biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c6c5d405260e0a6f512a9504195dc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eda80cb027c8107defa00011d491b002</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT GUT ENVIRONMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The insect gut environment is a unique microenvironment that facilitates the biodegradation of plastics, with the insect host and its gut microbiome collaborating to create an environment conducive to plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENZYME ACTIVITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enzyme activity is a measure of the ability of microorganisms to break down organic materials, including plastics, with certain enzymes playing a key role in the biodegradation process."</data>
