      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The mealworm gut microenvironment is a unique environment that facilitates the biodegradation of plastics, with the insect host and its gut microbiome collaborating to create an environment conducive to plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT HOST&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The insect host is the organism that provides the environment for the gut microbiome to break down plastics, with the host and its gut microbiome collaborating to create an environment conducive to plastic biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07aae06c64778453da4bda48f5347de5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;T. MOLITOR LINNAEUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"T. molitor Linnaeus is the species of mealworm used in the study, known for its ability to degrade PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor Linnaeus is the species to which mealworms belong."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-10004ab6a85cecf4effb74c306df57cf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SUPERNATANT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Supernatant is the liquid portion of the gut microbiome being studied for its effects on PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Supernatant is the liquid portion of the mealworm gut microbiome culture, which contains factors that enhance plastic degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The supernatant is a liquid fraction obtained from the gut microbiome of mealworms, which contains factors that enhance PS degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The supernatant is a liquid fraction of the mealworm gut content that contains the emulsifying agent."&lt;SEP&gt;"The supernatant is a liquid phase collected from the mealworm gut, containing secreted factors from both the mealworm and its gut bacteria, which may play a role in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-902ed6a67c601276c5dbf43c35dd824f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eba752cb179633f5dd054ee7c9ee2cba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL ENRICHMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial enrichments are used to enhance plastic degradation outside the mealworm, indicating a process of cultivating microorganisms for a specific purpose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SALINE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Saline is a nutrient solution used to help grow and maintain microorganisms, such as those found in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline solution is used to harvest the mealworm gut microbiome, providing a medium for the microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline is a solution used to prepare the intestinal cell suspension."&lt;SEP&gt;"Saline is a solution used to clean the insects before dissection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6dce72fccb3df94ec407aba3d4df8eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88659f9848d30be72c37a99b551a9a0a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70bab3579af07d0f99a5f948a90fe1e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
