    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC EXPERIMENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotic experiments are conducted to assess the role of the mealworm in the absence of significant gut microbiome activity, indicating a biological process of investigation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A PS diet is used to feed the mealworms, providing them with plastic as a source of nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS diet is a diet that affects the composition and function of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS diet is a diet that is protein-deficient but leads to an increase in protein levels after consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"The PS diet is positively correlated with the presence of Nitrospirales, Nitrosomonadales, and Planctomycetales."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS diet refers to the diet that includes PS, which is being studied for its ability to be depolymerized by Tenebrio species."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS diet refers to a diet that includes polystyrene, which can have toxic effects on T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-88706f91768bcf0eaa7a49ef2d4b771f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-668212da3bf356132cadb63df6ce09b6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96b716e9400e9e77e099de5cca7c548</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-DEGRADING BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS-degrading bacteria are microorganisms capable of breaking down polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS-degrading bacteria are microorganisms capable of degrading plastic, specifically polystyrene (PS). They were enriched and isolated from the gut microbiome of mealworms fed with PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS-degrading bacteria are microorganisms found in the gut of mealworms that are capable of breaking down plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"PS-degrading bacteria are microorganisms that can degrade polystyrene, including Exiguobacterium and Pseudomonas strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcb17715cb4e5148b33061c1b6cbf1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcc545cfe4d6e8e04c3698a149d4101a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc75b7e672a7f7c036713dfa2675d79a</data>
    </node>
