      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotic-treated mealworms are a group of mealworms that have been treated with antibiotics to suppress the growth of nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic-treated mealworms are mealworms that have been treated with antibiotics to eliminate their gut bacteria, including nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic-treated mealworms are mealworms that have been treated with antibiotics, which affects the composition and function of the gut microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Antibiotic-treated mealworms have decreased acetylene-reducing activities and lower δ15N values compared to Styrofoam-eating mealworms."</data>
