      <data key="d1">"Polyethylene degradation is a biological process by which an organism breaks down polyethylene, leading to changes in its toxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene degradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene degradation refers to the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process by which polyethylene is broken down into smaller components, which may be affected by the activity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The process of breaking down polyethylene by microorganisms, resulting in a decrease in molecular weight and an increase in oxidation level."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene degradation is a biological process by which microorganisms, such as Bacillus sp. YP1, break down polyethylene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene degradation refers to the breakdown of polyethylene into smaller components by microorganisms, and is a potential solution to the problem of plastic waste."</data>
