      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glycerol is a chemical used to store pure cultures of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycerol is a chemical used to store suspensions of isolated and crushed guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycerol is a metabolite that is affected by the different diets, with varying levels of excretion, indicating metabolic stress in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycerol is a type of nutrient source used for Greater Wax Moth (WM) larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycerol is a metabolite that is involved in the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycerol is a component of the 50% glycerol solution, mixed with distilled water in a volume ratio of 1:1."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycerol is a metabolite that is produced from the oxidation of fatty acids and is used as an energy source by insects."</data>
