    <node id="&quot;TRIGLYCERIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIPID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Triglyceride is a form of energy storage in insects, such as mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triglyceride is a type of biomolecule that stores fatty acids, which are oxidized to provide energy during starvation in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triglyceride is a type of lipid that is stored in the bodies of mealworms and is used as a source of energy during starvation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Triglyceride is a type of lipid that serves as an energy reserve for organisms, including mealworms, and is used to survive during starvation and environmental stress."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41635122b30ee45048cc885b38fff6ea</data>
    </node>
