    <node id="&quot;LIPID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lipid is a biochemical compound that is analyzed in the body of mealworms to assess the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid is a component of the mealworms' bodies that is extracted and analyzed in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid is a type of biomolecule that is affected by starvation in mealworms, with a significant decline in total lipid content observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid refers to a type of molecule that is involved in energy storage and other biological processes, which can be affected by biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid is a nutrient analyzed in the study, with its content being highest in control mealworms fed oatmeal."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid is a type of biomolecule that serves as an energy reserve for organisms, with high levels found in the fat body of insects, including mealworms, which helps them survive during starvation and environmental stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lipid is a type of nutrient that is essential for the growth and development of living organisms, including mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56c8b21b1eaba7633b49cea16714ddc1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TREHALOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Trehalose is a metabolite involved in biosynthesis in response to abiotic stresses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trehalose is a type of carbohydrate that is present in the insect body and plays a crucial role in maintaining organ function."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trehalose is a type of metabolite that can be produced in response to abiotic stresses."&lt;SEP&gt;"Trehalose is a nutrient that is utilized by Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its ability to grow on this carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-14f9f0280098bb86719394a4bd53e5bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191</data>
