      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Immune response is a biological process affected by nano- and microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune response refers to the response of an organism to pathogens or other foreign substances, which can be affected by biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The immune response is a defense mechanism in insects, including Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, that helps protect against pathogens and other foreign substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Immune response is a physiological response that is stimulated by certain microorganisms, such as ii infection in Cyprinus carpio."</data>
