    <node id="&quot;INSECT GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect gut is a physical characteristic of insects such as Tenebrio molitor that plays a significant role in the biodegradation of EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The insect gut is the digestive system of an insect, such as Tenebrio molitor, and plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insect gut is the location where plastic degradation activity is observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"The insect gut refers to the digestive system of an insect, which can harbor a community of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insect gut is a physical characteristic of insects where the microbiome and enzymatic activity take place, affecting the degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"The insect gut is a physical characteristic of insects that provides a habitat for microorganisms to live and interact with the insect's environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Insect gut refers to the digestive system of insects, which plays a key role in the degradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-260d8c268067de32e5ac98d66ab70a6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76cb64e0aa4e4039b70799a0df8943d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-001e8f54368c9a236f702fd09cddf4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROORGANISMS IN THE GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microorganisms in the gut of Tenebrio molitor play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics, including PVC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms in the gut of mealworms are responsible for the decomposition of plastics, including biodegradable and non-biodegradable materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc88563632a3abf926bf4e4ac16973fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NMR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NMR (Nuclear Magnetic Resonance) is a technique used to analyze the chemical structure of plastics during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR is a technique used to analyze the molecular structure of the PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR, or Nuclear Magnetic Resonance, is a technology used to analyze the chemical composition of the fecula."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR, or nuclear magnetic resonance, is a technique used to analyze the structure of molecules, including those involved in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR (Nuclear Magnetic Resonance) is a technology used to analyze the composition of frass and study the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR is a type of spectroscopy used for analyzing the molecular structure of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR is a technology being used to analyze the biodegradation of PE and WC by the lesser waxworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"NMR (Nuclear Magnetic Resonance) is a technique used to analyze the molecular structure of plastics and other materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dad389953d78e790a40a9267c5b591c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f2303f3680e9313daac77bb7e27e7da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c426315f0f412528b9c6fb2a82dff2c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3d6c72a17160a2bc126220798c799a6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6bd3778dedc6a0463017df9f8d6396eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33a0a8b02ff930ea552c8902e4d0defd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b7c2ef16f6809388c0c1a87c26bd5c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-395b01f15fd97b70e2368941120e9a37</data>
