      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight of PE mulching film is a measure of the size of the polymer chains, which can be affected by bacterial degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-af682f78e3e8970d7d70b027a8f79116</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAIN NYZ450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strain NyZ450 is a type of microorganism that is capable of degrading PE mulching films, but its effectiveness is increased when used in a consortium with Strain NyZ451."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRAIN NYZ451&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Strain NyZ451 is a type of microorganism that is capable of degrading PE mulching films, and its combination with Strain NyZ450 leads to a more significant decrease in the molecular weight of PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSORTIUM OF STRAIN NYZ450 AND STRAIN NYZ451&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The consortium of Strain NyZ450 and Strain NyZ451 is a combination of two microorganisms that work together to degrade PE mulching films more effectively than either strain alone."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
