      <data key="d1">"-C=C- bonds are a type of chemical bond that indicates surface oxidation of plastic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRACKS ON THE PE SURFACE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cracks on the PE surface are a physical property that indicates the degradation of plastic materials."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACE OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surface oxidation is a chemical property that indicates the degradation of plastic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surface oxidation is a chemical reaction that occurs on the surface of microplastics under UV radiation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40357516e3f9dd4b2969b73efe444c28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaffdadca6e8a3e9721b2dcb031b93f7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NYZ450&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NyZ450 is a bacterial strain that plays a major role in the degradation of PE mulching films, utilizing PE as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NYZ451&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NyZ451 is a bacterial strain that plays an auxiliary role in the degradation of PE mulching films, with a limited ability to break chemical bonds of PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-C BOND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-C bond is a chemical bond involved in the degradation of PS and lignin."&lt;SEP&gt;"The C-C bond is a type of chemical bond that is difficult to break, making PE resistant to biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROLYTIC FUNCTIONAL GROUPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNCTIONAL GROUP"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrolytic functional groups are necessary for the biodegradation of PE, but are lacking in PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEROXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Peroxidation is a pretreatment method that can make PE more bioavailable and easier to degrade."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
