      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lysinibacillus sphaericus is a type of bacteria that has been studied for its ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPERGILLUS NIGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SPECIES"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspergillus niger is a fungus capable of biodegrading thermally treated low-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus niger is a species of fungus that has been shown to colonize polystyrene film surface."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus niger is a type of fungus that has been studied for its ability to biodegrade low-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus niger is a type of fungus that has been found to be capable of degrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus niger is a microorganism that can colonize and degrade thermally oxidized high-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillus niger is a species of fungus that is capable of biodegrading thermally treated low-density polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3bd104d06a1ede06701ecfa96bccc2c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3cec3addc1bee202783dff1583ba54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f99668e767a56e2e64ece791653b952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRETREATMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pretreatment refers to the process of treating a material, in this case, PE, to make it more bioavailable and easier to degrade."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pretreatment refers to the process of treating microplastics and nanoplastics before they are released into the environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROXYLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydroxylation is a chemical reaction that involves the addition of a hydroxyl group to a molecule, in this case, the PE molecule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hydroxylation is a chemical reaction that involves the addition of a hydroxyl group to a molecule, involved in the biodegradation of PP polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carboxylation is a chemical reaction that involves the addition of a carboxyl group to a molecule, in this case, the PE molecule."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylation is a chemical reaction that involves the addition of a carboxyl group to a molecule, involved in the biodegradation of PP polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-78830eb6f2457838fda4728b21c17bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
