      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Greater Wax Moth is a type of microorganism that has a lower degradation efficiency of PS compared to Superworm and Yellow Mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth is a species of insect whose larvae are being studied for their ability to biodegrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"The greater wax moth is a genus of moth whose larvae are used to digest plastic waste, with their behavior and physiology being studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"The greater wax moth is a species of moth whose larvae are capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth is a type of larvae that can feed on PS and has a high survival rate, with a moderate decrease in mass weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Greater wax moth is one of the three species of larvae being studied, and its gut microbiome is being analyzed."</data>
