    <node id="&quot;MASS BALANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mass balance is a biochemical measure that is used to analyze the degradation of polyethylene (PE) by lesser waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance is a biological concept used to assess the fate of plastics, such as PE and PS, after degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance is the concept used to measure the degradation of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance refers to the accounting of the amount of material before and after a process, being used to study the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mass balance is a biological concept used to monitor the removal of the ingested plastics by mealworms."</data>
