    <node id="&quot;BIODIESEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodiesel is a product produced from the lipid content of mealworms, with its production costs and environmental impact being evaluated."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is a product that can be converted from lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is a product that can be produced from the lipids of larvae, such as those of the greater wax moth and mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is a type of biofuel that can be produced from vegetable oil and has a lower heating value."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is a product that can be produced from the fat of mealworms, making them a valuable resource for environmental use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodiesel is a type of fuel that can be produced from the grease of certain insects, such as the yellow mealworm."</data>
