    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSTRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microstructure refers to the internal structure of the LDPE substrate at a microscopic level."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microstructure of the LDPE substrate is affected by the degradation action of the Greater Wax Moth Larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOMOGENATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The homogenate is a paste made from the Greater Wax Moth Larvae, used to test its ability to degrade LDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONSUMPTION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Consumption Rate is a measure of the rate at which mealworms and beetles consume EPS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumption rate is a biological measure used to quantify the amount of EPS consumed by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumption rate refers to the amount of LDPE substrate consumed by the Greater Wax Moth Larvae or mealworms per day."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumption rate is a biological measure being studied in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The consumption rate is a biochemical measure of the amount of plastic consumed by mealworms per day."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumption rate refers to the rate at which the mealworms consume the polystyrene, which can influence the efficiency of the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Consumption rate is a measure of the amount of material, in this case PP, that is consumed by microorganisms over a given period of time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7b33a3915745323f1bd29bd2febf60b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53f87a406d4812c07e783e6cbfc09606&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd3092744be0c66dad5833977dedd913&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6b858a4eb57553f5b1ae041e1c7160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09d03c0a2dce3f57876d209a83a2e82a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Holes refer to the openings created in the LDPE substrate by the Greater Wax Moth Larvae or mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Openings or gaps that are formed in a material, such as polyethylene, as a result of degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHEWING PATTERNS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Chewing patterns refer to the visible marks left on the LDPE substrate by the Greater Wax Moth Larvae or mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICROSCOPIC INSPECTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microscopic inspection refers to the examination of the LDPE substrate using a microscope to observe the effects of degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KEYENCE VHX-6000&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"KEYENCE VHX-6000 is a type of microscope used for microscopic inspection."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EDGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Edges refer to the boundaries of the holes created in the LDPE substrate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORPHOLOGY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Morphology refers to the shape and structure of plastics, including PS and PU foam, which changes over time due to consumption by superworms and yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Morphology refers to the shape and structure of the LDPE substrate after degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXCRETED MATERIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MARKER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Excreted material refers to the substance produced by the Greater Wax Moth Larvae that affects the microstructure of the LDPE substrate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEGRADATION ACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
