      <data key="d1">"Weber et al. (2017) refers to a research study on the degradation of LDPE by microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUPA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pupa is a life stage of T. molitor that is formed after the larval stage, and its formation is influenced by the amount of reserves accumulated by the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupa is a life stage of Tenebrio molitor, mentioned in the taxonomic classification."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupa is a life stage of an insect, such as Tenebrio molitor, during which it undergoes transformation into an adult."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupa is a stage of development of an insect."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupa refers to the stage of development of the mealworms after they have stopped eating and are transforming into adult beetles."&lt;SEP&gt;"The pupal stage is a stage in the life cycle of an insect, such as the mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupa is a life stage of superworms and yellow mealworms, characterized by transformation into adult form."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pupa is a life stage of insects, including the lesser waxworm, that is part of the life cycle."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed48dc66abf9c27721101b1adac15e7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-503c588468d284ba03a34235957f9b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5710c6b3eb755779f706360ec72260e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab6b219720db5a6e3384c884c280984c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c16dd402d0a926c1a975280e2b32e84e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Infrared spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the chemical composition of the LDPE substrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Infrared spectroscopy is a technique used to analyze the chemical structure of materials, including HDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-361c5d4ba2e879627f4eb7fc4011ee3b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MECHANICAL WEAR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mechanical wear refers to the physical degradation of a material, such as polyethylene, due to mechanical forces."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOCHEMICAL OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biochemical oxidation refers to the chemical reaction that occurs when a material, such as polyethylene, is broken down by microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLIC GROUPS&quot;">
