      <data key="d1">"Carboxylic groups are a type of functional group that is thought to contribute to the biochemical oxidation of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOMOLECULES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biomolecules refer to the molecules that are produced by living organisms, such as lipids and free fatty acids, and may play a role in the degradation of polyethylene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical compound that is a component of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene is a component of poly (ethylene terephthalate), which is broken down by the bacterium during degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene is a chemical produced by nitrogen-fixing bacteria as a result of acetylene reduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene is a product of the acetylene-reducing activity of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d7f6907ee7ce47b00537b1458fcc029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLYCOL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A chemical compound that is not detected in the samples of polyethylene that have been degraded by the larvae of the greater wax moth and the mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycol is a potential product of the biodegradation of polyethylene by larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8624d79db8ed1c4488f890a1d0c085a5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681ece0a8beca8b22f3c6aa11a564f63</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOXYLIC ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A type of functional group that is thought to contribute to the biochemical oxidation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acids are a type of chemical property formed during the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acids are a type of functional group that forms during the biodegradation of PE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carboxylic acids are organic compounds released by PVC that may cause mealworms to lose mass."</data>
