    <node id="&quot;YELLOW MEALWORM LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The larvae of Tenebrio molitor, also known as yellow mealworm larvae, have been found to biodegrade plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yellow mealworm larvae are the juvenile stage of yellow mealworms, rich in protein and holding many economic benefits for practical production."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yellow mealworm larvae have been found to have the ability to biodegrade polyethylene plastics, including LDPE and HDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Yellow mealworm larvae are the stage of yellow mealworms being used to study biodegradation, with different survival rates and frass production observed across experimental groups."</data>
