    <node id="&quot;RHODOCOCCUS SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Rhodococcus sp. is a bacterium that has been investigated for its role in degrading polystyrene, highlighting its potential in environmental cleanup efforts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a type of bacteria associated with the gut microbiota of Tenebrio molitor larvae fed with both polystyrene and corn straw."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a type of microorganism that is capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a type of bacteria that is capable of degrading polypropylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a type of bacteria that can biodegrade polypropylene microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Rhodococcus sp. is a type of bacteria that has been reported to be involved in the degradation of styrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a53fba6106c000acc0dac3484d37a4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cefffe48b3d2ec347f880c77300fc041&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
