    <node id="&quot;LARVAL GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larval gut is a biological concept referring to the gut of the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval gut is the part of the mealworm's body where the biodegradation of polystyrene takes place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval gut is the part of the mealworm's digestive system where the degradation of polystyrene (PS) takes place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval gut of the yellow mealworm is the site where biodegradation of surgical masks occurs, with changes in the gut-bacterial community observed in response to different mask diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval gut of yellow mealworms is where the degradation of surgical masks takes place, with changes in gut bacterial and fungal diversities observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval gut refers to the digestive system of the larvae, where biodegradation of PP takes place."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval gut is the part of the T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae where biodegradation of LDPE takes place."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval gut is the digestive system of the mealworm where biodegradation of plastics occurs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06a44b308af148551c5b7feef324d88b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0ec64a7c629b14bfb6652f1960a337c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b2d6bcd4d2cc81a978694e417e76747e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7fa795762aa89809d8221dc9dda92fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1</data>
