      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TERMITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Termites are a genus of xylophagous insects that have been found to have nitrogen-fixing abilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termites are a species of insect that have a symbiotic relationship with microorganisms that degrade lignocellulose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termites are a type of insect that can degrade lignocellulose and other natural polymers, and have a complex gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termites are insects that are capable of breaking down lignin, and have a symbiotic relationship with their gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termites are insects that have a diet based on lignocellulose and have microorganisms that convert nitrogen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Termites have a symbiotic relationship with bacteria that helps in the decomposition of cellulose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0d13e8c770c847882a94a6b78b0979cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RUMINATING MAMMALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ruminating mammals are animals that have a symbiotic relationship with their gut microbiota, and are capable of breaking down cellulose."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d</data>
    </node>
