    <node id="&quot;METABOLITES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolites are molecules that are produced or consumed during the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolites are the compounds produced during the degradation of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolites are the products of metabolic processes, including those involved in the degradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolites are the end products of cellular processes, and 2489 of them were identified in the gut of larvae fed with different feedstocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolites were detected and annotated using LC-MS/MS and KEGG database."&lt;SEP&gt;"metabolites are small molecules produced by cellular metabolism, used for analyzing metabolic pathways and functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolites are substances produced by mealworms' metabolism, and their synthesis requires nitrogen, which is fixed by gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolites are substances that are produced during the metabolism of nutrients, such as proteins and nucleic acids, in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e69c793c3b67aed7a68bf864c2c7a309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-813b71242f366f10218c10631cd7dee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64b3e57543d6b365fff3ef2b14ddb309&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c810740a381d4d9e829e28c01e62564</data>
