    <node id="&quot;OLEIC ACID&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oleic acid is a fatty acid found in the frass or intestinal samples of PS-fed larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is a fatty acid that increased in content in the frass of PS-fed mealworms, probably due to lipid metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is a type of compound found in the diet and frass of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is a type of fatty acid found in the insects, accounting for about 50% of the fatty acid content in the PE and CEL groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is a type of fatty acid that is present in Tenebrio molitor and is negatively correlated with the lignocellulose diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is a type of fatty acid that is found in the biomass of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oleic acid is a type of fatty acid found in the larvae, with its content being measured and compared across different feeds."&lt;SEP&gt;"oleic acid is a fatty acid detected in the frass of insect larvae fed on PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1ead6f17ad517015b638608c5bfe6852&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f65bf081bdd3c6718fa0310993bfc0d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a52fc2936b4d2a771dbc2d6a37eeb710&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e155a60beeedb5736450fdc1ffa4699e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a170da66288c73388872b8a43fa51e33</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOSACCHARIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monosaccharide is a type of sugar that includes mannose, which is important for protein glycosylation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d</data>
    </node>
