    <node id="&quot;PCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCA is a statistical technique used to analyze the metabolites in the frass of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCA, or principal component analysis, is a technique used to analyze the gut microbial composition of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCA, or principal component analysis, is a biological concept used to investigate the impact of mask diets on the gut bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"PCA, or Principal Component Analysis, is a method used to visualize and analyze the gut bacterial communities of yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d616d4c3c3199d53c1ae93ebcf3589d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542</data>
