    <node id="&quot;HELEN GIKA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Helen Gika is a researcher who has provided support for the study of biodegradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT FAT BODY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect fat body is a physical characteristic of insects where fat is accumulated and stored."&lt;SEP&gt;"The insect fat body is a storage site for energy reserves, such as lipids."&lt;SEP&gt;"The insect fat body is a tissue that plays a crucial role in the metabolism and energy storage of insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLOMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolomics is a biological process used to study the impact of plastics on insect models and their central carbon metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolomics is a scientific journal that has published research on the biodegradation of plastics by insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolomics is the study of the metabolic processes that occur within living organisms, including the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolomics is the analysis of central carbon metabolism (CCM) metabolites, providing important information on how metabolic processes are being activated, and the deviation from normal processes during health, disease, and environmental perturbation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GC/MS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"GC/MS (Gas Chromatography/Mass Spectrometry) is a technique used to analyze the metabolic processes that occur within living organisms, including the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"GC/MS is a biochemical technique used to analyze the chemical composition of polystyrene (PS) samples before and after degradation by strain YT2."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8e38968f22c4cd9bef3f1562e4ca47e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FIEHN GC/MS METABOLOMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fiehn GC/MS Metabolomics is a specific type of GC/MS technique used to study metabolomics, including the biodegradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTH CATERPILLARS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wax moth caterpillars, also known as Galleria mellonella, can biodegrade polyethylene and have a unique hologenome."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b47eb2d42413e11dbd4e9bb9f2df12f</data>
    </node>
