    <node id="&quot;POLYSTYRENE-DEGRADING BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polystyrene-degrading bacteria are a type of bacteria that can break down polystyrene, and are found in the guts of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene-degrading bacteria are the microorganisms of interest in this study, capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polystyrene-degrading bacteria are the microorganisms that are responsible for the biodegradation of polystyrene."</data>
