    <node id="&quot;BEETLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beetles are a type of insect that can degrade lignocellulose and other natural polymers, and have a complex gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are the adult stage of Tenebrio molitor, which can degrade polystyrene with the help of their gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are a type of microorganism that consumes the hard, protective outer layer of the EPS cup, with an average consumption rate of 0.00 ± 0.01 mg/d."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are mentioned as being less effective at EPS biodegradation compared to mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are the adult stage of Tenebrio molitor and are capable of consuming EPS, but at a slower rate than mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are the adult stage of the T. molitor species and are being used in the experiment to study their consumption of EPS cups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are an order of insects that include the genus Tenebrio obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Beetles are an order of insects that include the species Tenebrio molitor."</data>
