    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER HORMAECHEI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A bacterium isolated from Tenebrio molitor, capable of biodegrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a bacterium that has been previously isolated from T. molitor and is involved in the biodegradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a bacterium that is related to Klebsiella oxytoca."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a bacterium that has been studied in the context of microbiome research, particularly in relation to its ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a species of bacteria that is capable of biodegrading polystyrene microplastics under anaerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a bacterium that can perform heterotrophic denitrification in the presence of methanol and sodium-succinate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a bacterium that is an opportunistic pathogen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a facultative anaerobic bacterial strain that can oxidize and depolymerize polystyrene under anaerobic conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a species of bacteria that is associated with the biodegradation of polystyrene and polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Enterobacter hormaechei is a species within the Enterobacter genus, with a sequence identity of ≥ 97.8% to the isolated strains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-652bf0615ec39fba0cedd113ec87a78a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-82390f5824b5ef543e1f258b1a47e167&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e81a4fde1bdef8287df342fc27193de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939f85d52d9301668deab282264e5fd9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3a889b716cac361e6e04405777075076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7cbc8be34e0de8aebc6fd547bacc627&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4af956dbe737dee68ab6b9834fe2fcc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3934e2c5488a209e54e10ba4c0335a6</data>
