    <node id="&quot;CITRATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrate is a nutrient that is used to differentiate Strain BIT-26T from other species of the genus Mixta, based on its inability to utilize citrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrate is a test used to biochemically characterize the bacterial isolates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrate is a type of metabolite that can be produced by certain bacteria, including some species of Stenotrophomonas."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UREASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Urease is a test used to biochemically characterize the bacterial isolates."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme involved in the nitrogen conversion process in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme that catalyzes the hydrolysis of urea into carbon dioxide and ammonia."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme that is involved in the breakdown of urea and is produced by the microbiota in the PE-oxo variant."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme that breaks down urea, with different bacteria having varying levels of urease activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Urease is an enzyme that is negative in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its inability to catalyze the hydrolysis of urea."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-84297b844ec01d2f58756b669806fd62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee46611b24ea3848df979ded841f06b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-39c4ff9e5812f88117b37503a70b0479&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a38885f67ed46b97bb84086f575fd43</data>
    </node>
