    <node id="&quot;LACTOSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lactose is a carbohydrate that is used to differentiate Strain BIT-26T from other species of the genus Mixta, based on its ability to produce acids from lactose."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactose is a nutrient that can be utilized by bacteria, with different species having varying levels of lactose utilization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactose is a nutrient that is utilized by Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its ability to grow on this carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lactose is a type of sugar that can be fermented by certain bacteria, including some species of Bacillus and Pantoea."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2665d67f816d2da20a065d708c370210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
