      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACILLUS MONOCULTURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus monocultures refer to the cultivation of a single species of Bacillus, which has been studied for its ability to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CITRIC ACID CYCLE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The citric acid cycle is a metabolic pathway involved in the degradation of polystyrene, where styrene is oxidized to phenylacetate."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOFILM GENERATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biofilm generation is the process by which microorganisms form complex communities on surfaces, contributing to the degradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIAL DETERIORATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Material deterioration refers to the breakdown of materials, such as polystyrene, due to the activity of microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC PATHWAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic pathways are biological concepts that describe the series of chemical reactions involved in the metabolism of an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolic pathways are the series of chemical reactions that occur within an organism, such as Tenebrio molitor larvae, to break down or synthesize molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolic pathways refer to the series of chemical reactions that occur within an organism to maintain life, and can be involved in the degradation of various substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolic pathways refer to the series of chemical reactions that occur within mealworms to break down lignocellulose and PS plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolic pathways refer to the series of chemical reactions that occur within microorganisms, allowing them to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolic pathways were analyzed using LC-MS/MS and KEGG database."&lt;SEP&gt;"Metabolic pathways are biological processes that can be affected by the ingestion of PS polymers with different molecular weights."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e8cdca8afb1d7153fba5e3c11b1f669&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b19ac5bdc755bb8e9deb8e317ce365dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5f4bda412174e8b173f180d9b4311ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53d382cbd1392dbcf9530428c2eb8584</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYRENE OXIDATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrene oxidation is the process by which microorganisms convert styrene into phenylacetate, a key step in the degradation of polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHENYLACETATE PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Phenylacetate production is the process by which microorganisms produce phenylacetate as a result of degrading polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c4804d2c00d1d5fff2b89eaf6da26da</data>
    </node>
