    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOMONAS SP. STRAIN Y2&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonas sp. Strain Y2 is a bacterium that has a styrene catabolic cluster, allowing it to degrade styrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonas sp. strain Y2 is a microorganism capable of degrading styrene, with a styrene catabolic cluster."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c02a8ea5e75c58dcb9cfbbcd64f37d82&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PBAT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PBAT is a type of biodegradable plastic that is being studied for its properties and potential applications."&lt;SEP&gt;"PBAT is a type of biodegradable polymer that is being mentioned as a potential future study subject."&lt;SEP&gt;"PBAT, or poly(butylene adipate-co-terephthalate), is a type of biodegradable plastic that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PBAT is a type of biodegradable plastic that may be studied in future research on plastic biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"PBAT is a type of degradable plastic mentioned as a potential area of future research."&lt;SEP&gt;"PBAT, or polybutylene adipate-co-terephthalate, is a type of biodegradable plastic that can be degraded by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-104d99248e84b2776ff5ca17c285a7bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f44f9d05edb3efaf7fdb8f0f1517549&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22ae90a77be18cbac99e5441d47ce2d7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COCKROACH GUT BACTERIA&quot;">
