    <node id="&quot;NIFH GENE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The nifH gene encodes dinitrogen reductase and is genetically conserved, making it a useful marker for detecting nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is a gene that encodes for an enzyme involved in nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is a gene that is involved in nitrogen fixation and is found in nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is a genetic marker used to identify and study nitrogen-fixing microorganisms, which are crucial for the nitrogen cycle."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is a genetic marker used to identify nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is a key gene involved in nitrogen fixation, and its presence is used to identify nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nifH gene is negatively correlated with the lignocellulose diet and the content of MUFA in Tenebrio molitor."</data>
