      <data key="d1">"Lysine decarboxylase is a type of enzyme that is present in Tenebrio molitor and is negatively correlated with the lignocellulose diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lysine decarboxylase is an enzyme involved in the amino acid synthesis process in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lysine decarboxylase is an enzyme that breaks down lysine, with different bacteria having varying levels of lysine decarboxylase activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lysine decarboxylase is an enzyme that is negative in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its inability to catalyze the decarboxylation of lysine."</data>
