    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT (MW)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight (MW) is a physical property of PET that affects its biodegradation, with different MWs being tested for their effect on biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight (MW) is a physical property of plastics that affects their biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The molecular weight of polypropylene (PP) affects its biodegradation patterns and the degradation process, with different molecular weights requiring different predominant bacteria for degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight (MW) is a physical property of polymers that affects their biodegradability, with lower MW polymers being more easily biodegradable than higher MW polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight (MW) is a physical property of polymers that affects their biodegradation, with different MW polymers being tested."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight is a physical property that affects the biodegradation of polystyrene, with different molecular weights influencing the gut microbiome of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The molecular weight (MW) of polystyrene (PS) is being studied to understand its degradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31b2c5f608adabba1cc6986356e96598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e136b8a35c0d60811b9daf0cbd5729f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7a93f0b3dbebad30b6aeabec429a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e24cc3865ed97850c3f25795ff514e8d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5</data>
    </node>
