    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LACHNATALEA SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Lachnatalea sp. is a genus of bacteria that is found to be highly abundant in the gut microbial community of larvae fed with PET, and is potentially involved in PET degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lachnatalea sp. is a genus of bacteria that shows potential for degrading natural organic polymers and is associated with PP degradation in T. molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRONOBACTER SP.&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cronobacter sp. is a genus of bacteria associated with plastic degradation and nitrogen fixation in T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter sp. is a genus of bacteria that is found in the gut microbial community of larvae fed with PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter sp. is another majority member of the gut microbiome in mealworms, known to be associated with insect guts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cronobacter sp. is a species of bacteria that appeared to be overrepresented in PS samples compared to CT samples, with a Log2-fold change of 5.8."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9c310f4f7adc3c5b8340e973a5af45e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c5b5ab19cbfa62cb38c185cba114ed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MIXTA SP.&quot;">
