      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacillus spp. NyZ451 is a bacterium that cooperates with Acinetobacter NyZ450 for the biodegradation of a PE mulching film."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CUTINASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cutinase is an enzyme produced by Humicola insolens that acts synergistically with lipase from Candida antarctica for PET hydrolysis."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cutinase is an enzyme that can degrade cutin, a component of plant cuticles, with potential applications in biotechnology and agricultural sciences."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cutinase is an enzyme that is involved in the degradation of PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cutinase is an enzyme that degrades PET, with limited research on its use for high-crystallinity PET."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfa5755e6c9a5eeae3f595d901dff422&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81610bdb5fdb95d9a333b42668532b9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATP-BINDING CASSETTE (ABC) TRANSPORTER PATHWAYS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ATP-binding cassette (ABC) transporter pathways are involved in the transport of intermediate products during the degradation of PP."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;QUORUM SENSING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Quorum sensing is a biological process that allows microorganisms to communicate and coordinate their behavior."&lt;SEP&gt;"Quorum sensing is a process by which bacteria communicate with each other to coordinate their behavior."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb2c1ef38dbbafa838f87d5f4d6fd6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FLAGELLAR ASSEMBLY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Flagellar assembly is a biological process that allows microorganisms to assemble their flagella and move towards or away from certain chemicals."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWO-COMPONENT SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Two-component system is a biological concept that refers to a system of genes and their regulation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Two-component system is a biological process that allows microorganisms to respond to certain environmental stimuli."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HOST-MICROBE INTERACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Host-microbe interaction is the interaction between a host organism and its associated microorganisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0817d79fa27f2f5b078e09086250c6e0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PP POLYMERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PP polymers are a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by T. molitor larvae, with different molecular weights affecting the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MONOXYGENASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Monoxygenase is an enzyme that is involved in the degradation of PS but is not upregulated in LG3 when using Mi-PS as a carbon source."&lt;SEP&gt;"Monoxygenase is an enzyme that plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of PP polymers, attacking and oxidizing the polymer to form oxygen-containing functional groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f91980be083a0bf5b52d43a640e9d787&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOEMULSIFYING FACTORS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bioemulsifying factors are biological molecules that are involved in the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bioemulsifying factors are substances that help to accelerate the biodegradation of PP polymers by emulsifying the plastic particles and making them more accessible to enzymes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-41b8c7f0b790b0289a7683fde0eca126&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MRPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MRPs are transporters involved in the efflux of plastics within cells, helping to reduce the metabolic pressure exerted on the plastics and allowing the larvae to survive and reproduce."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
