      <data key="d1">"Gene-GEV33-002024 is a gene that encodes for a peroxidase enzyme involved in the biodegradation of PP polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GENE-GEV33-013532&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gene-GEV33-013532 is a gene that encodes for a peroxidase enzyme involved in the biodegradation of PP polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSMEMBRANE PROTEINS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transmembrane proteins are proteins that transport molecules across cell membranes, involved in the biodegradation of PP polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-181e2c8b4d78916fefcf87c119f11d02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRITIONAL STRESS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutritional stress can alter the mitochondrial Mg²⁺ concentration, ultimately affecting cellular energy metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nutritional stress is a physiological response of the larvae to the presence of polypropylene (PP) as a carbon source, requiring adaptation for utilization."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INNATE DIGESTIVE ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Innate digestive enzymes are produced by the larvae and play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEFENSIVE FUNCTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Defensive functions are biological processes that help protect the larvae from harm, including the degradation of polypropylene (PP)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIGNAL TRANSDUCTION FUNCTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Signal transduction functions are biological processes that facilitate communication within the larvae and gut bacteria, influencing the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBOHYDRATE TRANSPORT AND METABOLISM-RELATED FUNCTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbohydrate transport and metabolism-related functions are biological processes that are involved in the utilization of carbon sources, including polypropylene (PP), by the larvae and gut bacteria."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOREACTOR&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bioreactor is a biological system, in this case, the larvae's gut, that facilitates the biodegradation of polypropylene (PP) through the activation of innate digestive enzymes and other functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larval gut can be considered a bioreactor where biodegradation of LDPE takes place."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN VIVO BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In vivo biodegradation is the process of biodegradation that occurs within a living organism, such as the larvae, and is more efficient than in vitro biodegradation for polypropylene (PP)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;IN VITRO BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"In vitro biodegradation is the process of biodegradation that occurs outside of a living organism, such as in a laboratory setting, and is less efficient than in vivo biodegradation for polypropylene (PP)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC-EATING INSECTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic-eating insects refer to insects that are capable of biodegrading plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Plastic-eating insects, such as T. molitor, are capable of degrading polypropylene (PP) and other plastics, and are being studied for their role in plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSIOLOGICAL CHARACTERISTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physiological characteristics of plastic-eating insects, such as T. molitor, are being studied to understand their role in plastic degradation and to develop new methods for plastic waste management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TARGETED MICROBES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Targeted microbes are specific microorganisms that are being studied for their ability to degrade polypropylene (PP) and other plastics, and may be used to develop new methods for plastic waste management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TARGETED ENZYMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Targeted enzymes are specific enzymes that are being studied for their ability to degrade polypropylene (PP) and other plastics, and may be used to develop new methods for plastic waste management."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b759b81206d0e33e320f2d61e540ae47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATP-BINDING CASSETTE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ATP-binding cassette (ABC) is a concept related to the process of binding ATP, which is crucial for various biological processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KYOTO ENCYCLOPAEDIA OF GENES AND GENOMES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kyoto encyclopaedia of genes and genomes (KEGG) is a biological concept that is being used to study the genetic basis of plastic degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69</data>
    </node>
