    <node id="&quot;WAX MOTHS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Wax moths are a type of insect that is capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moths are another type of insect whose larvae have been reported to degrade polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moths, specifically the larvae of Galleria mellonella, are capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Wax moths, also known as Galleria mellonella, are insects that can biodegrade polystyrene."</data>
