    <node id="&quot;HOST GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Host genes for PET depolymerization and metabolism are upregulated in mealworms, contributing to the biodegradation of PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Host genes refer to the genes of insects, such as Tenebrio molitor, that are involved in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Host genes refer to the genes of the mealworms that are involved in the biodegradation of PET."</data>
