    <node id="&quot;DIAZOTROPHIC COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A diazotrophic community is a group of microorganisms that are capable of fixing nitrogen, including those found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophic community refers to a community of microorganisms that can fix nitrogen, such as those found in Tenebrio molitor L."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophic community refers to a group of microorganisms that are capable of fixing nitrogen, such as those found in Tenebrio molitor L."&lt;SEP&gt;"The diazotrophic community refers to the group of microorganisms that are capable of nitrogen fixation and are present in the gut of insects, such as Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"The diazotrophic community is a group of microorganisms that are involved in nitrogen fixation and are present in the gut of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Diazotrophic community refers to a group of microorganisms that are capable of nitrogen fixation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The diazotrophic community refers to the group of microorganisms that are capable of fixing nitrogen, including those found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."</data>
