    <node id="&quot;LARVAL DEVELOPMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larval development is a stage of life that is affected by the biodegradation of PE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval development is the process by which Tenebrio molitor larvae mature and develop into adult beetles, influenced by factors such as nutrition and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval development is the stage of T. molitor that is responsible for biodegrading PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval development refers to the process of growth and development of the yellow mealworms from larvae to adults."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval development is the process by which T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae grow and develop."&lt;SEP&gt;"Larval development refers to the stages of growth and development of T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4265fd894f71345b4ef09c26e6adbda5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69679184959639a1ff81c7392cd5cef5</data>
    </node>
