    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRUDE FAT CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crude fat content is a measure of the amount of crude fat in Tenebrio molitor larvae, influenced by factors such as nutrition and biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE PROCESSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digestive processes refer to the biological mechanisms by which the larvae break down and utilize nutrients from their food sources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROLYSIS REACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrolysis reactions are a type of chemical reaction involved in the breakdown of polymers by the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENT CONTENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRITIONAL COMPONENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrient content refers to the amount and type of nutrients present in the larvae, including total sugar, fat, and crude protein."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GROWTH INHIBITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Growth inhibition is a physiological response of T. molitor larvae to microplastic ingestion, with reduced growth rates observed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Growth inhibition is a physiological response used to assess the impact of plastic ingestion on the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdc8398efba587929eebd0a0842f6e69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMER DEGRADABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymer degradability is a chemical property of plastics that affects the biodegradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymer degradability refers to the ability of polymers to be broken down by biological processes, such as those carried out by the T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MACROINVERTEBRATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Macroinvertebrate refers to a type of organism, such as the T. molitor larvae, that is visible to the naked eye and plays a crucial role in ecosystem functioning."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICOCHEMICAL PROPERTIES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physicochemical properties of polystyrene, such as molecular weight, affect its biodegradation in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Physicochemical properties refer to the physical and chemical characteristics of materials, such as molecular weight, hydrolyzability, and crystallinity, that can affect their behavior and interactions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a00d67f63d22d1959c8a565b6a86d22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYDROLYZABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hydrolyzability is a chemical property that refers to the ability of a material to undergo hydrolysis, a chemical reaction that involves the breakdown of a molecule using water."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymerization is a chemical reaction that involves the formation of a polymer from smaller molecules, such as monomers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerization is the process by which the plastics are formed, and it affects their degradation by the yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY RESERVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy reserves are a measure of the energy stored by T. molitor larvae, and are being studied to understand their growth and survival patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy reserves refer to the stored energy that an organism, such as the T. molitor larvae, uses to maintain its basic functions and activities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy reserves, such as lipids and carbohydrates, are crucial for the survival of insects, like T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESIDUAL PARTICLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Residual particles refer to the remaining fragments of a material, such as plastic, after it has undergone biodegradation or other forms of breakdown."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WASTE PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Waste production refers to the amount of waste generated by an organism, such as the T. molitor larvae, as a result of its metabolic activities."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE FOAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE foams are a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by Z. atratus superworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NEUROTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Neurotoxicity is a physiological response that can occur in organisms as a result of exposure to microplastics and nanoparticles."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cf697c73d05470fb4a143aa0e4700787</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOTOXICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biotoxicity is a physiological response that can occur in organisms as a result of exposure to microplastics and nanoparticles."</data>
