    <node id="&quot;ECOSYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d2">chunk-896c5c0e4d1805ded38b335876a02f78&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20bc31ca22e33a7b244779745e9eeb73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b50c5a85182344022614ffe10dc9382&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5d7f6907ee7ce47b00537b1458fcc029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ee541583aebc7a78ac49285860e4da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ecosystem is the community of living and non-living things that interact with each other in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecosystem refers to the community of living and non-living components that interact with each other in a particular environment, which can be affected by plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecosystem refers to the community of living and non-living components that interact with each other in a specific environment, and is affected by plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"The macroinvertebrate, such as the T. molitor larvae, plays a crucial role in ecosystem functioning and nutrient cycling."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecosystem refers to the community of living organisms and their environment, which can be disrupted by pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ecosystem refers to the community of living organisms that interact with each other and their environment, and it is influenced by the ability of microorganisms to biodegrade organic materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"The ecosystem is the community of living organisms, including the bacterium, that interact with each other and their environment."</data>
      <data key="d0">"ECOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SERRATIA SP.&quot;">
