      <data key="d1">"E. coli is a bacterial strain used as a negative control in the experiments."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a microorganism used to overexpress the lac640 gene and determine its PS and CS degradation ability."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a type of bacteria that was used in a study to compare biofilm behavior with Achromobacter xylosoxidans M9."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a type of bacterium that has been used as a reference in the study of biodegradation of polystyrene nanoplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a bacterium with a doubling time of 68.3 min in the exponential phase."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a type of bacteria used as a negative control in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"E. coli is a type of bacterium used as a negative control in the experiment."</data>
