      <data key="d1">"Lac640 is a gene that can be overexpressed in E. coli to determine its PS and CS degradation ability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lac640 is a laccase enzyme that is highly upregulated in both PS- and CS-fed groups and has the potential to degrade both PS and CS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lac640 is an enzyme involved in the degradation of PS and lignin."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lac640 is an enzyme used to treat PS/CS samples, potentially modifying their surface morphology and functional groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-158317f8eba5f6198135df044d385935&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-effe1e87d51e126ff4ec5cf9e49d6524&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1d39fc863538a777920c4eafb37bcf8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac5b96e63e6f5e34fe841f690d9f78ac</data>
