    <node id="&quot;CS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CS is a diet fed to mealworms, which alters the structure of their gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"CS is a diet that affects the gut microbial community of larvae, with a higher relative abundance of Firmicutes and lower relative abundance of Proteobacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"CS is a type of feedstock being used to feed the larvae, and its metabolites are being compared to other feedstocks."&lt;SEP&gt;"CS is another type of plastic being studied for degradation, with a different dependency on gut microbiota compared to PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"CS refers to a type of plastic that is being studied for its degradation by enzymes such as Lac640."&lt;SEP&gt;"CS was used as a feedstock for the mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"CS, or corn straw, is another type of feedstock used for mealworms, with its consumption and degradation also being studied."</data>
