      <data key="d1">"Polyethylene microplastics are a type of plastic that can have adverse effects on zebrafish."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene microplastics are a type of plastic that is degraded by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene microplastics are small plastic particles that can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene microplastics are small plastic particles that are being studied for their biodegradation by various microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene microplastics refer to small plastic particles made of polyethylene, which are being degraded by T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1d40b7debb6497167fa1aec874ebce45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe3a2cb3a17985d07d15bed638bd90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-933de951613fc7eadfd14dde9bd18b2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CR(VI)-CONTAMINATED INDUSTRIAL WASTEWATER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TOXIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cr(VI)-contaminated industrial wastewater is a toxic substance that requires remediation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CR(VI) REMEDIATION GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cr(VI) remediation genes are genes that are involved in the remediation of Cr(VI)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-db579d338d8f90574e3ac67a3ae9938d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COLEOPTERINC GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coleopterinc genes are involved in the response of Tenebrio molitor to bacterial challenges, indicating a role in immune response or defense mechanisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM BIOMASS PRODUCTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mealworm biomass production is a biological process that involves the use of mealworms such as Tenebrio molitor to produce biomass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85fe36521680f0d09a603eab04706561</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CROP WASTE RESIDUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
