    <node id="&quot;GENETIC CODE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DNA sequence provided can be considered as a genetic code, which is a set of rules used by living cells to translate information encoded in genetic material into proteins."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN SYNTHESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein synthesis is a biological process that occurs in mealworms, with some studies suggesting that it decreases during food deprivation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The genetic code in the DNA sequence is used to synthesize proteins, which is a biological process essential for the development and function of living organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DNA sequence and genetic code are related to the cell, which is the basic structural and functional unit of living organisms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUCLEOTIDE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DNA sequence is composed of nucleotides, which are the basic building blocks of DNA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CHROMOSOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DNA sequence is organized into chromosomes, which are thread-like structures that carry genes in the nucleus of living cells."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPLICATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DNA sequence is replicated during cell division, which is a biological process that ensures the continuation of genetic information from one generation to the next."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSCRIPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DNA sequence is transcribed into RNA, which is a biological process that allows for the translation of genetic information into proteins."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSLATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The RNA transcript is translated into proteins, which is a biological process that allows for the synthesis of proteins from genetic information."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The proteins synthesized from the genetic code have a specific structure, which is determined by the sequence of amino acids."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CELL DIVISION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The DNA sequence is replicated during cell division, which is a biological process that ensures the continuation of genetic information from one generation to the next."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-15780e819c8b33749983834a5716c31f</data>
    </node>
