    <node id="&quot;FOOD DEPRIVATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Food deprivation is a physiological response analyzed in the study, with mealworms showing significant changes in their biochemical characteristics when deprived of food."&lt;SEP&gt;"Food deprivation is a physiological response that occurs in mealworms when they are unable to access sufficient nutrients, leading to changes in their metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Food deprivation is a physiological response of insects to insufficient food supply, leading to changes in their metabolic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2281f98bcfd555a703fd86232dfa42fb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT BIODIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut biodiversity refers to the variety of microorganisms present in the gut of T. molitor, which changes when fed polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d57e056cd3b06b37d22117fc75e3a4df</data>
    </node>
