    <node id="&quot;MOLECULAR WEIGHT DISTRIBUTION (MWD)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molecular weight distribution (MWD) is a biochemical measure used to analyze the molecular weight of PS residuals after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution (MWD) is a physical property of PET that affects its biodegradation rate, with a range of molecular weights and properties."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution (MWD) is a physical property of polymers that affects their biodegradability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution is a measure of the range of molecular weights in a polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molecular weight distribution (MWD) is a measure of the range of molecular weights of polymer chains."</data>
