    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURFACE HYDROPHOBICITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surface hydrophobicity is a measure of the degree to which a surface repels water, with higher values indicating greater hydrophobicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surface hydrophobicity is a physical property of PET that affects its biodegradation rate, with a range of values and effects on biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surface hydrophobicity is a physical property of polymers that affects their biodegradation, with higher hydrophobicity making it more difficult for microorganisms to break down."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1679027e80b766e0469f7323db15b497&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1006283f24aba2aa605f9e719f36cf9</data>
