      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are bacteria that have the ability to convert atmospheric nitrogen into a form that can be used by plants and animals."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are microorganisms that have the ability to fix nitrogen, and they are found in the guts of mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are microorganisms that provide a source of nitrogen via nitrogen fixation in the larvae fed PET."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are present in the gut of Styrofoam-eating mealworms and play a crucial role in their survival by fixing atmospheric nitrogen."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are present in the gut of mealworms and have the ability to fix nitrogen from the atmosphere, providing a new nitrogen source for the mealworm's metabolism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Nitrogen-fixing bacteria are present in the guts of mealworms and are responsible for the nitrogen-fixing activity."</data>
