    <node id="&quot;INSECT BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect biodegradation is the process by which insects break down plastics into smaller molecules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIODEGRADATION TESTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biodegradation tests are experiments designed to measure the ability of microorganisms to break down plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation tests refer to the experiments conducted to evaluate the ability of T. obscurus and T. molitor larvae to biodegrade PE-MPs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INFLAMMATORY RESPONSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"IMMUNE RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Inflammatory responses are a type of physiological response in insects, including Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, that occurs in response to tissue damage or infection."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory responses are an immune response that can occur in organisms that ingest microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Inflammatory responses are an immune response that can occur when organisms ingest microplastics, leading to physical damage and decreased nutrient uptake."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe381daaa91bbff20758798e5baf82b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INTESTINAL INFLAMMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Intestinal inflammation is a type of physiological response in insects, including Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus, that occurs in response to gut microbiome imbalance or mechanical stimulation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC INTERMEDIATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic intermediates are compounds that are produced during the biodegradation of plastics like LDPE, LLDPE, and HDPE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-BASED DIET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A PE-based diet is a type of diet that is used to feed Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus larvae, where PE is the sole source of energy and carbon."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TENEBRIO OBSCURUS LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tenebrio obscurus larvae are a type of insect larvae that are capable of biodegrading plastics like LDPE, LLDPE, and HDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae is a life stage of the dark mealworm that is capable of biodegrading polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae are a type of microbe that can biodegrade polystyrene (PS), showing signs of oxidation and depolymerization of the PS polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio obscurus larvae are insects that have the ability to digest and biodegrade plastic products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d8c6850a83a1c6efd4f1a3a37a0a8181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e340b8704554cdc28486ac37e78ab0fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d47e7fe379fcd6b17740bc4d953cd3b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-326a8dda1cdd196236b9c836192c76f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FENTON SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fenton system is a chemical reaction used to extract PE-MPs from Tenebrio larvae frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OLIVE OIL-BASED EXTRACTION METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Olive oil-based extraction method is a chemical reaction used to extract PE-MPs from Tenebrio larvae frass."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-MPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-MPs is a type of plastic that is being studied for its degradation by Tenebrio larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-MPs is a type of plastic that was used as a diet for the larvae, and its effect on the gut microbiomes was analyzed."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-MPs refer to polyethylene microplastics, which are used in biodegradation tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-MPs refer to polyethylene microplastics, which are used in the study to assess their impact on the microbiome of Tenebrio larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"PE-MPs refers to polyethylene microplastics, which are used as a dietary component in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b30daa90b5c91314e1d65e87f191166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2e1faf524e6fabeb512a07b13f37e51e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9b693d867918f89c9b28997fe94fc830</data>
    </node>
