      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ARTIFICIAL CLIMATE CHAMBER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Artificial climate chamber is a controlled environment used to simulate specific temperature and humidity conditions for the biodegradation tests."&lt;SEP&gt;"Artificial climate chamber is a device used to control the environment for the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ee8f544a1849c80a5a1524c4f2674c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PY-GC/MS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Py-GC/MS is a biochemical measure used to analyze the composition of PE-MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Py-GC/MS, or pyrolysis-gas chromatography-mass spectrometry, is a technique used to analyze the degradation products of polyethylene microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-988ef111808996ddbe6e483d6505ab45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CARBONYL INDEX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Carbonyl index is a biochemical measure that indicates the level of oxidation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index is a biochemical measure used to evaluate the oxidation of PE-MPs."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index is a biochemical measure used to quantify the level of oxidation in polyethylene polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index is a measure of the level of oxidation in polyethylene polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index is a measure of the carbonyl groups present in a material, which can indicate the level of degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index is a biochemical measure that is used to analyze the degradation of polyethylene (PE) by lesser waxworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index is a measure of the degree of oxidation of microplastics, which affects their biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Carbonyl index is a measure of the level of carbonyl groups in a molecule, which can be used to assess the level of oxidation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cbf098ec253f99187f3c98d5d0589f7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa33fb34ba06610c290cdfd8a5b4e916&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b25215becbc007a60f24b86a2d6aaf26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-582f48080aab075de76c9c590558639f</data>
    </node>
