    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C12:0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C12:0 is a fatty acid found in bacteria, with different species having distinct fatty acid profiles."&lt;SEP&gt;"C12:0 is a fatty acid present in the cellular composition of the bacterial species Mixta tenebrionis sp. nov."&lt;SEP&gt;"C12:0 is a fatty acid present in the whole-cell fatty acid composition of Strain BIT-26T and other species of the genus Mixta."&lt;SEP&gt;"C12:0 is a fatty acid that is present in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its lipid composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"C12:0 is a type of fatty acid that is found in the biomass of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C14:0&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C14:0 is a fatty acid found in bacteria, with different species having distinct fatty acid profiles."&lt;SEP&gt;"C14:0 is a fatty acid present in the cellular composition of the bacterial species Mixta tenebrionis sp. nov."&lt;SEP&gt;"C14:0 is a fatty acid present in the whole-cell fatty acid composition of Strain BIT-26T and other species of the genus Mixta."&lt;SEP&gt;"C14:0 is a fatty acid that is present in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its lipid composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"C14:0 is a type of fatty acid that is found in the biomass of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98d4ea946a931acf7e5a8292c30ea4c7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-706b5d3a2fa68c3f52b58132d05b7165&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C16:1&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FATTY ACID"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C16:1 is a monoenoic fatty acid with a proportion of 9-12% for potatoes and polystyrene, and 13-22% for whey."&lt;SEP&gt;"C16:1 is a type of fatty acid that is found in the biomass of Tenebrio molitor and Tenebrio obscurus."&lt;SEP&gt;"C16:1 is a type of fatty acid, also known as palmitoleic acid, with its content contributing to the overall fatty acid composition."</data>
