      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Expanded Polyethylene (PE) is a type of plastic that affects the central carbon metabolism of insect models, with Mealworm and Wax Moth larvae showing increased metabolic activity when exposed to it."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CENTRAL CARBON METABOLISM (CCM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CCM is a biological process that refers to the metabolic pathways involved in the breakdown and synthesis of carbon-based molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"CCM is a suite of compounds within the most basic cellular pathways present in all living organisms, facilitating numerous biosynthetic and metabolic pathways in response to nutrient availability."&lt;SEP&gt;"Central Carbon Metabolism (CCM) is a biological process that comprises a suite of compounds within the most basic cellular pathways present in all living organisms, facilitating numerous biosynthetic and metabolic processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7c6ced866009d759592c16009bc619b4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PYRIMIDINE METABOLISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLIC MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pyrimidine metabolism is a biological process that is elevated in Black Soldier Fly larvae when exposed to Polyethylene terephthalate (PET)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrimidine metabolism is a metabolic pathway involved in the generation of substrates for basic cellular processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pyrimidine metabolism is a metabolic measure that can be perturbed by the ingestion of PS polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ee6535da22915c7094098e016b19d80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-939800f545beed77f5a7d1c026c250fb</data>
    </node>
