      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gene Wijffels is a researcher involved in the study on the impact of plastics on insect models."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CATE PAULI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cate Pauli is a researcher involved in the study on the impact of plastics on insect models."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INSECT MODELS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Insect models, including Black Soldier Fly, Mealworm, and Wax Moth, are used to study the impact of plastics on central carbon metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ORGANIC WASTE STREAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Organic waste streams are contaminated with plastic waste, which affects the ability of insect models to convert them into valuable protein products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Organic waste streams refer to the flow of organic materials, such as food waste, that can be used as nutrients for insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-915331bc1ae85fe139629eaebc4042cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROTEIN PRODUCTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Protein products are valuable nutrients that can be produced by insect models, but their production is affected by plastic waste."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BIOTRANSFORMATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Biotransformation is a biological process by which insect models can convert plastic waste into valuable protein products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biotransformation is a biological process that occurs within insects, including the Black Soldier Fly (BSF), Mealworm (MW), and Greater Wax Moth (WM), where they break down and transform plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biotransformation is the process by which the mealworms' gut environment breaks down the polystyrene molecules."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cc6b858a4eb57553f5b1ae041e1c7160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIQUID CHROMATOGRAPHY TRIPLE QUADRUPOLE MASS SPECTROMETRY (LC-QQQ-MS)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liquid chromatography triple quadrupole mass spectrometry (LC-QqQ-MS) is a technology used to analyze the central carbon metabolism of insect models."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TARGETED TMRM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Targeted tMRM is a technology used to analyze the central carbon metabolism of insect models."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6ce341034979daadf1f9dc7037397d1b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BLACK SOLDIER FLY (BSF)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"BSF is a well-studied insect species, cosmopolitan and applied to upcycle many organic substrates, with a relatively short lifecycle, fast growth rate, and easy to rear on a range of organic food stuffs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MEALWORM (MW)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"MW is the most investigated larval model in plastic biodegradation, proposed as a model in micro- and nanoplastic toxicity, and has a high potential in sustainable agriculture as an organic fertilizer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GREATER WAX MOTH (WM)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"INSECT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WM is a well-studied insect species, consuming large amounts of bee wax, which may give them an advantage to metabolize substances such as plastics, with a relatively short lifecycle, fast growth rate, and easy to rear on a range of organic food stuffs."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BEE WAX&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bee wax is a nutrient source for WM, containing a range of chemical compounds including alkanes and alkenes, which may give WM an advantage to metabolize substances such as plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOLASSES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Molasses is a food supplement that affects the metabolism and microbiota of insect models."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molasses is a supplement used in the artificial feeding of plastic to insects, potentially affecting their metabolism and ability to biotransform plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Molasses is a supplement used in the study to evaluate the impact of plastic on insect metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-394b3365ffb36d05dca2ef06bf74e462&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae2c294948460ef392ceeec82d5e81f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIPTERA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORDER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Diptera is an order of insects that includes the Black Soldier Fly (BSF)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GOTERRA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Goterra is a company that provides Black Soldier Fly (BSF) insects for research."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CSIRO INSECT LABORATORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ORGANIZATION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"CSIRO Insect Laboratory is a research facility that studies insects, including the Black Soldier Fly (BSF), Mealworm (MW), and Greater Wax Moth (WM)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c8dab62f56f2bfabf08bfe99049386a</data>
    </node>
