    <node id="&quot;CONTROL GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Control group is a concept used in the experiment, being represented by wheat bran."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control group refers to a group of T. molitor that are not fed EPS, used as a comparison to the EPS-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control group is a group of T. molitor and T. obscurus larvae that do not receive antibiotic treatment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control group is a concept used in the study to compare the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae under different dietary conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Control group is a group of T. molitor that is being used as a reference for comparison with other experimental groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control group is a set of mealworms that are not given any supplements, used as a comparison to the experimental groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"The control group refers to the group of T. molitor larvae that are being fed a standard diet, and are being used as a comparison to the other groups."</data>
