    <node id="&quot;ACHROMOBACTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been found to degrade various pollutants, including polystyrene and di(2-ethylhexyl)phthalate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been found to have various species capable of degrading different types of pollutants, such as hydrocarbons and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria that has been investigated for its role in degrading polystyrene, highlighting its potential in environmental cleanup efforts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria that includes a species capable of degrading di-(2-ethylhexyl) phthalate, showing its biodegradative capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria that was identified in the T. molitor larval gut isolates, with strain Achromobacter xylosidoxans OR859752 showing significant ability to degrade nanopolystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a type of microorganism that has been found to have robust enzymatic activity and historical efficacy in xenobiotic degradation, making it a potential candidate for polystyrene biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Achromobacter is a genus of bacteria that was found to have a significant difference in relative abundance between the bran and PE diets."</data>
