    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HT-GPC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"HT-GPC analysis is a biochemical measure used to examine the molecular weight of plastics, such as PE and PS, after degradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC analysis is a method being used to examine the performance of depolymerization and biodegradation of PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC analysis is a technique used to study the degradation of polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC analysis is a technique used to characterize the molecular weight and molecular weight distribution of LDPE before and after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"HT-GPC analysis is a technology used for analyzing molecular weights."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfe58fb1bbaa5c35e9c6c837d0b1050f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PUTATIVE GAS FRACTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Putative gas fraction is a biological concept that refers to the amount of plastic that is converted into gases, such as carbon dioxide, after degradation by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EXTRACTION METHOD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Extraction method refers to the process of isolating and purifying the degraded plastics, such as PE and PS, from the frass of mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CONTAMINATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Contamination refers to the presence of unwanted substances, such as bacterial biomass or secreted proteins, in the degraded plastics, such as PE and PS."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALKENE BONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alkene bonds are a type of chemical bond present in the biodegradation products of LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Alkene bonds are a type of chemical bond that is formed during the degradation of plastics, such as PE and PS, by mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-O STRETCHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-O stretching refers to the chemical property of the degraded plastics, such as PE and PS, that is associated with the incorporation of oxygen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R-OH BEND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R-OH bend refers to the chemical property of the degraded plastics, such as PE and PS, that is associated with the incorporation of oxygen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;R-OH STRETCHING&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"R-OH stretching refers to the chemical property of the degraded plastics, such as PE and PS, that is associated with the incorporation of oxygen."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENTEROBACTER ABSURIAE YTI&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Enterobacter absuriae YTI is a bacterium known for its ability to degrade PE, isolated from the gut of the Indian mealmoth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37</data>
    </node>
