      <data key="d1">"Fusobacteria is a class of bacteria that includes Sebaldella termiditis, which is associated with the degradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fusobacteria is a class of bacteria that is present in the gut of Alphitobius diaperinus, with a relative frequency of 3% in the PS group and 1% in the CT group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fusobacteria is a phylum of bacteria that is present in the gut of Alphitobius diaperinus, with a relative frequency of 3% in the PS group and 1% in the CT group."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fusobacteria is a phylum of bacteria that is present in the yellow mealworms' gut, and it plays a role in the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fusobacteria is a phylum present in the gut bacterial communities of yellow mealworms, with a relative abundance of 6.35% in the PP-fed group."</data>
