    <node id="&quot;MICROBIAL DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Microbial diversity is a measure of the variety of microorganisms in a sample, which was found to be higher in PS samples compared to CT samples for fungal microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial diversity refers to the variety of different microorganisms that are present in a particular environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbial diversity refers to the variety of microorganisms present in the gut of the larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7f79551ab9793788cd662ab66bca5ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COMMUNITY COMPOSITION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Community composition refers to the types and proportions of different microorganisms that are present in a particular environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Community composition refers to the variety of different species present in a community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e5407936cdb4f49bd5363f782dab563</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HIERARCHICAL CLUSTER ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hierarchical cluster analysis is a method used to analyze and visualize microbial community composition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hierarchical cluster analysis is a method used to group microorganisms based on their genetic similarity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Hierarchical cluster analysis is a method used to group the gut bacterial communities of yellow mealworms based on their similarity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df147b253e29abfa812d060407051e45</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;INCUBATION EXPERIMENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The incubation experiment is a type of experiment where microorganisms are allowed to grow and interact with their environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RELATIVE ABUNDANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A measure of the amount of a substance relative to others"&lt;SEP&gt;"Relative abundance refers to the proportion of a particular microorganism that is present in a sample."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5982537ede5118840b65596ee2a04896&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FREQUENCY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Frequency refers to the number of times a particular microorganism is detected in a sample."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASTERISKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Asterisks are used to indicate that a particular genus is strongly associated with plastic degradation."</data>
