    <node id="&quot;CITRATE UTILIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Citrate utilization is a biological concept used to determine the ability of bacteria to utilize citrate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Citrate utilization is a biological process that is negative in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its inability to utilize citrate as a carbon source."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GELATINASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gelatinase is an enzyme that breaks down gelatin, with different bacteria having varying levels of gelatinase activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gelatinase is an enzyme that is negative in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its inability to catalyze the hydrolysis of gelatin."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
