      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Arginine dihydrolase is an enzyme that breaks down arginine, with different bacteria having varying levels of arginine dihydrolase activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Arginine dihydrolase is an enzyme that is negative in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its inability to catalyze the hydrolysis of arginine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
