    <node id="&quot;ORNITHINE DECARBOXYLASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ornithine decarboxylase is an enzyme produced by Strain BIT-26T, distinguishing it from other species of the genus Mixta."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ornithine decarboxylase is an enzyme that breaks down ornithine, with different bacteria having varying levels of ornithine decarboxylase activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ornithine decarboxylase is an enzyme that is positive in Mixta tenebrionis, indicating its ability to catalyze the decarboxylation of ornithine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d043948723ae25a365e297c98300be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-146789a250a0dbaae0d8438de692e191&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014b72d0a2657cbc89c4dee5f2b32bba</data>
