    <node id="&quot;WCA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"WCA (Water Contact Angle) is a measure of the hydrophobicity of a surface, used to assess changes in the surface properties of polymers during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA is a measure of the surface properties of PS films, detecting changes after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA, or water contact angle, is a measure of the hydrophobicity of PS film."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA, or water contact angle, is a technique used to measure the hydrophilicity of surfaces, including PS films."&lt;SEP&gt;"WCA is a type of analysis used to study the biodegradation of PP by T. molitor and Z. atratus larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe29ef34ad1e5ab11c4ec7f5270fa94d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9859524b7a6851b786570d2a704e34f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2efbc0287662aa64684e4db6a131c3de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e6fd56772ef66691cf6f1c613ba42e1</data>
