    <node id="&quot;CATIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cations are a type of chemical property being measured in the insects' frass."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cations are positively charged ions, such as Mg²⁺, Na⁺, and K⁺, which are present in the frass of the insects."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cations, such as potassium, sodium, magnesium, and calcium, are involved in biochemical processes and are affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS)."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6338d56b535220f260826703b0f7229&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MITOCHONDRIA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mitochondria are major intracellular Mg²⁺ reservoirs, regulating coupled reactions in energy metabolism, including the TCA cycle, electron transport chain, and ADP/ATP translocation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MG²⁺ HOMEOSTASIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mg²⁺ homeostasis is involved in various cellular malfunctions, especially in relation to reactions where mitochondria are involved, and its dysfunction can affect cellular energy metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;V-ATPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"V-ATPase plays a dominant role in osmo-regulation and excretion in insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NA⁺/K⁺-ATPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase is involved in transport of ammonia from the hemolymph into the cytoplasm via the basolateral Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase and is stimulated synergistically by NH₄⁺ and K⁺."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ELECTRON TRANSPORT CHAIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The electron transport chain is a series of protein complexes involved in generating energy for the cell through the transfer of electrons."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADP/ATP TRANSLOCATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ADP/ATP translocation refers to the movement of ADP and ATP across the mitochondrial membrane, playing a crucial role in energy metabolism."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NH₄⁺&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"NH₄⁺ is an ammonium ion that can stimulate the Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase and is involved in the transport of ammonia from the hemolymph into the cytoplasm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HEMOLYMPH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hemolymph is the fluid in insects that is equivalent to blood in vertebrates, playing a role in the transport of nutrients and waste products."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CYTOPLASM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cytoplasm is the region between the cell membrane and the nucleus, where many metabolic processes take place."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BASOLATERAL NA⁺/K⁺-ATPASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The basolateral Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase is an enzyme involved in the transport of ammonia from the hemolymph into the cytoplasm via the Na⁺/K⁺-ATPase."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;THERMOGRAMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Thermograms are biochemical measures used to analyze the thermal degradation of PS and other substances."&lt;SEP&gt;"Thermograms are the graphical representations of the thermal transitions that occur during the heating of a sample, providing information about the physical and chemical structure of the polymers present."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a708f09b97ac93da05bd1d20bdfe174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3eb3742a8be739a1146cbf15e6b7ae5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIETARY CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
