    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL MASKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical masks are made of polypropylene material and have different layers, including outer, middle, and inner layers, which are ingested by yellow mealworms at varying rates."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIAL DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bacterial diversity in the larval gut of yellow mealworms changes when they are fed a diet of surgical masks, with potential implications for the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial diversity refers to the variety of different bacterial species present in a community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bacterial diversity refers to the variety of bacterial species present in a given sample or environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNGAL DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fungal diversity in the larval gut of yellow mealworms also changes when they are fed a diet of surgical masks, which may play a role in the degradation of the masks."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungal diversity refers to the variety of different fungal species present in a community."&lt;SEP&gt;"Fungal diversity refers to the variety of fungal species present in a given sample or environment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1070f8c33eb8afcfcffac95df9012d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d33654bada6ddaf4917586dd5fd41e9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NONWOVEN FABRIC&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nonwoven fabric is a type of material used to make the outer and inner layers of surgical masks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MELT-BLOWN FILTRATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Melt-blown filtration is a type of material used to make the middle layer of surgical masks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ITS GENES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENETIC CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"ITS genes are used to analyze the fungal diversity in the larval gut of yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ILLUMA MISEQ&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Illuma MiSeq is a type of sequencing technology used to analyze the bacterial and fungal diversity in the larval gut of yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATTENUATED TOTAL REFLECTION-FOURIER TRANSFORM INFRARED SPECTROSCOPY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Attenuated total reflection-Fourier transform infrared spectroscopy is a type of technology used to analyze the chemical composition of the frass of yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASK CONSUMPTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mask consumption refers to the process of yellow mealworms ingesting and degrading surgical masks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f2417ca11674320d88eecdf4cb66f9d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASKS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Masks are the primary product being studied for biodegradation, with different layers (outer, middle, inner) exhibiting varying degrees of degradation when consumed by yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MASK LAYERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Mask layers refer to the different layers (outer, middle, inner) of masks, which exhibit varying degrees of degradation when consumed by yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C-H STRETCH BONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C-H stretch bonds are a type of chemical bond present in polypropylene, which are affected by oxidation and degradation during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DECOMPOSITION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Decomposition rate refers to the rate at which mask materials are broken down during biodegradation, which is measured using DSC-TGA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUMBER AVERAGE WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Number average weight is a measure of the average molecular weight of polymer chains, which is used to analyze the biodegradation of polypropylene masks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;WEIGHT AVERAGE WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Weight average weight is a measure of the average molecular weight of polymer chains, which is used to analyze the biodegradation of polypropylene masks."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f370c2f246a6c8a776ae90277a5aacc8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURGICAL MASK&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Surgical mask is a type of product that is used as a diet for yellow mealworms in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Surgical masks are a type of product that is biodegraded by the yellow mealworm, with different layers showing varying degrees of biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT-BACTERIAL COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut-bacterial community of the yellow mealworm is composed of various families and genera of bacteria, with changes in composition observed in response to different mask diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAL GUT BACTERIAL COMMUNITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The larval gut bacterial community is a biological concept that refers to the community of bacteria in the gut of the yellow mealworm."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e663286500e382f6d296e2b683bf542</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNCLASSIFIED ENTEROBACTERIACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unclassified Enterobacteriaceae is a dominant genus in PU-fed groups, indicating a strong association with PU degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unclassified Enterobacteriaceae is a genus of bacteria present in the gut of yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Unclassified Enterobacteriaceae is a group of bacteria that is strongly associated with the degradation of plastics and is found in high relative abundances in the gut of yellow mealworms fed with different mask layer diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEBARYOMYCESACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGI"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Debaryomycesaceae is a family of fungi that is predominant in the bran-fed group of yellow mealworms, accounting for 55.50% of the gut fungal community."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ASPERGILLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aspergillaceae is a dominant family in PP-fed groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"Aspergillaceae is a family of fungi that is found in high relative abundance in the mask-fed groups of yellow mealworms and is associated with the degradation of plastics such as PE."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUREOBASIACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGI"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aureobasiaceae is a family of fungi that is found in high relative abundance in the outer-fed group of yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7a91a3c11281861b559c31c3107c72e7</data>
    </node>
