      <data key="d1">"Lesser waxworms are a type of microorganism that can degrade polyethylene (PE) and are used in the study to analyze the biodegradation of PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lesser waxworms are able to consume and digest PE, but with lower survival rates compared to those fed with WC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lesser waxworms are capable of degrading PE and can develop into a second generation with favorable PE biodegradation when fed a diet supplemented with nutrition."&lt;SEP&gt;"Lesser waxworms are microorganisms used to assess PE degradation and survivability rate."</data>
