      <data key="d1">"PDI is a measure of the broadness of the polymer distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of the molecular weight distribution of PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"The polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of the molecular weight distribution of the PP foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of the distribution of molecular weights in microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of the heterogeneity of polymer chain lengths, which increases during biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Polydispersity Index is a measure used to describe the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer sample."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of the distribution of molecular weights in a polymer, used to characterize the properties of microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of the heterogeneity of polymer chain lengths, which increases after biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"The polydispersity index (PDI) is a measure of the molecular weight distribution of polystyrene (PS)."</data>
