      <data key="d1">"Pseudomonadaceae is a bacterial family that is significantly more abundant in PS samples than in CT samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family of bacteria that is reported to be one of the main actors in insect's gut, involved in the breakdown of synthetic products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family that increased in relative abundance in the PP-fed group, indicating its potential association with PP degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family of bacteria that belongs to the class Gammaproteobacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family of bacteria that can degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Pseudomonadaceae is a family of bacteria that includes some of the isolated strains, which are capable of degrading polystyrene."</data>
