    <node id="&quot;A. DIAPERINUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROBE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"A. diaperinus is an insect species whose gut microbiome is being studied for its potential to degrade plastics, with a diverse community of microorganisms including bacteria and fungi."&lt;SEP&gt;"A. diaperinus is an insect that is able to survive on a non-conventional food source such as polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHA-DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alpha-diversity is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms in a sample, which was found to be lower in PS samples compared to CT samples for bacterial microbiota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BETA-DIVERSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Beta-diversity is a measure of the difference in diversity of microorganisms between samples, which was found to be higher in PS samples compared to CT samples for fungal microbiota."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PCOA PLOTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PCoA plots are a method of visualizing the differences in diversity of microorganisms between samples, which was used to compare PS and CT samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LOG2-FOLD CHANGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Log2-fold change is a measure of the difference in abundance of a microorganism between samples, which was used to identify overrepresented genera in PS samples compared to CT samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOULT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"LIFE STAGE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moult is a life stage of an insect, which was observed in A. diaperinus after feeding on polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAE WEIGHT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larvae weight is a measure of the physiological response of an insect to a food source, which was found to be reduced in A. diaperinus after feeding on polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRESSFUL REARING CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Stressful rearing conditions is a physiological response of an insect to its environment, which was observed in A. diaperinus after feeding on polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b6ddf9dd30d7258964408f9a915d3478</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYRENE MONOXYGENASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrene Monoxygenase is an enzyme involved in the styrene degradation pathway, consisting of subunits styA and styB, and regulated by styS and styR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PSEUDOGRACILLIBACILLUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pseudogracillibacillus is a genus of bacteria found to be significantly more abundant in PS samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9b4b45d826a6a7956015e680f5fb8ee6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;K. ROSEA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"K. rosea is a microorganism that is able to degrade malachite green, a chemical compound with a styrene core structure, which may indicate its potential to degrade polystyrene."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9095195e9cf06b9887c03abde6284d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYRENE CORE STRUCTURE&quot;">
