    <node id="&quot;ETHYLENE VINYL ACETATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POLYMER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethylene Vinyl Acetate is a type of plastic polymer that can be degraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, but has worse adverse effects on larval survival compared to other polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYOLEFIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyolefin is a type of plastic polymer that includes polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyolefin is a type of plastic polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyolefin is a type of plastic used as an experimental feedstock in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COPOLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Copolymer is a type of plastic polymer that includes ethylene vinyl acetate."&lt;SEP&gt;"Copolymer is a type of plastic polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Copolymer is a type of plastic used as an experimental feedstock in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAL SURVIVAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Larval survival is the process by which Tenebrio molitor larvae remain alive and healthy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYMERIZATION TYPES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polymerization types refer to the different types of chemical bonds that make up plastics, which can affect the biodegradation of plastics by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polymerization types refer to the different ways in which plastic polymers are formed, including polyolefin, polyester, and copolymer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLASTIC DEGRADATION ABILITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL FUNCTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plastic degradation ability is the ability of certain microorganisms, such as Aspergillus and Cladosporium, to break down plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9d7500fe4985cb2b885f9eb244ed3c2e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;EVA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"EVA is a type of diet fed to yellow mealworms, resulting in changes in the gut bacterial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"EVA is a type of plastic being studied for its degradation by yellow mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"EVA is a type of plastic polymer, associated with biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"EVA is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms, with a complex structure that has adverse effects on the larval weight change and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"EVA is a type of plastic, specifically ethylene-vinyl acetate, used as an experimental feedstock in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"EVA is likely an abbreviation for a chemical or material property, specifically Ethylene-Vinyl Acetate, a type of plastic or polymer."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT CORE MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Gut core microbiome refers to the community of microorganisms living in the digestive system of the yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ETHYLENE-VINYL ACETATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Ethylene-Vinyl Acetate is a specific type of chemical compound, also known as EVA."&lt;SEP&gt;"Ethylene-vinyl acetate is a type of plastic used as an experimental feedstock in the study, also referred to as EVA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PRISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"SOFTWARE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Prism is a software used for statistical analysis of the data."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-444b8acd02a76616457012e1ac0db23b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;YELLOW MEALWORMS' GUT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut of the yellow mealworms is where the degradation of plastics takes place, and its microorganisms play a crucial role in the process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LARVAL WEIGHT CHANGES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSIOLOGICAL RESPONSE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The weight changes of the yellow mealworms' larvae are affected by their diet, including the consumption of plastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The starvation group is a control group in the study, where the yellow mealworms are not fed any diet."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;O-H BEND&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The O-H bend is a chemical bond that is present in the plastics and their degradation products, and it is analyzed using FTIR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CH2 STRETCH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The CH2 stretch is a chemical bond that is present in the plastics and their degradation products, and it is analyzed using FTIR."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COVERAGE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Coverage is a measure of diversity, used to study the diversity of microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Coverage is a measure of the diversity of microorganisms in the yellow mealworms' gut."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d0e4cb4324bc684ebb2ca6136c04ad0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MORAXELLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moraxellaceae is a family of bacteria that belongs to the class Gammaproteobacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moraxellaceae is a family of bacteria that can degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moraxellaceae is a family of bacteria that includes some of the isolated strains, which are capable of degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Moraxellaceae is a family that increased in relative abundance in the PP-fed group, suggesting its potential role in PP degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bfd05eac1abc28ac416e6a56ccd6a9d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10f59d5d10f08e8107f36bff5a4c93ae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eadba0dcfe8eff9c8040ec5f17e1adb3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PEDICOCCUS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pedicoccus is a genus that disappeared in the PP-fed group, although it was dominant in the bran-fed group."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNWEIGHTED UNIFRAC ANALYSIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unweighted Unifrac analysis is a method used to compare the gut bacterial communities of yellow mealworms fed with different diets."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PORPHYROMONADACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Porphyromonadaceae is a family of bacteria present in the gut of yellow mealworms, with an increased relative abundance in the EVA-fed group."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-476e13b69587aa4e81395e2fd00a9d5a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIAL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Material is a general term that includes PP, PU, and EVA."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7043eb8aa4221f396a5c65fb6493bd41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYGONOMONAS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dygonomonas is a dominant genus in EVA-fed groups, accounting for 76.11%, and is specifically associated with EVA degradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEBAROMYCESACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Debaromycesaceae is the dominant family in bran-fed groups, but less than 1% in plastics-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPORIDIOBOLACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sporidiobolaceae is a dominant family in plastic-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AUREOBASIDIACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Aureobasidiaceae is a dominant family in PU-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SPOROBACTERIACEAE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FAMILY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sporobacteriaceae is a dominant family in EVA-fed groups, with a relative abundance of 88.55%."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HYPHOPICHA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Hyphopicha is a dominant fungal genus in bran-fed groups, but decreases or disappears in all plastics-fed groups."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FUNGAL PHYLA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGI"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fungal phyla are the phyla of fungi present in the gut of yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a3f07da33b55bf8a25fe06beee23e90e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;POLYISOCYANATES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL COMPOUND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Polyisocyanates are a component of polyurethane plastics, which can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;C=O BONDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL BOND"</data>
      <data key="d1">"C=O bonds are a type of chemical bond found in polyurethane plastics, which can be biodegraded by yellow mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3e34d58a20a707b35e8fcd5658ba2924</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CLADOSPORIUM SP. P7&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"FUNGUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Cladosporium sp. P7 is a fungus that has been found to biodegrade polyester polyurethane."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALCYCLIPHILUS SP.BQB&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BACTERIUM"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alcycliphilus sp.BQB is a bacterium that has been found to biodegrade adipate/phthalate polyester polyurethanes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ADIPATE/PHTHALATE POLYESTER POLYURETHANE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"POLYMER"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Adipate/phthalate polyester polyurethane is a type of plastic that has been found to be biodegradable by certain microorganisms, including Alcycliphilus sp.BQB."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMIDEASE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"ENZYME"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amidease is an enzyme that has been found to play a role in the biodegradation of plastics, including polyurethane."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-03f2fc4d98412efb8a792474cc47e558</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BACTERIALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
