    <node id="&quot;DIGESTIVE BIOFRAGMENTATION MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Digestive biofragmentation model is a theoretical framework used to predict and understand the fragmentation process of ingested plastics in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Digestive biofragmentation model is a theoretical framework used to simulate the size-reduction process of plastic particles in the intestinal tract."&lt;SEP&gt;"The digestive biofragmentation model is a biological process that simulates the time courses of the size-reduction process of PS and PE particles in mealworms."</data>
