      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Agilent 8700 LDIR is a specific type of LDIR instrument used to count and characterize microplastics in the mealworm intestine."&lt;SEP&gt;"Agilent 8700 LDIR is the specific model of LDIR equipment used in the study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STERILE SCALPEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Sterile scalpel is used to remove the head of the mealworm larva."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TWEEZERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Tweezers are used to gently remove the intestine of the mealworm larva."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LIQUID NITROGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Liquid nitrogen is used to crush the intestine samples."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METAL MEMBRANE FILTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL FEATURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metal membrane filter is used to filter the digestion solution and collect the residual microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ANTIBIOTIC PERFORMANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Antibiotic performance is a biological concept that refers to the ability of mealworms to withstand oxidative stress and damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TRANSPORTERS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PROTEIN"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Transporters are proteins that are involved in the uptake and transport of nutrients in mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Transporters are proteins that help mealworm larvae absorb nutrients from their food, and their production is affected by the type of plastic ingested."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE-FED MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PE-fed mealworms are microorganisms that have been fed a diet of PE microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS-FED MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS-fed mealworms are microorganisms that have been fed a diet of PS microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PVC-FED MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PVC-fed mealworms are microorganisms that have been fed a diet of PVC microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BRAN-FED MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bran-fed mealworms are microorganisms that have been fed a diet of wheat bran."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;UNFED MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Unfed mealworms are microorganisms that have been deprived of food sources."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DIHYDROETHIDIUM (DHE)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Dihydroethidium (DHE) is a chemical reaction that is used to analyze ROS levels in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;BICINCHONINIC ACID (BCA)&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Bicinchoninic Acid (BCA) is a chemical reaction that is used to quantify protein levels in mealworms."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PA FILTER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PA filter is a physical property that is used to filter microplastics."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NUTRIENT EXHAUSTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nutrient exhaustion is a condition that occurs when mealworms do not receive enough nutrients, leading to negative growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RANDOM INTERNAL SCISSION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Random internal scission is a process where polymer chains are broken down randomly, resulting in heterogeneous chain lengths."&lt;SEP&gt;"Random internal scission is a type of chemical reaction that occurs during the depolymerization of plastics, resulting in the breakdown of polymer chains."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENDO-TYPE DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Endo-type depolymerization is a type of chemical reaction that occurs during the biodegradation of plastics, resulting in the breakdown of polymer chains."&lt;SEP&gt;"Endo-type depolymerization is a type of depolymerization where polymer chains are broken down internally."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-67028993c2650049216602d03fb3f786&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATERIAL CRYSTALLINITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Material crystallinity is a physical property of plastics that affects the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ATACTIC STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Atactic structure is a type of molecular structure found in some plastics, and it affects the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTALLINE STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crystalline structure is a physical property of plastics that affects the biodegradation process."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;AMORPHOUS FRACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Amorphous fractions are a type of molecular structure found in some plastics, and they are more easily degraded than crystalline fractions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRYSTALLINE FRACTIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crystalline fractions are a type of molecular structure found in some plastics, and they are more resistant to degradation than amorphous fractions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-77a9d70651c9f13362e4c1e3ce10eab0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PE POLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PE polymer is a type of crystalline plastic that contains side chains and is less likely to be attacked and depolymerized by mealworms compared to PS and PVC polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PVC POLYMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PVC polymer is a type of plastic that is more likely to be attacked and depolymerized by mealworms compared to PE polymers, but its depolymerization rate is slower than that of PS polymers."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LDIR TECHNIQUE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"TECHNOLOGY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The LDIR technique is a method used to count and characterize microplastics in the mealworm intestine."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;COPEPODS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Copepods are a type of organism that can ingest microplastics, leading to intestinal blockage and physical damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRABS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"MICROORGANISMS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Crabs are a type of organism that can ingest microplastics, leading to intestinal blockage and physical damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZEBRA FISH&quot;">
