      <data key="d1">"Zebra fish are a type of organism that can ingest microplastics, leading to intestinal blockage and physical damage."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GUT MICROENVIRONMENT OF MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The gut microenvironment of mealworms is the environment inside the gut of mealworms, where microplastics can be depolymerized and degraded."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1536c14bdcd58ae9dabf3a49f6724cd8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEPURATION&quot;">
