    <node id="&quot;ENERGY BUDGET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy budget is the amount of energy that an organism uses to survive, grow, and reproduce."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PITS AND HOLES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL PROPERTY"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Pits and holes are the structures that are formed on the surface of polystyrene during biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a221e0c62ecd5a2502ec0a4473ab0999</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DYNAMIC ENERGY BUDGET MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Dynamic Energy Budget model is a mathematical model used to describe life cycles of different organisms and assess changes in physiological processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEB THEORY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEB theory describes the energy and mass fluxes in organisms and is used to assess changes in physiological processes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserves are a measure of the amount of energy that is stored in an organism for future use."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to the energy stores that an organism uses to sustain itself during times of scarcity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to the energy stores that organisms use to maintain their structures and support their growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to the stored energy and nutrients that mealworms use to survive and grow."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserves refer to the stored energy sources in the larvae, such as lipids and glycogen, which are used to maintain life and support growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATURATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maturation is a biological process that occurs in organisms as they develop and become ready to reproduce."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maturation is the process of becoming mature, which is not considered to occur during the larval stage of T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Maturation refers to the process by which mealworms develop and grow into adults."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STANDARD DEB MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Standard DEB model is a version of the Dynamic Energy Budget model that is used as a starting point to derive new equations in new model versions."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SIMPLIFIED DEB MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Simplified DEB model is a version of the Dynamic Energy Budget model that allows for significant simplifications of standard DEB model equations."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KOOIJMAN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kooijman is a person who has contributed to the development of the Dynamic Energy Budget model."&lt;SEP&gt;"Kooijman is a reference to a researcher who has contributed to the development of the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAGER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jager is a person who has contributed to the development of the Dynamic Energy Budget model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ZIMMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Zimmer is a person who has contributed to the development of the Dynamic Energy Budget model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;LLANDRES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Llandres is a person who has contributed to the development of the Dynamic Energy Budget model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY CONDUCTANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy conductance is a biochemical measure that is used to estimate the energy available to T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy conductance is a measure of the rate at which energy is mobilized from reserves in an organism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Energy conductance refers to the rate at which energy is transferred within the larvae's body, measured in units of length per unit time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MATURITY MAINTENANCE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maturity maintenance is a biological process that occurs in organisms as they maintain their current state of maturity."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTION BUFFER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproduction buffer is a biological concept that refers to the accumulation of reserves that are necessary for reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reproduction buffer is a measure of the amount of energy that is stored in an organism for reproduction."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reproduction buffer refers to the energy reserves that are allocated for reproduction in T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reproduction buffer refers to the energy reserves that are used to support reproduction in T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The reproduction buffer is a component of the DEB model that represents the energy stored for reproduction and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"The reproduction buffer refers to the energy reserves that an organism has available for reproduction, and in this context, it is being studied in terms of its role in larval development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ISOMORPHISM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Isomorphism is a biological concept that refers to the idea that organisms do not change shape during growth."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eee7e44e4c15567a057d7d295d240211</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DEB MODEL&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"DEB model is a biological concept that is used to study the growth and survival patterns of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"DEB model is a biological concept that refers to a model of growth and development in organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"DEB model, or Dynamic Energy Budget model, is a mathematical framework used to describe the energy and mass fluxes in living organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DEB model is a theoretical framework used to understand the dynamics of energy and mass in organisms, and is applied to study the survival and development of larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DEB model is used to analyze the development of T. molitor larvae and reserve dynamics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The DEB model, or Dynamic Energy Budget model, is a theoretical framework used to describe the growth and development of organisms, including insects like T. molitor."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVES DYNAMICS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserves dynamics refers to the process by which an organism's energy reserves are allocated and utilized, and in this context, it is being studied in terms of its role in larval growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VON BERTALANFFY GROWTH RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The Von Bertalanffy growth rate is a specific type of growth rate that is used to describe the growth of organisms, and in this context, it is being used to model the growth of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Von Bertalanffy growth rate refers to the rate at which the larvae grow, measured in units of length per unit time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STYROFOAM CHIPS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Styrofoam chips are a type of material that is being used as a food source for the T. molitor larvae in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION 1 GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starvation 1 group is a concept used in the study to compare the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae under starvation conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The starvation 1 group refers to the group of T. molitor larvae that are not being fed any food, and are being used to study the effects of starvation on growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STARVATION 2 GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Starvation 2 group is a concept used in the study to compare the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae under starvation conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"The starvation 2 group refers to the group of T. molitor larvae that are not being fed any food, but are being allowed to eat droppings and moult residues, and are being used to study the effects of starvation on growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"The PS group refers to the group of T. molitor larvae that are being fed a diet of Styrofoam chips, and are being used to study the effects of this diet on growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS LARGE GROUP&quot;">
