      <data key="d1">"Lublin, Poland refers to the location of the Cricket Farm, and is being used as a source of insects for the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;JAGER AND ZIMMER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PERSON"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Jager and Zimmer are references to researchers who have contributed to the understanding of the DEB model and its application to organism development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Jager and Zimmer refer to the authors of a paper that is being cited in the experiment, and are being used as a reference for the DEB model."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6dcd4cd232a018bcab118acc67b3f0f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMINS AND MINERALS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitamins and minerals are added to the oatmeal to provide essential nutrients for the larvae's growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;RESERVE DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOCHEMICAL MEASURE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reserve density is a biochemical measure that is used to estimate the energy reserves of T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserve density is a biochemical measure that refers to the amount of reserves that are available for growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Reserve density refers to the amount of energy stored in the larvae's reserves, crucial for their growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;REPRODUCTION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Reproduction rate is a measure of the larvae's ability to reproduce, influenced by factors such as food availability and energy reserves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRUCTURAL BODY LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural body length refers to the physical length of the larvae's body, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUMETRIC BODY LENGTH&quot;">
