      <data key="d1">"Volumetric body length refers to the volume of the larvae's body, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PHYSICAL BODY LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Physical body length refers to the physical length of the larvae's body, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUMETRIC LENGTH OF RESERVE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volumetric length of reserve refers to the volume of the larvae's energy reserves, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC MAINTENANCE RATE COEFFICIENT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic maintenance rate coefficient refers to the rate at which the larvae's body maintains its structure and function, measured in units of time."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY INVESTMENT RATIO&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy investment ratio refers to the proportion of energy allocated to different functions within the larvae's body, measured in units of energy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXIMUM REPRODUCTION RATE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum reproduction rate refers to the maximum rate at which the larvae can reproduce, influenced by factors such as food availability and energy reserves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXIMUM STRUCTURAL BODY LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum structural body length refers to the maximum physical length of the larvae's body, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXIMUM VOLUMETRIC BODY LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum volumetric body length refers to the maximum volume of the larvae's body, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRUCTURAL BODY LENGTH AT PUBERTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structural body length at puberty refers to the physical length of the larvae's body at the onset of puberty, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUMETRIC BODY LENGTH AT PUBERTY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volumetric body length at puberty refers to the volume of the larvae's body at the onset of puberty, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;CRITICAL STRUCTURAL LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Critical structural length refers to the minimum physical length of the larvae's body required for survival, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUME-SPECIFIC SOMATIC MAINTENANCE POWER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volume-specific somatic maintenance power refers to the rate at which energy is used to maintain the larvae's body, measured in units of energy per unit volume."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VOLUME-SPECIFIC COSTS FOR STRUCTURE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Volume-specific costs for structure refers to the energy required to maintain the larvae's body structure, measured in units of energy per unit volume."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MAXIMUM RESERVE DENSITY&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Maximum reserve density refers to the maximum amount of energy stored in the larvae's reserves, measured in units of energy per unit volume."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY CONTENT OF A SINGLE EGG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy content of a single egg refers to the amount of energy stored in a single egg, measured in units of energy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;TOTAL NUMBER OF EGGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Total number of eggs refers to the total number of eggs produced by the larvae, measured in units of count."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY DENSITY THRESHOLD FOR A SINGLE EGG&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy density threshold for a single egg refers to the minimum amount of energy required for a single egg to develop, measured in units of energy per unit volume."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY DENSITY THRESHOLD FOR PUPATION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy density threshold for pupation refers to the minimum amount of energy required for the larvae to pupate, measured in units of energy per unit volume."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRACTION OF MOBILIZED RESERVES ALLOCATED TO THE SOMA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fraction of mobilized reserves allocated to the soma refers to the proportion of energy allocated to the larvae's body, measured in units of energy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FRACTION OF ALLOCATED RESERVES FIXED IN EGGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Fraction of allocated reserves fixed in eggs refers to the proportion of energy allocated to egg production, measured in units of energy."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROPORTIONALITY COEFFICIENT FOR VOLUMETRIC BODY LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proportionality coefficient for volumetric body length refers to the ratio of volumetric body length to structural body length, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PROPORTIONALITY COEFFICIENT FOR RESERVE LENGTH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Proportionality coefficient for reserve length refers to the ratio of reserve length to structural body length, measured in units of length."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-355ef52836a4c27f1290730187a78818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;STRUCTURES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Structures refer to the physical components of an organism, such as its body or tissues, that are maintained and grown using energy from reserves."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SOMATIC MAINTENANCE COSTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Somatic maintenance costs refer to the energy expended by an organism to maintain its bodily functions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Somatic maintenance costs refer to the energy expenses associated with maintaining the structure and function of an organism's body."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FEEDING CONDITIONS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"DIET"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Feeding conditions refer to the availability and quality of food that an organism consumes, which affects its energy reserves and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MULLER AND NISBET&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Muller and Nisbet are references to researchers who have contributed to the understanding of the DEB model and its application to organism development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
