      <data key="d1">"Rearing boxes are a type of equipment used to rear larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;FAECES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"WASTE PRODUCT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Faeces are a waste product of larvae that is removed from the rearing boxes."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-998b63e5349034d477c2087c139669ed</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY DENSITY THRESHOLD&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy density threshold is the minimum amount of energy required for T. molitor larvae to reach pupation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;KAPPA&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Kappa is a parameter in the DEB model that represents the allocation of energy to growth and maintenance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OOGENESIS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oogenesis is the process of egg production, which is not directly considered in the DEB model used in this study."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e819d53f76bcab4b74eba714efd32163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY DENSITY&quot;">
