      <data key="d2">chunk-9a97d5b092508f2e837932274d6b3282</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VIT&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vit is a dietary component that is being tested for its effect on the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;DROPPINGS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Droppings are a source of food for T. molitor larvae, and are being tested for their effect on growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MOULT RESIDUES&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Moult residues are a source of food for T. molitor larvae, and are being tested for their effect on growth and survival."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PS + OAT + VIT GROUP&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"PS + oat + vit group is a concept used in the study to compare the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae under dietary conditions that include PS, oat, and vit."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MACRONUTRIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Macronutrients are a type of nutrient that is necessary for the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;MICRONUTRIENTS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Micronutrients are a type of nutrient that is necessary for the growth and survival of T. molitor larvae."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-54ed790759cee2111ae15e840cf2c48e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;VITAMIN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"NUTRIENT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Vitamin is a nutrient being added to the diet of T. molitor larvae to study its effects on their growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;GLYCOGEN&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"METABOLITE"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Glycogen is a metabolite that is stored in the insect body and plays a key role in sustaining the nervous system."&lt;SEP&gt;"Glycogen is not affected until fuel reserves, such as lipids, are present."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ENERGY DISTRIBUTION&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Energy distribution refers to the allocation of energy sources in the larvae to maintain life and support growth and development."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;ALPHITOBIUS DIAPERINUS PANZER&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"GENUS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Alphitobius diaperinus Panzer is a species of insect that belongs to the same family as T. molitor and has been studied for its metabolic response to food deprivation."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;HAEMOLYMPH&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"PHYSICAL CHARACTERISTIC"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Haemolymph is a physical characteristic of insects that plays a key role in sustaining the nervous system."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;NERVOUS SYSTEM&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL CONCEPT"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Nervous system is a biological concept that refers to the system of organs and tissues that coordinate and control the actions of an insect."&lt;SEP&gt;"The nervous system of insects, such as T. molitor larvae, relies on carbohydrates for sustenance."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91831340731171413dc4c412a325e034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;METABOLIC RESPONSE&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"BIOLOGICAL PROCESS"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Metabolic response refers to the changes in metabolic processes that occur in response to food deprivation or other environmental factors."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;OXIDATION OF FATTY ACIDS&quot;">
      <data key="d0">"CHEMICAL REACTION"</data>
      <data key="d1">"Oxidation of fatty acids is a chemical reaction that produces energy for insects."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f71fddc259d51158d5c79f38bf41523f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;SURVIVAL PROBABILITY&quot;">
