    <edge source="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;" target="&quot;POLYPROPYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">124.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Tenebrio molitor biodegrades Polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor can biodegrade polypropylene through gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is capable of biodegrading polypropylene, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has been found to be capable of biodegrading polypropylene, with the insect's gut microbiome playing a key role in the breakdown of the plastic polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading polypropylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is capable of biodegrading polypropylene, with the larvae able to depolymerize and biodegrade PP polymers with high molecular weight.""&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor can biodegrade polypropylene, indicating a relationship between the two."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor can ingest and degrade polypropylene material in disposable surgical masks, leading to changes in the chemical structure of the material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has been found to biodegrade polypropylene, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae can feed on and degrade polypropylene, with significant changes in their gut bacterial and fungal communities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor, the yellow mealworm, is capable of biodegrading polypropylene via gut-microbe-dependent depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has been found to biodegrade polypropylene, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is capable of biodegrading polypropylene."</data>
