    <edge source="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;" target="&quot;GUT BACTERIA&quot;">
      <data key="d3">36.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Gut bacteria are related to Tenebrio molitor in that they live in its gut and play a crucial role in degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut bacteria live in the gut of Tenebrio molitor, or mealworms, and may play a role in the degradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae have gut bacteria that have the ability to degrade PS, which suggests a symbiotic relationship between the two."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has gut bacteria that play a significant role in the biodegradation of EPS."</data>
