    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR&quot;" target="&quot;BIODEGRADATION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">294.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation is the process by which Tenebrio molitor larvae break down polystyrene, indicating a relationship between the biological process and the microorganism."&lt;SEP&gt;Tenebrio molitor, a species of beetle also known as mealworms, is capable of biodegrading various types of plastics, including polystyrene, polyethylene, polyvinyl chloride (PVC), and other plastic mixtures, through a biological process. The biodegradation process involves the gut microbiome of Tenebrio molitor, where microorganisms break down the plastics into smaller components. The larvae of Tenebrio molitor are directly involved in the biodegradation process, and they can degrade plastics through both gut-microbe-dependent and independent depolymerization. This ability makes Tenebrio molitor a potential tool for reducing plastic waste in the environment. The biodegradation process can lead to changes in the composition of the insect and the molecular mass of the polymer. Tenebrio molitor's ability to biodegrade plastics has been studied extensively, and it has been found to be capable of degrading expanded polystyrene foam, polyethylene terephthalate, and other types of plastics. Overall, Tenebrio molitor plays a significant role in the biodegradation of plastics, and its capabilities are being explored for their potential to mitigate plastic waste. Biodegradation, in the context of Tenebrio molitor, refers to the biological process by which the insect breaks down plastics into smaller, more manageable components, highlighting the intricate relationship between Tenebrio molitor and biodegradation.&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has been shown to be able to biodegrade certain types of plastics, such as polyethylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is capable of biodegrading certain plastics, such as Expanded Polystyrene (EPS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is being studied for its potential to degrade plastics, which could contribute to a better understanding of biodegradation processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor is capable of biodegrading plastics, including polyethylene and polypropylene, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae of Tenebrio molitor, known as mealworms, are capable of biodegrading plastics through a process of biodegradation."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation process, plastic breakdown"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect biology"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect larvae"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect-microbe interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect-microbe interactions"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect-plastic interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, mealworms"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbe-dependent depolymerization"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microorganism capability"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microorganisms"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic waste"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, species capability"&lt;SEP&gt;"biological process, insect activity"&lt;SEP&gt;"biological process, larvae capabilities"&lt;SEP&gt;"biological process, microbe-dependence"&lt;SEP&gt;"insect-polystyrene interaction, biodegradation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-6e25fe1af3bede4605e7b94d457c9634&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5050676818c53a0ef6d691d3049e923c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30a7209d626a6319ba5600bea7f27299&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fd138e047a780efd715a5ab4701b58c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca3745cb01a4209e2eae28914dde3b52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-edd352a71a8bc6e66ece9484f8b59118&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0d2f43eebe2309fba46c5335d76df56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-014a80fd61677e73708fa28913d7fc56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-30c4244cae75095bda7fb526c3d0c9d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65434948dabde813d99972f40a04d8de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3f0582a5d7e55961a1ce4d971d3e4a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e5b6629e8c030ab3162553d83aa6eca4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa27760a0a889fe7b58360dbb150cdf3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f7eff62476fb3de27969b584ac3e605&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95142a3f585446bd848eeedadd1ab713&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-59defb995f5b0409c31d1922916c2f22&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4c0c246e98a503a16ace92f28394b584&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bdf2753a9a78b282c1ca2c0539e3203d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d908d878ed4e7fc36f3af71a5be7f2ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c16f995987af72f86486559556052e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-276c82b9935756a3e668c788458ff922&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7768b61a3d166f2cd01d4e87ac88cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827853316f7304c444884dc82f757802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-37f447b9d6a8b38f80be0854c9c294af&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5922f60fcd06ac6ffa27018026871346&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9528beb2e85a7fb89449a9233eb979bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cdbea1d06006b95d57c8b628d9e3f8f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56af93e805daf3987d95ff99ab8e891d</data>
