      <data key="d3">32.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Klebsiella oxytoca is found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor and may be responsible for its ability to degrade polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Klebsiella oxytoca is isolated from the gut of Tenebrio molitor, suggesting a symbiotic relationship between the two organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor and Klebsiella oxytoca are related in that the gut bacteria of Tenebrio molitor, including Klebsiella oxytoca, play a crucial role in degrading polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae have been found to have Klebsiella oxytoca bacteria in their guts, which enables them to degrade polystyrene."</data>
