      <data key="d3">98.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Gut microorganisms can play a role in degrading polystyrene in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics by Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a role in the biodegradation of plastics by Tenebrio molitor, making them a key factor in the insect's ability to break down plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor larvae have gut microorganisms that are capable of biodegrading polyethylene, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has been found to have a gut microbiota that plays a role in the degradation of polystyrene, which suggests a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has gut microorganisms that are capable of biodegrading plastics like polystyrene, which is a significant discovery in the field of plastic waste management."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor, the mealworm species, has gut microorganisms that play an essential role in the digestion of refractory food and polystyrene biodegradation and mineralization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene by Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms in Tenebrio molitor larvae play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor has gut microorganisms that play a role in biodegradation and mineralization of polystyrene."</data>
