    <edge source="&quot;BIODEGRADATION&quot;" target="&quot;DEPOLYMERIZATION&quot;">
      <data key="d3">239.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polymers, resulting in depolymerization and a decrease in molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which the larvae break down the PP polymer, with depolymerization being the first step."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depolymerization is a key step in the biodegradation of plastics like PP, and is carried out by microorganisms in the gut of T. molitor and Z. atratus."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depolymerization is the process of breaking down polymer chains into smaller components, which is a part of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;BIODEGRADATION and DEPOLYMERIZATION are two closely related processes. BIODEGRADATION is the process by which microorganisms break down organic materials, including plastics, through various chemical reactions. One of the key steps in BIODEGRADATION is DEPOLYMERIZATION, which is the process of breaking down polymers into smaller molecules. DEPOLYMERIZATION is a crucial step in the BIODEGRADATION of plastics, as it allows microorganisms to break down the long-chain structure of polymers into smaller components. This process can occur in various contexts, including the BIODEGRADATION of microplastics, polystyrene (PS), and other types of plastics. Mealworms, for example, have been found to break down plastics, including PS and PE, into smaller polymer chains through DEPOLYMERIZATION. DEPOLYMERIZATION can also occur during the BIODEGRADATION of other materials, such as surgical masks, resulting in a decrease in molecular weight. Overall, DEPOLYMERIZATION is a key process in the BIODEGRADATION of plastics and other organic materials, and is essential for the breakdown of these substances into smaller, more manageable components.&lt;SEP&gt;"Depolymerization is a process that contributes to biodegradation, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation of LDPE involves depolymerization, which breaks down the polymer into smaller molecules."&lt;SEP&gt;"Depolymerization is a process that occurs during the biodegradation of LDPE polymers."</data>
