      <data key="d3">22.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation of PE microplastics by mealworm larvae leads to oxidative stress and lipid peroxidation, despite the larvae's remarkable capacity for removal and biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Oxidative stress is a biological process that is affected by the biodegradation of polystyrene (PS) by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation of microplastics by mealworms leads to oxidative stress, which is a physiological response to the ingestion and breakdown of microplastics."</data>
