    <edge source="&quot;BIODEGRADATION&quot;" target="&quot;MICROORGANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">204.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation is a biological process by which microorganisms break down organic materials, such as plastics, into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is a process carried out by Microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic materials, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic materials, such as polypropylene and polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms like Rhodococcus ruber, Microoccus luteus, and Pseudomonas species break down plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms can play a role in biodegradation, breaking down organic materials including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms play a crucial role in biodegradation, breaking down organic materials, such as plastics, into harmless components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are responsible for the biodegradation of organic substances, such as polystyrene and poly(ethylene terephthalate)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are capable of biodegrading polyethylene, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are capable of biodegradation, which is a process by which they break down organic substances, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms play a crucial role in biodegradation, breaking down plastics into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are responsible for the biodegradation of PS films, breaking them down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polyethylene, breaking it down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms are involved in the biodegradation of plastics, with mealworms being a type of microorganism that can consume and break down plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms play a role in the biodegradation of PS."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down organic materials, including plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is carried out by microorganisms, which break down organic materials into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down plastics, indicating a relationship between the process and the organisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is a process that involves the breakdown of organic materials by microorganisms."</data>
