    <edge source="&quot;BIODEGRADATION&quot;" target="&quot;CANNIBALISM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">27.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation and cannibalism are two biological processes that are related in the context of microorganisms, such as Z. atratus larvae, that exhibit cannibalism when under nutritional stress."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannibalism can decrease the utilization of plastics in biodegradation experiments, as adults consume larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannibalism may affect the biodegradation of plastics in the guts of insect larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Cannibalism is a biological process that can contribute to the biodegradation of polymers."</data>
