    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BIODEGRADATION&quot;" target="&quot;POLYETHYLENE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">167.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation is a biological process by which microorganisms and insects break down polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which polyethylene is broken down into simpler components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene undergoes biodegradation in the gut of superworms and yellow mealworms, breaking down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, such as mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by microorganisms, including Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation may be involved in the degradation of polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is being broken down by microorganisms through the process of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by mealworms through a process of limited extent depolymerization."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is subject to biodegradation by microorganisms, which breaks it down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene, influenced by factors such as surface hydrophobicity, molecular weight distribution, and crystallinity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down polyethylene, resulting in its degradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a type of plastic that can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, including those found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is being biodegraded by microorganisms in the mealworm's gut."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene has been shown to be biodegradable by certain microorganisms, such as those found in the gut of Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which polyethylene is broken down, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene is a type of plastic that is capable of being biodegraded by certain species of microorganisms, which is an important aspect of plastic waste management."</data>
