    <edge source="&quot;BIODEGRADATION&quot;" target="&quot;MICROBIOME&quot;">
      <data key="d3">153.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation is an important mechanism for recycling nutrients and reducing waste, and is often mediated by the microbiome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is influenced by the microbiome of the organism, which determines the types of enzymes and microorganisms present."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is influenced by the microbiome of Tenebrio molitor larvae, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome of insects is being studied for its role in the biodegradation of plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome plays a crucial role in biodegradation, as it is the community of microorganisms that break down organic materials into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is influenced by the microbiome, which plays a crucial role in the breakdown of organic matter."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics, indicating a relationship between the community of microorganisms and the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome is involved in the biodegradation of plastics by insects, such as Zophobas aratus and Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome plays a crucial role in biodegradation, providing the community of microorganisms that break down plastics into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome plays a key role in biodegradation, as microorganisms in the microbiome break down organic materials into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome plays a crucial role in biodegradation processes, as seen in the context of polystyrene degradation by gut microbial flora."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome of insects, including superworms and yellow mealworms, plays a key role in the biodegradation of plastics by providing the necessary microorganisms for the degradation process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The microbiome plays a crucial role in the biodegradation of organic materials, including plastics, by providing a community of microorganisms capable of breaking down these materials."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microbiome is related to biodegradation."</data>
