    <edge source="&quot;BIODEGRADATION&quot;" target="&quot;MICROPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">223.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation can occur with microplastics, which can affect their fate and transport in the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is an important process for breaking down microplastics, which can help to reduce their adverse effects on the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microplastics are broken down into simpler compounds, reducing their harm to the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics have been found to be biodegradable by certain species of insects, including Tenebrio molitor, although the extent of this capability is not well understood."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can be biodegraded by microorganisms, indicating a relationship between the plastic particles and the biological process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is a process by which microorganisms break down microplastics, which are small plastic particles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics are produced during the biodegradation of plastics, such as polystyrene and low-density polyethylene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, with varying rates of consumption and degradation, indicating a complex interaction between the plastic material and the biological process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics are broken down through the process of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is a biological process by which an organism breaks down microplastics, leading to changes in their toxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can undergo biodegradation, but their persistence in the environment is a concern."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is a process that can break down microplastics, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can be biodegraded by microorganisms, which break them down into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is a process that can break down microplastics, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can be biodegraded by certain microorganisms, reducing their impact on the environment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics are produced during the biodegradation of larger plastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can be biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor larvae, resulting in residual microplastic particles and inducing oxidative stress in the larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can undergo biodegradation, which is the process by which microorganisms break them down."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics undergo biodegradation when ingested by mealworms, changing their molecular structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics undergo biodegradation, which is affected by various environmental factors."&lt;SEP&gt;"Biodegradation is the process by which microorganisms break down microplastics into simpler compounds, reducing their environmental impact."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, environmental factors"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microplastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microplastics"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microplastics, fate, transport"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microplastics, oxidative stress"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic material"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic properties"&lt;SEP&gt;"biological process, chemical properties"&lt;SEP&gt;"chemical change, breakdown"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental impact, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental impact, biological process"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental pollution, biodegradability"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental process, pollution"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental remediation, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental remediation, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental remediation, plastic pollution"&lt;SEP&gt;"microplastics, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic degradation, environmental impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"pollution, biodegradation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-0a3d3cf8ea423f7e0f637dddade1bbf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-779ca6b59945309c6bf5040c9fb474ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf7769e197cb664b8d9e41a4c93eec50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df896f6505a6c800d1edd6c75fce9b4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b04ae62930e9961f964284418f1848b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64a060d0c9650ae8bed2ca9b44eef10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1d3c25b9affee2f535cb531a09a2384&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17052974ec1c317689bf07f0684f130f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bf8041a3cdcd6091f6c96b8b67229df2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9fb491e686c96e54f8ea43a9f1ba97eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e4b3c26a06ad850bb97d0ca2d9217be1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c64d0f1648a87497fbcae56f3089b417&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ffec9fc63ae323ee0c22c612bb89755&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d76783f53d38e8c7423dff747f0413d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3fe22bd6c91507d8d1e60d24886e0eb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aaf626f7d7f62d0cee4a0e5efafeb69&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-648afbc8ee82935d4026f5915152491c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a24fcfbc571e8620a1fc59b215b42e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9bd2f7b94f62fa18de9e02426577d241</data>
