    <edge source="&quot;BIODEGRADATION&quot;" target="&quot;GUT MICROORGANISMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">101.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Biodegradation is facilitated by gut microorganisms, which play a crucial role in breaking down plastics like polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms are involved in the biodegradation of polyethylene, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms in mealworms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastic waste, particularly polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms are involved in the biodegradation process of organic substances, including polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms are responsible for the biodegradation process in Tenebrio molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms are responsible for the biodegradation of polystyrene in various organisms, including mealworms and superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a role in the biodegradation of plastics, such as polystyrene, by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene by mealworms, indicating a relationship between the two."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of polystyrene by breaking it down into simpler compounds."&lt;SEP&gt;"Gut microorganisms play a crucial role in the biodegradation of plastics, indicating a strong relationship between the two entities."</data>
