    <edge source="&quot;ZOPHOBAS ATRATUS&quot;" target="&quot;POLYSTYRENE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">205.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Zophobas atratus can biodegrade polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller pieces."&lt;SEP&gt;Zophobas atratus, also known as superworms, has been found to have a significant relationship with polystyrene, a type of plastic material. Zophobas atratus is capable of biodegrading polystyrene, breaking it down into simpler compounds, and has been used in studies to investigate the biodegradation of polystyrene, particularly in the context of microbiome research. The biodegradation process is facilitated by the insect's gut bacterial- and fungal-microbiomes, which aid in the degradation of polystyrene. Zophobas atratus larvae have also been found to biodegrade polystyrene, indicating that this ability is present throughout the insect's life cycle. The insect's ability to biodegrade polystyrene makes it a potential solution for plastic waste management. Additionally, Zophobas atratus has been shown to have a higher consumption rate of polystyrene compared to other species, such as Tenebrio molitor, and is capable of degrading low-density polystyrene. The biodegradation process results in the fragmentation of polystyrene into microplastics and changes in the insect's gut microbiota. Overall, the relationship between Zophobas atratus and polystyrene is one of degradation, with the insect playing a crucial role in breaking down the plastic material into simpler compounds.</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, insect larvae"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect-plastic interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, metabolism"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microbiome research"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microorganisms"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, mineralization"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic degradation, environmental impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic ingestion"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic pollution"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic waste management"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic waste"&lt;SEP&gt;"insect degradation, plastic pollution"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-b9fcb421212175a148a0a1858582cfb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df045e015825dac8935c9c6d8a402cda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfd8d6b8105d9868a4ffadf5779d0df5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d642e5476221b3ea202c68d7e6070b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d068dbad68e3ecd909a551f43f82b893&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a8076792f39f6c801b538312a7b45fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f91ffc7c76e8e0a1757d91f7cf62f568&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3667703f7416ebab666e65b375dd8582&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03980ce7209ce3f1b1c62c6ed9961e27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5d6035f4b0686837c8c4319bab80d70&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b79a227bc8e127f6b71fd2edb0e650a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-56f83fc7c1ea25f2ead74aceccfe4cf2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-422e833d3381bd5fd0b5a3d63d9047f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e127a4930b6154498b93c2e94f2b7c20&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7232abef4870641de7945afeb6a4bf93&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-00a6288e1109e01eac1ce7ecb35f2eda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5279ebea7d4d5e22eebe3106de3ba1c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-550dde13ffd2abcf536dd87f7d4c1b40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22e4b8000531766cffd145ef32353af2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7e3ac1a351ece6e7f29ea15d8b1c721d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-530244abdca5889849fcf86f017ebd77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bce368b44455642f4b9a1dacc4cdf0f3</data>
