    <edge source="&quot;POLYSTYRENE&quot;" target="&quot;TENEBRIO MOLITOR LINNAEUS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">67.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Polystyrene is biodegraded by Tenebrio molitor Linnaeus, which is a type of insect that can break down this type of plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor Linnaeus has been found to biodegrade polystyrene, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor Linnaeus can degrade polystyrene, using it as a sole diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae of Tenebrio Molitor Linnaeus can digest and degrade polystyrene, indicating a direct relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor linnaeus is capable of degrading polystyrene through a process of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor Linnaeus biodegrades polystyrene, breaking it down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tenebrio molitor Linnaeus can biodegrade polystyrene, indicating a relationship between the microorganism and the polymer."</data>
