      <data key="d3">33.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Gut microbiota play a crucial role in the digestion and biodegradation of PET by T. molitor larvae, influencing their consumption rates and degradation efficiencies."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae have a symbiotic relationship with gut microbiota, which contributes to the biodegradation of PP polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota in the T. molitor larvae contributes to the biodegradation of PET, with antibiotic suppression affecting this process."&lt;SEP&gt;"The gut microbiota of T. molitor larvae contributes to the biodegradation of PET, with a complex interaction between the host and the microorganisms."</data>
