    <edge source="&quot;LDPE&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">84.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"LDPE is being consumed by mealworms, and its effects are being studied."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is being degraded by mealworms, which is the focus of the biodegradability experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is degraded by mealworms, which affects their growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is preferred by mealworms over LLDPE, indicating a strong relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are able to degrade LDPE, but their growth is not significantly affected by LDPE consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are used to degrade LDPE plastic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can ingest and metabolize LDPE microplastics, with significant differences in molecular weight distribution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can metabolize LDPE, resulting in changes to its crystalline structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworms are also able to degrade LDPE, but to a lesser extent than the Greater Wax Moth Larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can consume LDPE, with an average consumption rate of 0.00102 mg per day per mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consuming LDPE experience a lower mass gain than those consuming HDPE, potentially due to the higher bioresistance of LDPE."</data>
