    <edge source="&quot;LDPE&quot;" target="&quot;T. MOLITOR LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">27.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"LDPE is a type of plastic that can be ingested and digested by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is a type of plastic that is being compared to PET in terms of biodegradation by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae consume LDPE as part of their diet, leading to biodegradation of the plastic foam."&lt;SEP&gt;"The T. molitor larvae also biodegrade LDPE, with the process and effects being studied through High-Temperature Gel Permeation Chromatography and other methods."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, comparison"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, polymer breakdown"&lt;SEP&gt;"ingestion, digestion"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-11de08c24a626abb11d37d71e9567e2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92ea4ca7a83af5c086ae157fb801b326&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61cd3a131593ce6b058802713d43ddb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449dceb5649c6baa34ecc2218cd3e9e1</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;LDPE&quot;" target="&quot;T. MOLITOR&quot;">
      <data key="d3">181.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"LDPE can be biodegraded by T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor can biodegrade LDPE, with a high rate of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae are used to study the biodegradation of LDPE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae biodegrade LDPE, resulting in a decrease in molecular weight and the formation of new oxidative functional groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae were fed with LDPE, and their gut microbiomes were analyzed to understand the effect of LDPE on the microbial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"LDPE is degraded by T. molitor, resulting in broad depolymerization and significant reduction of molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor is being studied for its ability to biodegrade LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor is involved in the biodegradation of LDPE, breaking it down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae depolymerize LDPE, resulting in a decrease in molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor performs biodegradation of LDPE, resulting in both broad and limited extent depolymerization patterns."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor can digest LDPE and convert it to CO2, with around 50% of the carbon remaining in the frass and nearly 40% converted to CO2."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor is capable of biodegrading LDPE, as shown by the changes in the FTIR and ¹H NMR spectra of the frass samples."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor is capable of degrading LDPE polymers, resulting in a decrease in molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae are able to biodegrade LDPE, as shown by the decrease in stability of the plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae are capable of biodegrading LDPE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae can consume and degrade LDPE, with a higher specific LDPE consumption rate than T. obscurus larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae can depolymerize LDPE, with the process being gut-microbe independent."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae consume LDPE, indicating a relationship between the genus and the product."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor larvae contribute to the biodegradation of LDPE, with the involvement of gentamicin affecting the process."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. molitor, or mealworms, are capable of biodegrading LDPE, or low-density polyethylene, plastics."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, digestion"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect contribution, antibiotic effect"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect larvae"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, microorganism-plastic interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic decomposition"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, polyethylene"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, polymer degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, species interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption, plastic degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"depolymerization, polymer degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, microbiome"&lt;SEP&gt;"insect biodegradation, plastic degradation"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-ffb4e34985ec90215629dc19750c8bdf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3ab754d1dc0a02ee3f869d2b082a710e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2cfbb4289b0cc4c8b69884f6d57c447&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-639bb2429f20c4fe3994c4a0d15f3295&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-51f749234fed052c982d79f81b93cc29&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc908e62eec4d1d05265c6e451cca84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b21eb0db725b38c3e0b5c01526ce90b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0cba3b06dd82e87d3b582bc21c475868&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd4d84d6de496440fcabc6616d1c96ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3099f2d6fd3abc2f73550f579999b13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f75b58db5211fc7348ccca8206b9bbae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6ac1b1db6ffab6f4cfea7a525785a2fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-22d348f5320f96e129128362b6e0407c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89a76f613b36454134940f78fba1c0f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3380732c060363504db5f6e4b8610b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b95a108327e39d37d20bdd99db541164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f28f1c36076d1f249dbc4cd67b16f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-843d5746868067bce1a2f15dfc1571e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-109486cd939a227e73354d0478c59ecf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5a94048d4a1499a73a50e74a59245e6</data>
