      <data key="d3">163.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"LDPE is degraded by T. obscurus, resulting in broad depolymerization and significant reduction of molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus can biodegrade LDPE, causing oxidative stress and ecotoxicity."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus can biodegrade LDPE, with a high rate of biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae are used to study the biodegradation of LDPE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae biodegrade LDPE, resulting in a decrease in molecular weight and the formation of new oxidative functional groups."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae were fed with LDPE, and their gut microbiomes were analyzed to understand the effect of LDPE on the microbial community."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus is being studied for its ability to biodegrade LDPE."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus is involved in the biodegradation of LDPE, breaking it down into smaller components."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae can biodegrade LDPE microplastics, leading to changes in their molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae depolymerize LDPE, resulting in a decrease in molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus can also digest LDPE and convert it to CO2, with similar carbon conversion efficiency as T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus is also capable of biodegrading LDPE, with similar patterns of biodegradation as T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus is capable of degrading LDPE polymers, with higher plastic polymer digestibility than T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae also consume LDPE, indicating a relationship between the genus and the product."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae are also able to biodegrade LDPE, similar to T. molitor."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae are capable of biodegrading LDPE polymers."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae can consume and degrade LDPE, with a lower specific LDPE consumption rate than T. molitor larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"T. obscurus larvae can depolymerize LDPE, with the process being gut-microbe independent."</data>
