      <data key="d3">53.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms are able to degrade PP, but their growth is not significantly affected by PP consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are capable of consuming and biodegrading PP, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP is being used as a control in the biodegradability experiment involving mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP is degraded by mealworms, which affects their growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"PP is not easily consumed by mealworms due to its semicrystalline structure, indicating a weak relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms may be capable of degrading PP, a type of plastic material."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are used to degrade PP polymers, and the degradation process is affected by the molecular weight of PP."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can consume PP, with an average consumption rate of 0.0125 mg per day per mealworm."</data>
