    <edge source="&quot;PVC&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">56.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms can consume PVC, with an average consumption rate of 0.00249 mg per day per mealworm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can ingest and metabolize PVC microplastics, but with limited digestion and varying effects depending on the region."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms from Tai'an and Shenzhen can metabolize PVC, resulting in changes to its crystalline structure."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is degraded by mealworms, which affects their growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"PVC is degraded by mealworms through an oxidative process, with changes in the gut microbiota."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consuming PVC experience a significant reduction in mass, potentially due to the release of carboxylic acids and the lack of nutrients in PVC."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can survive on PVC microplastics, and their survival rates and body weights were affected by PVC consumption."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms show a low mass loss when fed PVC, indicating a possible difficulty in consuming PVC."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, symbiotic relationship"&lt;SEP&gt;"consumption, difficulty"&lt;SEP&gt;"degradation, growth"&lt;SEP&gt;"ingestion, limited digestion"&lt;SEP&gt;"metabolism, microplastics degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic consumption, degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic consumption, mass reduction"&lt;SEP&gt;"survival, microplastics"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-31f2ee9a779791fef2da810debc12720&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9a27dff473ed210517e6461ad3e5d783&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b0491f3e96c1d355b8431b9d74868f63&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9424d3ce58d3ff2e0adc795d24fe84f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-475b22fe6100b14cced604f739663fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ed721221326657b60aadb09faeeac92&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-236f4db8df75799fa6a0a07921158cf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff201df58dec460c49cd31920c29f11a</data>
    </edge>
