    <edge source="&quot;BRAN&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">300.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms can be fed bran as a nutrient supplement, which affects their survival and growth."&lt;SEP&gt;BRAN and MEALWORMS have a significant relationship, as BRAN is used as a nutrient source and control diet for MEALWORMS in various studies. BRAN provides MEALWORMS with energy, supports their growth, and helps relieve the constraint of lack of nitrogen sources and other nutrients. MEALWORMS fed with BRAN serve as a control group, allowing for comparison of their growth and survival with those fed other substances, such as polyether-PU foam, microplastics, and polystyrene. As a conventional diet, BRAN affects the nitrogen-fixing activity of MEALWORMS and is a nutrient source that results in higher δ15N values. BRAN is a type of diet that is used as a control in studies and is nutritionally adequate for MEALWORMS. It is a component of the MEALWORMS' diet, used as a comparison to plastic diets in experiments, and is also used to supplement the diet of MEALWORMS. MEALWORMS can be reared on BRAN, and their weight loss and feed consumption are measured when they are consuming BRAN as a control diet. Additionally, BRAN can be supplied to MEALWORMS to eliminate the harmful effects of microplastic feeding, promoting their growth and survival. When MEALWORMS are co-fed BRAN with plastics, such as polystyrene, it enhances their survival and growth rates, suggesting a beneficial effect of this co-diet on MEALWORM health. BRAN is also a source of nutrition that can facilitate faster rates of polystyrene degradation by MEALWORMS. Overall, BRAN plays a crucial role in the study of MEALWORMS, particularly in the context of biodegradability experiments and the impact of plastic consumption on their growth and development. MEALWORMS fed with BRAN have a higher survival rate and mass increase compared to those without a food source, and BRAN is used to compare the effects of microplastic consumption on MEALWORMS, with varying effects on their survival and development.</data>
      <data key="d5">"consumption, nutrition"&lt;SEP&gt;"control, comparison, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, control"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, mealworms"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, nitrogen fixation"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, nutrition"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, nutritional adequacy"&lt;SEP&gt;"growth, development"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient source, biodegradability experiment"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient source, feeding"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient, diet"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient, insect growth"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient, mealworms"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient, organism"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, augmentation"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, biodegradation enhancement"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, control group"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, control"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, development"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, diet"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, feeding"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, growth enhancement"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, growth"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, growth, survival"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, health benefit"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, mealworms"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, substrate-organism interaction"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, survival rate"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, survival rate, metabolite production"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, survival"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-2e97dc712df43805c553423ceb65cd6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2338bb97657d74ab5d8a444849037692&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-220952ca1d34f3ffef65c5d71e22015e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81552b76a273b31cc2bd9ed21ed7a919&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5193c909193ddd73442615b27f4f9be3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a522a615bbcac2e06f97f2e4e61975b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-630e33352368a0c7f34d56ad45a38e56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96aac7c9638ee245b9db5df3ec1d2a1f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ada834fc8d4bea41c0ce1770d6f57e4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17b1e554820493d86eb8bc96ba8bef37&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7c343b12adf5bbce5bf80b96909fe66d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5740f0973ff804cae61f6fc12f3e3753&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38e212e8bab88c4d7b6d63a157e27c00&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e05bc34fccfca5e177064daf8346866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf827d2b1d02488e17469a22da9e252&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1769c4becf46c99994cb7ced2bffda1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d99a98d885ec6495c4dc902866c4ab9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b12451ba2a22e6f74c543f982a0a7b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c29fa50fac7d523f43c540627750c823&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-53dd546535ef4247004faab1fa475889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f748ef0b9e55c370617ad91bcf219c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9af0d95fd5f52d02b9cb33387951963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-640f0655e17fab473cca3b460c2795de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c651f9305c4265540ed7deeb891eae71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-718900b924b6910a58e8ead81c01c723&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb9111bd088e1990cde867c6d85cf28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-838d20fb5f3709d303402ea916d8172f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dea2d94de229e98ea99b0d40b7b077ad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89ff8edff56325c22cfed3871f4fbf48&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-12ceb4368e146509caa737d9534ce3c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a6517509e242b0396ba75e2d6e09a1d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77817419b966e501f1106866cbea7350&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70735757eafccc0f762f21f5d3ac8556&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-05b7bf66b11c66f02e73a07fb823b8fa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0638e0fe93dc27e678672a164e6088c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b0b175969d87b3be377f65b988d0a52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e45f9527e7b07e945435dae572dc387&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc6b858a4eb57553f5b1ae041e1c7160&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818a01113d8c07554629cc5edfd28f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a214d2b1c90aeb78e6e8562679d4963&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-086890e8567c60d8cfa7c03b0cc61f9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3646a65acc7cbdc1d20742888b17613a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38f2f3673b813b3a817c014229c9565</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRAN&quot;" target="&quot;MEALWORM LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">90.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bran can enhance the biomass levels and survival of mealworm larvae, but it can also disturb the removal of microplastics in their intestinal tracts."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is added as a co-diet to increase the mealworm larvae's affinity for the PE feedstock, stimulating their consumption and biodegradation of plastic."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran supplementation enhances the growth and survival of mealworm larvae, and affects the biodegradation of PE microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran supplements enhance the biomass levels and survival of mealworm larvae, but slightly disturb the PE removal efficiency in the gut microenvironment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm larvae consume bran as a food source, which is combined with PE microplastics to create a feedstock."&lt;SEP&gt;"The addition of bran to the diet of the mealworm larvae helps to mitigate the negative effects of biodegrading PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworm larvae are able to digest and utilize the nutrients from the bran, which improves their growth and biodegradation of PE microplastics."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is a type of feed that results in the highest content of fatty acids in mealworm larvae."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworm larvae are fed bran as a control diet in the experiment."</data>
      <data key="d5">"diet, control"&lt;SEP&gt;"dietary supplementation, mitigation of negative effects"&lt;SEP&gt;"feed type, fatty acid content"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient supplementation, plastic consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, feedstock"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, growth"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, microplastic removal"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-fccc204d8a48c645da49bd7b3175c262&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f267b48449a40d614a2f325799752dea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f7d44b3f99233bb4389ceea0cd62617&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1175f4bdc5e5c267806fa6c0ff19fcc4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e32e296ef016e2403df45f75eedee219&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a660790845c6a68ed38b428a7756fc84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a2991bc47bdc7fe9bc0d7c0d3e23f60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa1a88a43b40afd043514c5f6898ee71&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54f1dd7372cfa3dc5f348864eed2261</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="&quot;BRAN&quot;" target="&quot;LARVAE&quot;">
      <data key="d3">30.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Bran is used as a control feedstock for the larvae in the experiment, and its effect on the larvae's growth and biodegradation ability is compared to that of polystyrene microplastics (MPs)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Bran is used as a control feedstock for the larvae in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae of Tenebrio molitor are fed a diet that includes bran, which affects their biodegradation of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae are being fed bran, which serves as a control group for the experiment, indicating a relationship between the nutrient and the microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"The larvae were fed with bran as a food source."</data>
      <data key="d5">"control, feedstock, larvae"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, biodegradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"diet, nutrition"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrient intake, biological response"&lt;SEP&gt;"nutrition, growth"</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-89344d5b5d9debdca45ab8c7c963a585&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5540fc6fe4d3ef0fd986ec36a589c77f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dcf2bd0dbdce4d7299bfc35487eaf0f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-20395efa1299dc8b777774e765ad1159&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16810fc8beb169dfca32904d41bd992b</data>
    </edge>
