    <edge source="&quot;MEALWORMS&quot;" target="&quot;STYROFOAM&quot;">
      <data key="d3">160.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms are able to eat Styrofoam, but at a lower rate than superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are capable of degrading Styrofoam, with a consumption rate that can be enhanced by supplementation of nitrogen-containing feed."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume Styrofoam, which affects their nutritional composition and energy content, indicating a potential adaptation mechanism."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can biodepolymerize styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are capable of eating Styrofoam as their sole diet."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can degrade and mineralize Styrofoam, and their gut microbiota plays an essential role in this process."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms degrade Styrofoam, and the degradation process is influenced by the chemical composition and structure of Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms eat Styrofoam, which is then degraded by the mealworms, resulting in changes to the chemical structure and composition of the Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrofoam is being degraded by mealworms in their gut, through a process involving microbes and extracellular enzymes."&lt;SEP&gt;"The mealworms are responsible for decomposing the Styrofoam, with the carbon content of the Styrofoam being measured over time."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are being fed Styrofoam, which is being degraded by the mealworms and their gut bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are fed with styrofoam as a diet to study the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can degrade Styrofoam."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms are capable of eating Styrofoam, which is related to their nitrogen-fixing activity."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can degrade Styrofoam, a type of plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms eat Styrofoam, and this consumption is associated with the presence of gut nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrofoam is a type of vinyl plastic that is eaten and digested by mealworms, and its degradation requires the presence of nitrogen-fixing bacteria."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrofoam is used as a sole diet for mealworms in this study, indicating a nutritional relationship."</data>
