      <data key="d4">"Mealworms experienced starvation before being fed different diets in the study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation affects the survival and growth of mealworms, with its effects being compared to those of different diets."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a condition where the mealworms are not fed, used as a control in the experiment."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a physiological response of mealworms when they are not consuming enough food."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a physiological response that is being studied in mealworms that are not being fed, with varying effects on their growth and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a physiological response that occurs in mealworms when they are unable to access sufficient nutrients, leading to changes in their metabolic processes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Starvation is a type of physiological response that is being measured in the experiment, with starved mealworms losing 2.6 ± 0.2% of their average weight, indicating a negative physiological response to the lack of food."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms show significant changes in their biochemical characteristics when starved, indicating a physiological response to starvation."</data>
