      <data key="d3">73.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms can ingest and biodegrade microplastics, including PS and PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume and degrade microplastics, with varying effects on their survival and development."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms ingest microplastics, which can accumulate in their bodies and affect their growth and survival."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms have been found to degrade microplastics, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can be degraded by mealworms, indicating a relationship between the two entities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms ingest and biodegrade microplastics, breaking them down into smaller particles."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms ingest microplastics, leading to biodegradation and a reduction in their size, but also experience oxidative stress and physiological changes."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics are ingested by mealworms, causing oxidative stress and damage."</data>
