      <data key="d3">63.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Mealworms are also fed Polyethylene (PE) to study their plastic degradation capabilities."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can also degrade polyethylene, similar to polystyrene, indicating their potential role in breaking down different types of plastic waste."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can ingest and degrade PE."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene (PE) is being compared to PU Foam in terms of its biodegradation by mealworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms consume polyethylene, including low-density polyethylene (LDPE) and high-density polyethylene (HDPE)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Mealworms can biodegrade PE through a process of limited-extent depolymerization, resulting in an increase in molecular weight."&lt;SEP&gt;"Polyethylene (PE) is ingested by mealworms, causing oxidative stress and damage."</data>
      <data key="d5">"biodegradation, comparison"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, insect digestion"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, plastic consumption"&lt;SEP&gt;"biodegradation, polymer degradation"&lt;SEP&gt;"degradation, feeding"&lt;SEP&gt;"ingestion, oxidative stress"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic consumption, biodegradation"</data>
