      <data key="d3">75.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Polystyrene (PS) is produced from the polymerization of styrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene is a chemical property of polystyrene (PS) that can be detected in the frass and carcasses of mealworms and superworms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene is a component of polystyrene (PS)."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene is a decomposition product of polystyrene (PS), indicating the breakdown of the polymer."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene is a type of chemical that is used to make polystyrene (PS) and is also a potential impurity in PS products."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene is a chemical compound used in the experiment to study polystyrene (PS) biodegradation."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene is a chemical compound that is a component of polystyrene (PS) and has been found to be transformed by certain microorganisms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene is a chemical property that is formed during the degradation of polystyrene."&lt;SEP&gt;"Styrene is a monomer that makes up PS, with its degradation affected by the presence of bran and water."</data>
