    <edge source="&quot;MICROPLASTICS&quot;" target="&quot;NANOPLASTICS&quot;">
      <data key="d3">58.0</data>
      <data key="d4">"Both microplastics and nanoplastics are small plastic particles that can be ingested by mealworms and affect their gut microbiome and metabolome."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics and nanoplastics are both small plastic particles that can be ingested by organisms and cause harm."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics can degrade into nanoplastics, which can have negative impacts on ecosystems and human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics and nanoplastics are related in the context of plastic pollution."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics and nanoplastics are both types of small plastic particles that can have harmful effects on the environment and human health."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics may be further broken down into nanoplastics, although this was not detected in this study."&lt;SEP&gt;"Microplastics and nanoplastics are both types of toxins that can harm the environment and human health, and their pollution and reduction strategies are being studied."</data>
      <data key="d5">"chemical composition, environmental impact"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental impact, human health"&lt;SEP&gt;"environmental pollution, human health"&lt;SEP&gt;"microplastic formation, nanoplastic formation"&lt;SEP&gt;"physical property, environmental issue"&lt;SEP&gt;"plastic pollution, size comparison"&lt;SEP&gt;"toxicity, environmental impact"</data>
